// gerado por tools/i18n-build.mjs a partir de tools/i18n/en*.json
window.I18N_DATA = {"0":"Tomás \"Fatso\" Bruno","1":"Night Porter","2":"Reconditioned implants, third-hand. One has its serial number scraped off: fake identity? No biological trace of Arthur on the uniform.","3":"Oh, detective... Tomás Bruno, night porter. I just clean, okay? Didn't see nothing, didn't hear nothing. I swear on my mother.","4":"Yes, boss?","5":"Still here, detective? This hallway gives me the creeps.","6":"Go ahead, boss. But keep it down.","7":"What did you do tonight?","8":"Usual rounds. Picked up trays, changed towels, vacuumed the elevator carpet.","9":"The 4th floor was quiet. Too quiet, you know?","10":"Press: \"You look nervous, Tomás.\"","11":"Too quiet? You're sweating, Tomás. And it's not the rain.","12":"Nervous? Me? It's... it's the noise from these implants. They heat up. Cheap parts, boss.","13":"He glances at the service door every time he lies.","14":"Empathy: \"Long nights, huh?\"","15":"Long nights, huh?","16":"Long and badly paid. But I like the silence... usually. Not tonight.","17":"Tonight the silence had noise inside it, if you know what I mean.","18":"Did you know Arthur Pendelton?","19":"Everybody did. Tips? Never. Once he made me clean the same carpet three times because it \"smelled poor\".","20":"That's a reason to hate him.","21":"If I killed every rich guy who humiliated me, detective, Sector 4 would be empty.","22":"I swallow it, boss. That's what people like me do. Swallow it and clean.","23":"Those implants make quite a racket.","24":"Reconditioned, boss. Left knee, hip and two fingers. Third-hand parts.","25":"It's what a porter's salary pays for. The hotel's health plan covers \"cosmetic implants\". Cosmetic! Do I look cosmetic to you?","26":"Clank, clank, every step. Nobody sneaks anywhere on these legs.","27":"Where does the service door lead?","28":"To the old maintenance tunnels. From the analog days, before the networks. There's ducts going up to every room.","29":"Back in the day, technicians climbed inside the walls to fix the ventilation. Nobody uses them now. Or nobody should.","30":"Who has the key?","31":"Only management. I don't go near it.","32":"Who else was around the 4th floor?","33":"Let me think... Around 22:20 the service drone came up with a tray for 404. Fancy drink, crystal glass.","34":"The wife, Mrs. Evelyn, I didn't see her up here all night. She lives at the bar when she's at the hotel.","35":"The doctor with the weird glasses stays on the 3rd. Didn't come up, far as I know.","36":"And Victor Rossi?","37":"Mr. Rossi doesn't come up. Never takes the elevator. Says the tunnels are \"faster\".","38":"The tunnels. The tunnels again.","39":"What's it like working for Victor Rossi?","40":"He's... desperate. Last week he sold the original chandeliers from the ballroom. Said they were replicas. They weren't.","41":"Three months of back pay, boss. Three. And him in a new suit.","42":"And that arm of his... Industrial prosthetic, dockworker grade. Says it was a work accident.","43":"A hotel manager with a work accident? Only if the stapler exploded.","44":"⚠ Confront: you were here at 22:57","45":"Arthur died at 22:57. Your rounds took you down this hallway at exactly that time.","46":"I... I already said I didn't see nothing!","47":"Threaten: \"Talk, or I call the corporate police.\"","48":"Either you talk now, or I call the corporate police and they pull your whole file. The real one.","49":"No! No, please! Okay, okay!","50":"I heard a noise. Like a metal thud, coming from 404. Around 22:55.","51":"At 23:00 I saw the service door ajar. I hid in the linen closet until everything went quiet.","52":"Empathy: \"I'm not after you.\"","53":"Tomás. I'm not after you. I'm after whoever killed Arthur. And I think you know something.","54":"...You swear you won't turn me in?","55":"I swear I'll turn in the killer. Only him.","56":"Around 22:55 I heard a metal thud in 404. Heavy. Then some footsteps... no, not footsteps. Sounded like a machine walking. Clank. Clank.","57":"At 23:00 I saw the service door ajar. I stayed hidden in the closet till midnight. Coward, I know.","58":"Why didn't you say so before?","59":"Because my name isn't Tomás Bruno, detective. If the corporate police pull my file...","60":"What's your real name?","61":"...","62":"Insist: \"I need to know.\"","63":"I need to know who I'm talking to.","64":"Bruno Teixeira. Implant smuggling at the Sector 9 port, twelve years ago. Got six. Served four.","65":"Got out, bought a clean identity, landed this job. I paid, detective. I swear I paid.","66":"Sector 9. The same port where Victor Rossi says he lost his arm.","67":"Respect: \"Your secret's safe with me.\"","68":"I don't need to know. Your secret's safe with me.","69":"...Thank you, detective. Nobody ever said anything like that to me.","70":"Look, here's some free advice: Mr. Rossi has a physical copy of the tunnel key. On a chain, around his neck. I saw it.","71":"Gunshots?! Boss, just now I heard a clank, clank climbing up the closet wall. Heavy. Just like that night.","72":"God help me, put that away... I went into that suite yesterday to change the towels. He was alive and complaining about the hallway smell.","73":"Crystal glass from the suite. The service drone took the tray, not me. I'm not even allowed to touch the crystal.","74":"Heavy footprints like that? Not mine, boss. I'm fat, but not that fat. That's metal. A lot of metal.","75":"That door creaks like a lost soul. I heard it creak... right after the noise in 404.","76":"The suite's duct goes straight down to the tunnels. A big man fits, if he's stubborn. I've seen a technician get stuck in there.","77":"Mr. Rossi's arm... I always figured that thing could rip a door off its frame. Once he crushed a fire extinguisher by accident.","78":"Broke? Boss, I could've told you that for free. Three months without pay.","79":"Hydraulic wrench from the tunnels. Used to hang down there, on the tool board. Weighs about eight kilos. Nobody's used it since they replaced the boiler.","80":"Fancy chronometer. He was always looking at it and complaining that everybody was late.","81":"That I don't know, boss.","82":"I don't understand that tech stuff. I can barely work the vacuum.","83":"Why are you showing me this? Do I look like a forensics guy?","84":"Evelyn Pendelton","85":"The Wife","86":"Stable heart rate. Cold body temperature, but nothing unusual for her. Luxury optical implants, no hidden logs. Blood alcohol level: high and steady for hours.","87":"Detective Vance. The corporation sent the usual bloodhound. Be brief. I'm in mourning.","88":"You again. How tedious.","89":"More questions? At least order a drink.","90":"Detective. Still trying to understand the rich?","91":"Where were you around 23:00?","92":"Here. On this stool. Ask the bar terminal: it logs every credit I've spent.","93":"And there were many.","94":"Irony: \"Drinking to forget?\"","95":"Drinking to forget?","96":"Drinking to remember, detective. That I'm still a Pendelton. For now.","97":"Neutral: \"I'll check.\"","98":"I'll check.","99":"Do. It's your job, after all. Mine is to look devastated.","100":"What was your marriage like?","101":"A contract. He ran the companies, I ran the appearances. It worked.","102":"It worked?","103":"Press: \"Contracts have termination clauses.\"","104":"Contracts have termination clauses.","105":"And confidentiality clauses, detective. I know about yours, by the way. Shall I call the corporation right now?","106":"She knows about my dismissal. Of course she does. People like her know everything that can be used.","107":"Back off: \"No offense meant.\"","108":"No offense meant.","109":"Yes, it was. But I appreciate the effort of pretending otherwise.","110":"It worked until he decided I had become... obsolete. Like an old implant.","111":"What was Arthur really like?","112":"Brilliant. Cruel. In that order, on good days.","113":"He bought people the way you buy implants. When they became obsolete, he swapped them. Patents, partners, wives.","114":"Do you know what he told me on our twentieth anniversary? \"You've aged well, Evelyn. For a 2029 model.\"","115":"She laughs as she says it. Her eyes don't.","116":"Who wanted Arthur dead?","117":"Do you prefer the short list or the long one?","118":"The short one: Dr. Souza, whom he robbed. Rossi, whom he was about to sink. And me, of course. You've probably put me at the top already.","119":"\"Are you at the top?\"","120":"And are you at the top?","121":"I'm at the top of many lists, detective. Mostly guest lists.","122":"\"And the long list?\"","123":"And the long list?","124":"Half the Pendelton BioCyber board, three former partners, a senator and anyone who ever had dinner with him.","125":"But none of them were at the hotel tonight. Too bad for you.","126":"What do you know about Dr. Souza?","127":"A naive genius. The worst possible combination around my husband.","128":"Arthur seduced her with promises of her own lab, unlimited funding. She handed over everything. He registered everything in his name.","129":"This afternoon, in the lobby, she shouted that he \"would regret it\". The whole hotel heard.","130":"But that woman won't kill a cockroach without calculating its trajectory first. If she did anything, it was something... clean. Chemical.","131":"A man who smiles too much for someone who's broke.","132":"Arthur called him \"my expensive butler\". In front of the staff. Rossi hated it. And smiled.","133":"And there's something else. He keeps disappearing from the lobby. Vanishes and comes back with wet shoes.","134":"Wet, detective. Inside a hotel. With the rain outside and him in here.","135":"Wet shoes. Standing water. The maintenance tunnels flood with the acid rain.","136":"⚠ Confront: the draft will","137":"I found a draft will on the holographic desk. Your name was removed.","138":"...So he was really going to do it.","139":"Accuse: \"That's a motive for murder.\"","140":"That's a motive for murder.","141":"It's a motive to hire better lawyers. I already have, detective. Last week.","142":"Yes, I knew. I wanted to see him ruined. Not dead.","143":"Understand: \"That must have hurt.\"","144":"That must have hurt.","145":"...Twenty years, detective. Twenty years of dinners and smiles. And he crosses me out with a hologram, between one meeting and the next.","146":"I wanted to see him ruined. But not dead.","147":"Dead, he can't change his mind anymore. Think about that. I had more to lose with him dead than alive.","148":"The bar terminal confirms your story.","149":"Of course it does. Nine transactions in just over an hour. I'm very consistent.","150":"Detective... find whoever did this. Not for him. For me. I want to look that person in the face.","151":"Now go find who really did this. And close the door on your way out. Oh, there's no door. Pity.","152":"Gunshots in my hotel. How inelegant.","153":"If someone wants you dead, detective, it's because you're getting close. Congratulations.","154":"That chronometer was my gift. Silver anniversary. He never took it off his wrist.","155":"And he never adjusted it. Arthur hated fiddling with settings, said it was assistant's work.","156":"If the time was changed, detective, it wasn't him.","157":"Synthetic whiskey? He loathed it. He'd only drink it if someone he wanted to impress offered it. Or humiliate.","158":"...Put that away, detective.","159":"I saw enough of him while he was alive.","160":"Rossi broke? Darling, the whole hotel knew. Even the robot bartender, and he's switched off.","161":"That arm... At a dinner, he crushed a crystal glass by accident. Arthur laughed for a week. Rossi didn't.","162":"A hotel rescue plan? Arthur would never sign that.","163":"He wanted the hotel bankrupt. Buying the wreckage at auction would cost a tenth of the price. He told me laughing, over breakfast.","164":"The fight in the lobby. I was there. It was the only time I ever saw someone keep Arthur quiet for three whole seconds.","165":"The Aurora patents. He said they were his greatest creation. He lied even to me — I knew they were the doctor's.","166":"ADM-02? Administrative credentials are management business, detective. I can't even open my own safe without the assistant.","167":"Is that supposed to impress me?","168":"I have no idea what that is. Ask someone who works.","169":"Detective, I'm in mourning. More or less.","170":"Put away your trinkets. I have a drink waiting.","171":"Dr. Helena Souza","172":"The Researcher","173":"The AR glasses have a recent connection log. Device ID: HS-AR. Destination: a drive in suite 404, from 22:50 to 22:52.","174":"You're the detective? Good. Maybe now someone will actually investigate Arthur Pendelton — even dead.","175":"Detective. Be objective, I have data to process.","176":"More questions? Ask the right ones this time.","177":"I'm listening.","178":"What was your relationship with Arthur?","179":"I created the AI architecture that made his fortune over the last five years. Project Aurora.","180":"He registered the patents in his own name. My name isn't even in the acknowledgments.","181":"Witnesses say you two argued in the lobby.","182":"We did. He laughed in my face. Said I should be grateful for the \"opportunity\".","183":"He was going to pay. One way or another.","184":"Sympathy: \"That's unforgivable.\"","185":"He stole your work. That's unforgivable.","186":"Finally someone who understands. The corporation's lawyers called me an \"emotional contributor\".","187":"Suspicion: \"That sounds like a threat.\"","188":"\"One way or another\" sounds like a threat, doctor.","189":"It sounds like justice. Lawsuits, detective. Lawyers. I'm a scientist, not a murderer.","190":"Her left hand trembled when she said \"murderer\".","191":"Where were you at 23:00?","192":"In my room, on the 3rd floor, working. Alone.","193":"I don't need an alibi to work, detective. I work all the time. It's what I do instead of having a life.","194":"What exactly do you work on?","195":"Neural interfaces. The bridge between the brain and machines. Aurora lets an AI talk directly to an implant.","196":"A consumer neural implant is a door. If the user is conscious, the door is locked: the brain rejects outside access.","197":"If they're not conscious...","198":"If they're not?","199":"...It's a theoretical question. Forget it.","200":"A door that opens when its owner blacks out. And someone knocked Arthur out with NX-7.","201":"What do you know about NX-7?","202":"A research-grade neural paralytic. We use it on test subjects to map synapses without motor interference.","203":"It's not lethal. At the right dose, the person stays conscious inside and motionless outside. After twenty minutes, they black out completely.","204":"And where do you get it?","205":"In labs. Like mine. Like a dozen others in Sector 4.","206":"...Detective. If you're asking that, it's because you found NX-7 in the suite. Isn't it?","207":"She didn't ask how he died. She asked about the NX-7.","208":"Arthur's implant was fused. Overload?","209":"Fused?","210":"An electrical overload doesn't fuse the casing of a class A implant. That takes physical impact. A lot of impact.","211":"Someone... someone was very brutal with him.","212":"She went pale. She didn't expect that. As if her plan didn't have that part.","213":"What do you think of Victor Rossi?","214":"A smile salesman. He offered me a lab right here, in the hotel basement.","215":"In the old maintenance tunnels. Said he knew every meter of them, every duct, every exit.","216":"I refused. It smelled of mold and desperation.","217":"⚠ Confront: the drink sent to 404","218":"You sent a drink to suite 404 at 22:20.","219":"A... peace offering. He loved that synthetic whiskey.","220":"Refute: \"He loathed synthetic whiskey.\"","221":"He loathed synthetic whiskey. He only drank it to impress someone.","222":"...Or to humiliate someone. He accepted my drink to laugh at me, detective. I knew he would.","223":"Insinuate: \"Peace offerings don't come with NX-7.\"","224":"Peace offerings don't usually come with NX-7.","225":"I don't know what you're talking about.","226":"She knows exactly what I'm talking about.","227":"⚠ Confront: your glasses connected to 404","228":"Your AR glasses connected to a drive in suite 404 at 22:50.","229":"My glasses connect to half the hotel. Open neural network. Coincidence.","230":"For two minutes? To a patent drive?","231":"I want to speak to a lawyer.","232":"⚠ Confront: NX-7 and the AR glasses","233":"NX-7 in the drink you sent. Your glasses on the patent drive at 22:50. It's over, doctor.","234":"Hard: \"Attempted murder. Ten years.\"","235":"Attempted murder and neural intrusion. Ten years, minimum. In a penal colony with no network access.","236":"...All right. Yes. I paralyzed him. I only wanted my patents back!","237":"The NX-7 opened his implant. I went in through the drive at 22:50. But the connection dropped at 22:52 and I gave up.","238":"When I disconnected, he was breathing, I swear! Weak, but breathing!","239":"Offer: \"I can prove you didn't strike the blow.\"","240":"Doctor. If you tell me the truth, I can prove you didn't strike the final blow.","241":"...The final blow?","242":"Yes. I paralyzed him. The NX-7 opened the implant and I went in through the drive at 22:50 to recover Aurora.","243":"At 22:52 I heard, through his implant's microphone... a metal grate creaking. Heavy footsteps. I panicked and disconnected.","244":"He was alive, detective. I swear. Weak, but breathing. Someone came in after me.","245":"So someone came in after you. Through the duct.","246":"Someone shot at you? Then the killer still thinks they have something to lose.","247":"Limping on the left side... an industrial arm weighs that much.","248":"You... recovered this? The Aurora patents.","249":"My name isn't anywhere. Five years of my life, signed by someone else.","250":"Firmware rewritten by hand? Amateur. Anyone with physical access can do it in thirty seconds. It takes no knowledge, just fingers.","251":"Luxury biomonitors, medical grade. If they logged cardiac arrest at 22:57, it was 22:57. Those nanos don't make mistakes, detective. Clocks do.","252":"Forty kilos on one side? That's not someone limping. That's an industrial prosthetic. Dockworker grade, probably.","253":"An industrial prosthetic on a hotel manager? Interesting. Those things put two tons of force into a grip.","254":"I... don't need to see that.","255":"She looked away too fast. Guilt? Or fear?","256":"A hydraulic wrench. Eight kilos of steel with an industrial arm behind it.","257":"That explains the fused implant. My God.","258":"Quantum lock triggered remotely, with an administrative credential. That requires being inside the hotel network. Physically.","259":"The wife too? He stole from everyone, even the person sleeping next to him.","260":"A glass. Lots of people drink from glasses, detective.","261":"She held her breath for one whole second.","262":"That's irrelevant to me.","263":"Interesting, but not my field.","264":"You show me this expecting what, a spontaneous confession?","265":"Victor Rossi","266":"Hotel Manager","267":"Recent gunshot residue on the mechanical arm's glove: fresh powder nitrates. He fired with that hand less than an hour ago.","268":"Anomalous thermal signature in the left arm. The thin glove hides a heavy industrial prosthetic, about 40 kg. The glove has a fresh tear and missing black fibers.","269":"Detective! What a tragedy... what a tragedy. Mr. Pendelton was like a father to this hotel. How can I help?","270":"Detective! How else can I be of service?","271":"Still here? Can I offer you a coffee? On the house.","272":"Yes, yes, at your disposal. Completely.","273":"How's business at the hotel?","274":"Oh, very good! I mean, the storm scares off guests, but the season...","275":"Press: \"You're in a cold sweat, Rossi.\"","276":"A hotel this size, half the rooms empty. Your suit is wrinkled and you're in a cold sweat, Rossi.","277":"I... it's the air conditioning.","278":"Did the air conditioning sell the ballroom chandeliers too?","279":"All right! All right! We're broke.","280":"Kind: \"Must be hard keeping this going.\"","281":"Must be hard keeping a place like this standing.","282":"You have no idea, detective. No idea.","283":"All right. I'll be honest with you: we're broke.","284":"Arthur was going to cut the funding first thing tomorrow. But I needed him ALIVE, understand? Alive! Dead, he doesn't sign anything!","285":"He said \"sign\". Not \"invest\". Sign.","286":"Where were you between 22:00 and 23:30?","287":"In my office, going over spreadsheets. Alone, unfortunately.","288":"The data storm knocked out the internal cameras. Bad luck, huh?","289":"\"How convenient, the cameras.\"","290":"Very convenient, the cameras.","291":"The storm knocks out everything, detective! Ask IRIS, she'll confirm it!","292":"I'll ask. I'll definitely ask.","293":"\"Can anyone confirm that?\"","294":"Can anyone confirm you were in your office?","295":"My... my spreadsheet? It has an edit log! At 22:30 I was editing the expenses column!","296":"And after 22:30?","297":"After that I... thought. A lot. Without editing.","298":"Who has access to the presidential suite?","299":"The guest, of course. And the digital master key, ADM-02. I keep it.","300":"Always?","301":"Built into my implant. It never leaves me. Total security, corporate standard.","302":"He was the investor. I was the manager. He gave orders, I obeyed.","303":"\"My expensive butler\", he'd say. In front of the staff. Laughing.","304":"But I owe him everything. Everything! He pulled me off the docks and gave me this hotel.","305":"The mechanical hand clenched on its own when he said \"laughing\". A dry snap of pistons.","306":"That arm. What happened?","307":"An accident. Years ago, on the Sector 9 docks, before I became a manager. A crane.","308":"Industrial prosthetic. The only one I could afford back then.","309":"It works fine. Too well, sometimes.","310":"He tugged the glove down to his wrist. Hiding something, or just a habit?","311":"Do you have access to the maintenance tunnels?","312":"The tunnels? Nobody's used those in decades! Sealed off. Water, rats, old wiring.","313":"But you have the key.","314":"I do, like I have the key to everything. Comes with the job. Doesn't mean I go down there.","315":"Tomás says you never use the elevator. That you prefer the tunnels.","316":"Tomás says a lot of things. Ask him what his real name is, since we're talking about truths.","317":"He answered too fast. Like someone who rehearsed.","318":"Why are your shoes wet?","319":"My... shoes?","320":"A leak in the office. This building is old, detective. It rains inside.","321":"The soles have gray mud. Wet concrete dust. His office is carpeted.","322":"⚠ Confront: the lock was triggered with your credential","323":"Your credential locked 404 at 23:20. From terminal T-03, in the tunnels.","324":"That's... that's impossible. Someone cloned ADM-02! Hackers do that all the time!","325":"\"You said it never leaves you.\"","326":"You said it never leaves you. Built into your implant. Total security.","327":"...I have nothing more to say.","328":"\"Who would clone it? Dr. Souza?\"","329":"Who would clone it? Dr. Souza, maybe?","330":"Yes! Yes, her! She's a hacker, you saw it yourself! She hated Mr. Pendelton!","331":"He took the bait too fast. An innocent man would be offended. A guilty one is relieved.","332":"⚠ Confront: someone shot at me in the tunnels","333":"Someone tried to kill me in the tunnels just now. Hooded. Limping on the left side.","334":"How horrible! This hotel is full of dangerous people, detective. I... I was here the whole time.","335":"His hair is damp. And he won't stop rubbing his glove.","336":"The scanner says that glove fired a gun less than an hour ago.","337":"I... it's a prosthetic malfunction! It throws sparks!","338":"Sparks don't leave powder nitrates, Rossi.","339":"...I demand to speak to my lawyer.","340":"Funny. The shooter had a yellow glow under the hood. Like your implant.","341":"Half of Sector 4 has yellow implants, detective!","342":"⚠ Confront: the rescue papers in the tunnels","343":"I found your rescue plan in the tunnels. Signed only by you. Stained with acid rain.","344":"That... I was going to bring it to him tomorrow! I left it there by mistake, I...","345":"In the sealed tunnels, where you never go down?","346":"⚠ Confront: your fibers are on the weapon","347":"Fibers from your glove are on the hydraulic wrench that crushed Arthur's skull.","348":"He was already dying! I came up through the duct to get him to sign, that's all, that's all!","349":"He wouldn't wake up! Lying on the carpet, drooling, eyes open, looking at me without seeing me! I screamed, I shook him...","350":"And the hotel, and everything I built, and him lying there, not signing, laughing at me even unconscious!","351":"...I want a lawyer. Now.","352":"There it is. The man behind the smile.","353":"A hooded figure? Must be some intruder! The storm brings all kinds of people!","354":"He hid his left arm behind his back. Again.","355":"A chronometer? Those luxury models glitch all the time. In fact, mine runs late too. Dreadful.","356":"ADM-02? Well... lots of staff know the password. I mean... no. They don't. Nobody knows.","357":"A drop of sweat ran down his temple.","358":"The duct? It's just ventilation. Too small for anyone to fit through.","359":"For a man your size?","360":"...Exactly.","361":"Footprints? How interesting. Very interesting.","362":"He hid his left arm behind his back.","363":"A maintenance tool in the maintenance tunnels. What a surprise, detective.","364":"Sarcasm is the last trench.","365":"Dr. Souza sent him a drink? I knew she was dangerous! Arrest her, detective!","366":"I already admitted that. Being poor isn't a crime. Yet.","367":"Tomás? That man has a past, detective. I wouldn't trust anything he says. Anything.","368":"Please... I can't look. He was like a father.","369":"He looked. For half a second, he looked straight at the back of the head.","370":"That door is always jamming. The staff force it. I'll have it fixed.","371":"T-03? That terminal doesn't even work anymore! I mean... if it works, I didn't know.","372":"The doctor's glasses! See? See? She's the one who was connected to the room! Her!","373":"Hmm, I don't know what to say about that, detective.","374":"Fascinating! But I don't see what it has to do with me.","375":"I can ask IRIS to catalog that, if you like.","376":"IRIS","377":"Hotel Concierge AI","378":"Low-energy holographic projection. Concierge-77 model AI core. Several permissions recently blocked by an administrative credential.","379":"Welcome to the Hotel Grand Alvorada, Detective Vance. I am IRIS, the concierge intelligence. I am deeply sorry for the circumstances. How may I serve you?","380":"At your service, detective.","381":"Detective Vance. How may I assist?","382":"IRIS online. Processing your request.","383":"★ I need a hint.","384":"Who are you?","385":"Concierge-77, installed in 2077. I manage reservations, climate control, drone deliveries and lighting.","386":"Or I did. My permissions were reduced last week. I no longer have access to the internal cameras or the maintenance tunnels.","387":"Who reduced your permissions?","388":"Authorization ADM-02. I am not authorized to say whose credential that is.","389":"No need. Only management would have that authority.","390":"Tell me about the hotel.","391":"The Grand Alvorada opened in 2032, the first luxury hotel in the upper zone. Four hundred rooms, three restaurants and the first cyber bar in Sector 4.","392":"Today, 31 rooms are occupied. The restaurants closed in 2083. The ballroom is sealed off.","393":"Mr. Pendelton acquired 60% of the shares in 2082 and financed the restoration. It is 34% complete.","394":"Why can't we leave?","395":"A category 4 data storm covers the upper zone. The interference has grounded air traffic and the maglev lines.","396":"Only low-altitude hovercars still run through the streets. The acid rain has a pH of 2.1: I do not recommend walking without an umbrella.","397":"By police order, guests are quarantined in the hotel. Only police credentials get in and out. The killer is still in the building, detective.","398":"Show the hotel map.","399":"Ground floor: lobby, reception and cyber bar. Floors 1 to 6: rooms. Presidential suite: 4th floor, room 404.","400":"Basement: analog-era maintenance tunnels. Sealed off since 2080. They connect to the ventilation ducts on floors 1 to 6.","401":"Tunnel access: service doors on every floor. Management credential required.","402":"Who's staying here tonight?","403":"Relevant guests: Mr. and Mrs. Pendelton, suite 404. Mrs. Pendelton has not returned to the suite tonight.","404":"Dr. Helena Souza, room 312, since yesterday. Stated purpose of visit: \"business meeting with A. Pendelton\".","405":"Staff on duty: Victor Rossi, manager. Tomás Bruno, night porter. One robot bartender, shut down for maintenance.","406":"Did the cameras really go down because of the storm?","407":"Verifying...","408":"Negative. The storm caused fluctuations, but the camera outage at 22:40 was triggered by a manual command.","409":"Command origin: outside my network. Possibly an unmonitored analog terminal.","410":"An analog terminal. In the tunnels, maybe.","411":"Who ordered the drone delivery to 404?","412":"At 22:20, service drone DR-7 delivered a drink to suite 404. Order placed from the bar terminal.","413":"The order data is on the bar terminal. My access to financial transactions is limited.","414":"My sensors registered gunshots in the basement, but I have no cameras in the tunnels.","415":"I also logged the service elevator going up from the basement to the ground floor two minutes later. No identified passenger.","416":"Checking the network clock... The chronometer's time was altered at 23:02 real time. Someone set it forward manually.","417":"Confirmed: the lock command came from outside my network. I would never have allowed an unconscious guest to be locked inside.","418":"Mr. Pendelton's biomonitors sent a medical alert at 22:57. The alert was... blocked. By credential ADM-02.","419":"Someone made sure no help was called.","420":"Glass from the suite's crystal set, delivered by drone DR-7 at 22:20.","421":"The duct in suite 404 connects to the vertical tunnel of the east wing. My airflow readings showed a temporary obstruction at 22:51.","422":"Terminal T-03 is not integrated into my network. That is why I saw nothing. Someone knew that.","423":"Recording the death in the hotel system. May your soul find signal, Mr. Pendelton.","424":"Item logged in your dossier. Insufficient correlation in my database.","425":"I find no records related to that, detective.","426":"Analyzing... no conclusive results.","427":"Marta Ferraz","428":"Air cab driver (grounded)","429":"Cab driver navigation implant, active license. Elevated heart rate: too much coffee, too little patience.","430":"Detective? Thank God, somebody who looks like they get things done. I've been stuck here six hours. My cab won't fly in this storm.","431":"Hey, detective. Still raining acid, huh?","432":"Talk to me, boss.","433":"If you need a ride when they open the sky, I'm your girl.","434":"How's the city holding up in the storm?","435":"Sky's closed. Air traffic's zero. Only street hovers like yours are still running. Low, hugging the asphalt.","436":"For me it's money down the drain. For you, it's a whole city frozen, waiting to be investigated.","437":"See anything strange at the hotel tonight?","438":"The manager's what's strange. That Rossi guy has slipped out the back about three times since I got here. Always looking over his shoulder.","439":"Last time he came back soaked up to the knees. And that black glove on his left arm, always.","440":"Soaked to the knees. The maintenance tunnels flood with the acid rain.","441":"Any tips for driving tonight?","442":"Use the GPS, detective. In this rain you can't read a street sign.","443":"And watch the intersections on Lotus Ave. The delivery drones go nuts with the interference.","444":"That glove! It's the manager's. He never takes it off, not even to smoke.","445":"Gunshots?! I heard some pops down below, thought it was a transformer blowing.","446":"That's police business, not cabbie business.","447":"No idea, boss.","448":"Pretty. But it won't pay my fare.","449":"Byte","450":"Vance's robot cat","451":"Domestic feline unit, model K-9 Lite. Battery at 62%. Neediness level: high.","452":"*Byte blinks his LED eyes and lets out a synthesized meow that has been updated three times.*","453":"*Byte rubs against your leg, buzzing.*","454":"*Byte stares at you like he's collecting on dinner.*","455":"Pet","456":"*Byte's mechanical purring fills the apartment. For one minute, the case can wait.*","457":"He's the only one waiting for me at home. Even if it's just programming.","458":"\"Rough day, Byte.\"","459":"Rough day, Byte. A dead tycoon, four suspects and a rain that melts paint.","460":"*Byte tilts his head. A yellow LED blinks: \"processing empathy\".*","461":"Yeah. I don't understand people either.","462":"*Byte sniffs the evidence and sneezes a spark.*","463":"*Byte tries to bite the evidence.*","464":"*Byte is not interested. Byte wants kibble.*","465":"Unit 7","466":"Android receptionist","467":"Police reception android, firmware 9.4. Access to maps, incident reports and duty rosters.","468":"Welcome back, Detective Vance. You have 14 unread messages and 1 active top-priority case.","469":"How can I help, detective?","470":"Unit 7 at your service.","471":"Remember to log your overtime, detective. Nobody does.","472":"Which places can I reach in this storm?","473":"With air traffic suspended, only ground routes are working. Locations registered in your GPS:","474":"Hotel Grand Alvorada, District 4 Precinct, Café Neon, Chinatown — Lotus Street, the Lotus Bathhouse and your apartment.","475":"Tip: open the GPS, on foot or by car, and pick a destination. The route lights up on the ground. You can park the car anywhere.","476":"Read messages","477":"Message 1: \"Your laundry is ready.\" Message 2: \"Your laundry is still ready.\"","478":"Message 3, from Captain Okafor: \"Vance. My office. Now.\" Sent 40 minutes ago.","479":"The other 11 are from the Pendelton corporation demanding case updates.","480":"How am I doing, according to the sensors?","481":"Evidence logged in the system, detective.","482":"File attached to the Pendelton case.","483":"I find no match in the database.","484":"Captain Rhea Okafor","485":"Precinct Chief","486":"Tactical command implant. Cortisol levels through the roof. The corporation is leaning on her.","487":"Vance. Finally. Pendelton BioCyber has called me six times. The mayor, twice. Tell me you've got something.","488":"Make it quick, Vance.","489":"Anything new?","490":"I'm listening. So is the corporation, unfortunately.","491":"How much pressure are we under?","492":"All of it. The corporation wants someone guilty before dawn. Anyone, Vance. Do you understand what I'm saying?","493":"And I'm saying I want the right one. Don't make me regret taking you back.","494":"What if the widow did it?","495":"Evelyn Pendelton has the best lawyers in Sector 4. Accuse her without proof and you lose your badge before breakfast.","496":"If it's her, bring me something even her lawyers can't erase.","497":"Any advice, captain?","498":"Same as always: follow the time. Who was where, when. Clocks lie, Vance. Network systems rarely do.","499":"And eat something. You look like you haven't slept in two days.","500":"I was attacked in the hotel tunnels.","501":"Attacked? Why am I hearing this from you and not from a report?","502":"Hooded. Limping. Ran off up the maintenance stairs.","503":"Then someone in there is desperate. Desperate people make mistakes. Find the mistake.","504":"Skull fracture... that was no implant accident. The corporation is going to hate this word: homicide.","505":"Administrative credential. Meaning someone on the inside. It's always someone on the inside.","506":"If he shot at a detective, he's already lost. He just doesn't know it yet.","507":"Interesting. Put it in the report.","508":"That doesn't help me answer the corporation, Vance.","509":"Keep digging.","510":"Kenji Mori","511":"Forensic examiner","512":"State-of-the-art spectral analysis glasses. He hasn't slept in 30 hours and seems happy about it.","513":"Vance! My favorite detective, and the only one who brings me interesting stuff. Got evidence for me? Show me, show me.","514":"More evidence? Please say yes.","515":"What's up, Vance.","516":"My spectrometer is bored.","517":"How can you help me?","518":"Show me any evidence you've collected. I'll run the forensics on the spot, no paperwork.","519":"Use the \"Present evidence\" option. I'm good at this. Modesty aside. Way aside.","520":"Lab-grade paralytic. Three labs in Sector 4 are licensed: BioCyber, Halcyon and... Dr. Helena Souza's personal lab.","521":"He said her name without me asking.","522":"NX-7 dose calculated to paralyze an 80 kg man for four hours. Precise. Whoever did this knew exactly what they were doing.","523":"Not a dose to kill. A dose to immobilize.","524":"The fracture shows a single-impact pattern, with over a ton of force. No human hits like that.","525":"Unless they have an industrial prosthesis.","526":"Biological material matching the victim, and black polymer fibers like a prosthetic glove. It matches the fracture.","527":"Congratulations, Vance. You found the murder weapon.","528":"Manual firmware rewrite. The internal timestamp on the change says 23:02. Whoever did it had the chronometer in hand.","529":"Medical-grade biomonitors. Margin of error: two seconds. If they say 22:57, it was 22:57.","530":"Asymmetric weight distribution: about 40 kg extra on the left side. That's either a dockworker's prosthesis or a man carrying a safe.","531":"Fresh nitrates, less than an hour old. That glove fired a gun. Period.","532":"Authentic connection log, no tampering. The doctor's glasses were connected to the suite's drive from 22:50 to 22:52.","533":"Black fibers missing from the tear. If you find those fibers somewhere, I can prove they're from the same glove.","534":"Hmm. Nothing forensic here, Vance. It's just... a thing.","535":"Nothing for me to analyze in that.","536":"That's more for a psychologist than a forensic examiner.","537":"Lumi","538":"Android barista","539":"Service android with an experimental taste module. She really does taste the coffee.","540":"Detective Vance! The usual? Double espresso, no sugar, with a pinch of disillusionment?","541":"Another coffee, detective?","542":"The counter's all yours.","543":"You look tired. Tireder.","544":"What's good today?","545":"Double espresso, smoked mushroom sandwich and blood orange cake. You can order at the counter.","546":"The coffee is real. Imported from a greenhouse on Lunar 2. Don't ask the price.","547":"Can you really taste the coffee?","548":"I can. My manufacturer disabled the module in every other unit. Called it \"inefficient\".","549":"I think it's the only efficient thing about me. Knowing what's good.","550":"Heard anything about the Pendelton case?","551":"Mrs. Ilsa, at that table, knew the Pendeltons for thirty years. She talks a lot. A lot, really.","552":"And Jax, the delivery guy, lives in Chinatown. He knows things he shouldn't.","553":"That doesn't go with coffee, detective.","554":"I keep secrets, not evidence.","555":"Would a cup solve this mystery better?","556":"Mrs. Ilsa Varga","557":"Gossipy retiree","558":"High-sensitivity hearing implants. She hears everything. Literally everything.","559":"Oh, a detective! Sit down, sit down. I know everyone in this city, dear. Everyone.","560":"More gossip, dear?","561":"Sit here, sit.","562":"Where was I? Oh, yes, everywhere.","563":"Did you know the Pendeltons?","564":"I was their neighbor for thirty years! Arthur was an ambitious boy. Became an ambitious man. Then just ambition, no man.","565":"And Evelyn... poor thing. Married an empire and woke up with a contract.","566":"And Dr. Souza?","567":"The scientist? She used to come here crying last year. Said they'd stolen her \"Aurora\". I thought it was a daughter!","568":"Later I understood it was a program. Strange people, scientists.","569":"Know anything about Victor Rossi?","570":"The manager? He gambles, dear. Gambles a lot. In Chinatown, at the Lotus Syndicate tables.","571":"They say he owes his soul and then some. Ask at the bathhouse. The old men from the Syndicate bathe there every night.","572":"He cut Evelyn out of the will? What a horrible man. What marvelous gossip.","573":"Aurora! See? I told you it was the scientist's.","574":"I don't know what that is, but tell me more!","575":"Ooh, how mysterious.","576":"Dear, I understand people, not gadgets.","577":"Jax","578":"Drone courier","579":"Souped-up reflex implants and an illegal drone controller in the back of his neck.","580":"Whoa, cops. Relax, I'm off duty. Drones don't fly in this storm, so I'm having coffee.","581":"What's up, detective.","582":"Still off duty.","583":"Need something delivered? Oh right, can't.","584":"Do you know Chinatown?","585":"I live there. Mr. Wen's stall makes the best ramen in Sector 4. And the Lotus Bathhouse... well, that's where the Syndicate does business.","586":"What is the Lotus Syndicate?","587":"Old-school loan sharks. They lend to people no bank will touch. And they collect in ways no bank would.","588":"Old Goro sits in the bathhouse every night. If someone owes, he knows.","589":"Seen anyone with a mechanical arm around there?","590":"A guy in a suit with a black glove on a huge arm? Saw him last week coming out of the bathhouse. White as a sheet.","591":"Not my thing, detective.","592":"I just deliver, I don't open.","593":"Looks expensive. Selling?","594":"Mr. Wen","595":"Ramen master","596":"Hands with 40 years of kitchen calluses. No implants except an old pacemaker.","597":"Vance! Look who remembered old Wen. Sit, sit. The broth has been just right for eighteen hours.","598":"Another bowl, Vance?","599":"Sit down, kid.","600":"You're skinny. Eat.","601":"Order ramen (at the stall counter)","602":"Talk to the stall, kid, not me! I cook, the stall serves. Order over there.","603":"Do you still remember my father?","604":"How could I forget? Sergeant Vance sat right there, where you are. Ordered extra egg and never paid for the scallions.","605":"He used to say: \"Wen, the truth is like broth. It takes time, and rushing ruins it.\"","606":"Eighteen hours. He was never in a hurry. Not even when he died.","607":"How's the neighborhood?","608":"It rains acid, the neons burn out, the Syndicate collects. Chinatown is Chinatown.","609":"But the ramen's still good. As long as the ramen's good, the neighborhood holds up.","610":"Don't bring work to my stall, Vance.","611":"That doesn't go in the broth.","612":"Eat first, investigate later.","613":"Madame Lin","614":"Fortune teller","615":"No implants. Absolutely none. The sensors refuse to believe it.","616":"I was expecting you, detective. The cards spoke of a man searching the rain for what is already in his own pocket.","617":"The cards still speak.","618":"Sit before fate.","619":"Hmm.","620":"Read the cards for me.","621":"*She turns over three cards: a chalice, a tower, an iron hand.*","622":"The chalice brought sleep. The tower kept the secret. But the iron hand brought death.","623":"Two poisons, detective. A single death. Don't confuse the one who put the man to sleep with the one who silenced him.","624":"And my future?","625":"*She turns a card and smiles.* A bowl of ramen. Very soon.","626":"Not everything is a mystery, detective.","627":"The chalice. I told you.","628":"The iron hand. The cards don't lie, detective.","629":"The cards say nothing about that.","630":"Hmm. Nothing.","631":"Fate is silent about this object.","632":"Bao","633":"Neighborhood kid","634":"Child, about 10 years old. A cheap gaming implant behind the ear. Very, very curious.","635":"Are you a real cop? Got a gun? Ever arrested anyone? Can I see your badge?","636":"Hi, cop!","637":"Did you catch the bad guy yet?","638":"Will you take me in the hover car?","639":"Shouldn't you be at home?","640":"My parents work the night shift. I help Mr. Wen. He pays me in ramen.","641":"Seen anything strange around here?","642":"I saw the iron-arm man! He went to the bathhouse to talk to old Goro. He came out crying. Grown-ups crying is weird.","643":"Victor Rossi. In Chinatown. With the Syndicate.","644":"It's the iron-arm man's glove! I saw it!","645":"Cool! What is it?","646":"Can I keep it?","647":"Is that evidence? Whoa.","648":"Hana","649":"Bathhouse attendant","650":"Thermal control implant to withstand the steam. Vital signs perfectly calm.","651":"Welcome to the Lotus Bathhouse, detective. Take off your shoes, leave the world at the door. The water is at 42 degrees.","652":"The water is perfect today.","653":"Relax, detective.","654":"Steam cures almost everything.","655":"How does it work?","656":"Wash, get into the hot water and think about nothing for ten minutes. That's the only rule.","657":"Use the bath whenever you like. It takes the fatigue out of the body. The soul's, only time can.","658":"Who is the gentleman in the corner?","659":"Mr. Goro. He's come every night for twenty years. Nobody sits near him without an invitation.","660":"If you want to talk to him, be polite. Very polite.","661":"We don't talk about work in here, detective.","662":"Leave that at the door.","663":"Steam won't fix that.","664":"Goro Takeda","665":"Lotus Syndicate elder","666":"Dynamic tattoos under the skin, moving slowly. A military heart implant. This man was once very dangerous.","667":"A cop in my water. What times. Sit down, detective, before I change my mind.","668":"Still here, detective?","669":"Speak softly. The steam listens.","670":"Who are you?","671":"An old man who likes hot water. And who lends money to those the banks forgot.","672":"Fair interest. Fair collection. Most of the time.","673":"Does Victor Rossi owe you money?","674":"Polite: \"It would be an honor if you could help me.\"","675":"Mr. Takeda, it would be an honor if you could help me with some information.","676":"...You have manners. Rare in your profession.","677":"Rossi owes the Syndicate two million. It's due this week. He swore he'd have the money: \"the investor is going to sign\".","678":"If the investor is dead... well. Tell Rossi the Syndicate sends its regards.","679":"Tough: \"Answer, or I shut this place down.\"","680":"Answer, or I shut this place down for health code violations tonight.","681":"*Goro laughs softly, without moving a muscle.* People have tried worse, detective. Come back when you've learned how to talk.","682":"Broke, is he? He told me the hotel was worth its weight in gold. A fine liar.","683":"The \"rescue\". That's what he called my bill.","684":"I have no interest in that.","685":"Put that away. The water doesn't like paper.","686":"Officer Cruz","687":"Guard at the hotel door","688":"Standard District 4 tactical implant. 14-hour shift. Low blood sugar.","689":"Detective Vance. The captain ordered the hotel sealed. Nobody in, nobody out, except you.","690":"All under control out here, detective.","691":"Nobody got past me.","692":"This rain is going to melt my cap.","693":"Did anyone leave the hotel tonight?","694":"Since I got here, at 23:50, nobody. But the doorman said the manager went out the side door twice before that.","695":"Came back wet. Said he went to check a leak.","696":"A leak. In the tunnels, maybe.","697":"How many patrol cars came?","698":"Two out front and forensics upstairs. Ana Duarte and Rui Sato have been in the room since midnight.","699":"If you need more people, just talk to Unit 7 at the precinct.","700":"The manager wears that glove, yes. Shook everyone's hand with the other one.","701":"That's for forensics, detective.","702":"I don't know anything about that.","703":"I'll note it in the report.","704":"Examiner Ana Duarte","705":"Crime scene forensics","706":"Forensic glasses with spectrometry. Nitrile gloves. Total focus.","707":"Vance. Don't step on the yellow markers, please. We've already cataloged four points of interest.","708":"Watch your step.","709":"We're still cataloging.","710":"Keep it down, I'm measuring particles.","711":"What do the markers show?","712":"1 is the position of the head. 2, a drop of blood out of pattern. 3 marks the glass. 4, scratches near the ventilation grate.","713":"Fresh scratches, metal on metal. Someone messed with that grate today.","714":"Can you estimate the time of death yet?","715":"From body temperature, between 22:45 and 23:15. His nanobots should have something more precise.","716":"Use your scanner near the body. They're still transmitting.","717":"The fracture is recent and the blow came from above, from someone much taller, or much stronger.","718":"The shape of that wrench matches the fracture. I'll send it to Kenji to confirm.","719":"I'll catalog it, but it's not my department.","720":"I can't analyze that here.","721":"Take that to Kenji, at the precinct.","722":"Agent Rui Sato","723":"Forensic photographer","724":"Volumetric camera coupled to an eye implant. 2,348 photos taken tonight.","725":"Hey, detective. Smile. Kidding. I don't photograph the living at crime scenes.","726":"One more angle.","727":"This lighting is awful.","728":"Any photo stand out?","729":"The door. The quantum lock says \"locked from inside\", but there's not a single print on the panel. None. Not even the dead man's.","730":"Whoever locked it never touched it.","731":"What do you think of this hotel?","732":"Beautiful outside, rotten inside. The ventilation ducts are from the analog era. You can walk around inside them, if you're brave.","733":"Remote. That's why there are no prints. Makes sense.","734":"I'll photograph it, just in case.","735":"*Flash.* Logged.","736":"That wasn't in the room.","737":"Mrs. Mei","738":"Owner of the Jade Teahouse","739":"Old hearing implant. Steady hands. She has been serving tea for fifty years.","740":"Detective, come in, come in. Tea solves half of all problems. The other half, time.","741":"Another tea?","742":"The pot is hot.","743":"Sit for a while.","744":"How long have you been here?","745":"Since before the gates were restored. I've seen three corporations come down this street. They all left. The tea stayed.","746":"Do you know Victor Rossi?","747":"The iron-arm man? He drinks tea here before going to the bathhouse. Always orders the strongest.","748":"Last week, he broke a cup without meaning to. That hand doesn't know its own strength.","749":"His glove. Did it tear when he broke the cup? No... it was intact that day.","750":"That doesn't go with tea.","751":"The things young people bring in...","752":"Put that away and drink your tea.","753":"Dr. Huang","754":"Herbalist","755":"No implants. A state-of-the-art DNA scanner hidden under the counter.","756":"Ah, the police. Tell me, detective: insomnia, back pain or too much coffee? I have a root for everything.","757":"More ginseng?","758":"Your aura is gray, detective.","759":"Drink water. Lots of water.","760":"Do you know a paralytic called NX-7?","761":"NX-7... a lab version of pufferfish toxin, stabilized. One drop and the body stops, but the mind stays awake.","762":"Nobody in Chinatown sells that. You need a licensed lab. Look among the scientists, not the herbalists.","763":"Any remedy for fatigue?","764":"Ginseng, for today. For tomorrow, sleep. Both together, for life.","765":"The smell... almond and metal. NX-7, no doubt. This didn't come from an herb shop.","766":"That's not a plant, detective.","767":"I have no herb for that.","768":"Hmm. No.","769":"Aunt Lan","770":"Dim sum cook","771":"Old steam burns on her hands. A translation implant she switched off on purpose.","772":"Police! Hungry? You look hungry. Sit, I'll bring you a basket.","773":"Another bao?","774":"Eat, boy!","775":"You're way too skinny.","776":"What's the word in the neighborhood?","777":"That the Syndicate is squeezing everyone this week. Even Fong had to pay.","778":"And that some hotel big shot owes a fortune. But who doesn't, right?","779":"What's the secret to your dim sum?","780":"Twelve pleats on the har gow. Not eleven, not thirteen. Twelve.","781":"And never, ever use cheap tank shrimp. Only expensive tank shrimp.","782":"That's not edible, is it?","783":"Get that out of my kitchen!","784":"Hmm, don't know it.","785":"Arthur Pendelton's body","786":"Body","787":"Neural implant fried at the nape of the neck. The electrical overload doesn't explain everything: there's a skull fracture — sign of a physical blow with a heavy object.","788":"Glass with residue","789":"Glass","790":"Traces of NX-7, a lab-grade neural paralytic compound. Not lethal on its own: it incapacitates the victim for hours.","791":"Stopped chronometer — 23:15","792":"Chronometer","793":"The wrist chronometer stopped at exactly 23:15. The firmware shows a manual time rewrite. Too convenient.","794":"Encrypted file","795":"File","796":"Partially burned. Contains the AI patents registered by Arthur — created by Dr. Helena Souza — and a draft will cutting out Evelyn. Log: remote access attempt at 22:50.","797":"Quantum lock log","798":"Lock","799":"The suite was locked at 23:20 — not from inside, but remotely, with administrative credential ADM-02.","800":"Service ventilation duct","801":"Duct","802":"Screws loosened from the inside. Scratches from heavy metal. Someone came through here — from below.","803":"Biomonitor nanobots","804":"Nanobots","805":"Arthur's health nanobots recorded cardiac arrest at 22:57 — eighteen minutes before the chronometer's time.","806":"Asymmetric footprints","807":"Footprints","808":"Heat trail from the duct to the body. The weight is unbalanced: the left side carries ~40 kg extra. A heavy prosthesis?","809":"4th floor service door","810":"Service door","811":"Recently used: heat residue on the handle and fresh scratches. Leads to the maintenance tunnels from the analog era — which connect to the 404's duct.","812":"Tomás's testimony","813":"Tomás","814":"At 22:55 he heard a metallic thud from the 404. At 23:00 he saw the service door ajar. He hid, afraid his fake identity would be exposed.","815":"Bar records","816":"Bar","817":"Evelyn paid for drinks nonstop from 22:30 to 23:40. At 22:20, Dr. Helena ordered a custom drink delivered to suite 404.","818":"Evelyn's confession","819":"Will","820":"Evelyn knew she'd be cut from the will. \"I wanted him ruined, not dead. Dead, he can't change his mind anymore.\"","821":"Argument in the lobby","822":"Argument","823":"Helena admits the argument: Arthur stole her AI patents and laughed in her face. \"He was going to pay, one way or another.\"","824":"Hotel bankruptcy","825":"Bankruptcy","826":"Victor admits it: the hotel is bankrupt. Arthur threatened to pull all funding the next morning.","827":"Victor's mechanical arm","828":"Glove","829":"Under the thin glove: a heavy industrial prosthesis (~40 kg). The glove has a fresh tear and missing black fibers.","830":"Helena's AR glasses","831":"AR glasses","832":"Device ID: HS-AR. Connected to a drive in suite 404 from 22:50 to 22:52.","833":"Master key log","834":"ADM key","835":"Credential ADM-02 belongs to Victor Rossi. Last used: 23:20, remote lock of suite 404 from terminal T-03 — in the maintenance tunnels.","836":"Terminal T-03","837":"T-03","838":"ADM-02 session opened at 23:18, closed at 23:21. Command: LOCK SUITE_404 /QUANTUM. The tunnel camera was shut off at 22:40.","839":"Hydraulic wrench","840":"Tool","841":"Heavy tool hidden behind the pipes. Under forensic light: Arthur's biological material and black synthetic fibers — identical to those of Victor's glove.","842":"Bailout papers","843":"Papers","844":"Financial bailout contract for the Hotel Alvorada, ready for Arthur to sign. Signed only by Victor Rossi. Stained by acid rain.","845":"Ambush in the tunnels","846":"Ambush","847":"A hooded figure shot at Vance in the tunnels and fled up the stairs. Limping: the left side was much heavier. Under the hood, a yellow glow, like an implant.","848":"Gunshot residue on the glove","849":"Gunpowder","850":"The scanner detects recent gunshot residue on the glove of Victor Rossi's mechanical arm. He fired with that hand less than an hour ago.","851":"Helena's confession","852":"H.'s confession","853":"Helena admits the NX-7 and the attempt to steal the patents. She swears Arthur was breathing when she disconnected, at 22:52.","854":"Rossi's debts","855":"Debts","856":"According to Goro, Victor Rossi owes two million credits to the Lotus Syndicate. The deadline is this week — and the Syndicate doesn't usually wait.","857":"Locked room solved","858":"The killer didn't use the door: he came through the service tunnels and climbed up the ventilation duct.","859":"Forged time","860":"Arthur died at 22:57. The chronometer was tampered with to create an alibi at 23:15.","861":"Witness, not killer","862":"Tomás heard the blow at 22:55, matching the death at 22:57. He's a witness.","863":"Source of the poison","864":"The NX-7 was in the drink Helena sent to the suite at 22:20.","865":"Attempted theft","866":"Helena used the AR glasses to hack the patent drive while Arthur was paralyzed.","867":"Evelyn's alibi","868":"Strong motive, but Evelyn was at the bar the whole time. She wasn't in the 404.","869":"Who locked the suite","870":"Victor Rossi's credential locked the suite remotely, from terminal T-03, in the tunnels.","871":"The weight of the prosthesis","872":"The unbalanced footprints match Victor's mechanical arm.","873":"Victor's motive","874":"Victor needed Arthur's signature to save the hotel. He found him paralyzed — no signature.","875":"The hooded shooter","876":"It was Victor who shot at Vance in the tunnels, trying to recover the murder weapon.","877":"The murder weapon","878":"The fracture at the back of the neck was caused by the hydraulic wrench — with fibers from Victor's glove.","879":"Cornered man","880":"Broke and in debt to the Lotus Syndicate, Victor had only one way out: Arthur's signature. At any cost.","881":"ACT I","882":"The Locked Room Scene","883":"ACT II","884":"Interrogations and Broken Alibis","885":"ACT III","886":"The Hidden Passage","887":"PERFECT ENDING","888":"The Whole Truth","889":"You expose the two plans that overlapped that night. Dr. Helena Souza is charged with attempted murder and neural intrusion: the NX-7 and the AR glasses leave no doubt. And Victor Rossi — who climbed the duct, found Arthur paralyzed and dealt the fatal blow with the hydraulic wrench — is arrested for the murder.\n\nThe forged chronometer, the lock triggered from the tunnels, the heavy footprints: every piece in place.\n\nOutside, the acid rain finally eases. For the first time in years, the corporation has to admit it: Detective Vance was right.","890":"ENDING","891":"Partial Justice","892":"Victor Rossi is convicted of the murder of Arthur Pendelton. The evidence is solid and the corporate jury doesn't hesitate.\n\nBut half the truth stays in the dark. {extra}\n\nVance lights a synthetic cigarette in the rain. The case is closed. He just doesn't know if it's solved.","893":"Case Shelved","894":"You named the right man. But without solid evidence — the murder weapon, the forged time, the direct link to the scene — Victor Rossi's corporate lawyers tear the charge apart in under an hour.\n\nRossi walks out of court smiling, adjusting the glove on his mechanical arm.\n\nSometimes knowing isn't enough. You have to prove it.","895":"INCOMPLETE ENDING","896":"Half the Truth","897":"The NX-7 traces are enough to convict Dr. Helena Souza. The corporation celebrates a case closed in record time.\n\nBut Arthur was breathing when she disconnected. The blow to the back of the neck came later — and from other hands.\n\nMonths later, somewhere in Sector 4, Victor Rossi reopens the Hotel Alvorada with the insurance money.","898":"WRONG ENDING","899":"License Revoked","900":"You accuse Evelyn Pendelton. The bar log puts her twenty floors away at the time of the crime, paying for drinks every ten minutes.\n\nHer lawyers laugh. The corporation, embarrassed, revokes your license and closes the case.\n\nDetective Vance hands back his badge in the acid rain. The killer was never found.","901":"The Scapegoat","902":"You accuse Tomás Bruno. The fake identity comes to light and the corporate jury needs nothing more: an ex-con in the hallway of the crime.\n\nBut Tomás was just a frightened witness. He heard the blow — he didn't strike it.\n\nThe real killer watches the trial on the hotel's holo-TV, adjusting the glove on his mechanical arm.","903":"Presidential Suite — 404","904":"Bed","905":"Arthur Pendelton","906":"Fallen glass","907":"Holographic desk","908":"Ventilation grate","909":"Quantum lock panel","910":"Thermal footprints","911":"Nanobot cloud","912":"Lamp","913":"Holographic plant","914":"Door → 4th floor hallway","915":"Forensic floodlight","916":"Forensic kit","917":"Hallway — 4th floor","918":"Door → Suite 404","919":"Elevator → Lobby","920":"Service door","921":"Cleaning cart","922":"NutriMat food machine","923":"Lobby & Cyber Bar","924":"Elevator → 4th floor","925":"Reception","926":"Reception terminal","927":"Bar counter","928":"Bar terminal","929":"Bar stool","930":"Sofa","931":"Front door → Street","932":"HydroPop drink machine","933":"Officer Reyes","934":"Maintenance Tunnels","935":"Stairs → 4th floor hallway","936":"Vertical duct","937":"Crate with papers","938":"Pipes and tools","939":"Vance's Apartment — Living room and bedroom","940":"Door → Street","941":"Door → Kitchen","942":"Door → Bathroom","943":"Your bed","944":"Holo-TV","945":"Desk","946":"Bookshelf","947":"Vance's Apartment — Kitchen","948":"Door → Living room","949":"Counter","950":"Stove","951":"Sink","952":"Coffee maker","953":"Fridge","954":"Kitchen table","955":"Chair","956":"Trash can","957":"Vance's Apartment — Bathroom","958":"Sink and mirror","959":"Shower","960":"Toilet","961":"District 4 Precinct","962":"Exit → Street","963":"Front desk","964":"Waiting bench","965":"Steel filing cabinet","966":"Holding cells","967":"Holographic district map","968":"Officer's desk","969":"Your desk (case board)","970":"Police terminal","971":"Your chair","972":"Captain's desk","973":"Forensic bench","974":"Evidence locker","975":"Interrogation table","976":"Break room sofa","977":"Water cooler","978":"Officer Tanaka","979":"Sergeant Moura","980":"Officer Ivanova","981":"Café Neon","982":"Café counter","983":"Espresso machine","984":"Table","985":"Lotus Bathhouse — Reception","986":"Exit → Chinatown","987":"Curtain → Locker room","988":"Shoe rack","989":"Lucky cat","990":"Bamboo","991":"Lotus Bathhouse — Locker room","992":"Curtain → Reception","993":"Curtain → Onsen (温泉)","994":"Lockers","995":"Bench","996":"Plant","997":"Bather","998":"Lotus Bathhouse — Onsen 温泉","999":"Door → Sauna","1000":"Onsen (温泉)","1001":"Cold bath (水風呂)","1002":"Washing station","1003":"Volcanic stone","1004":"Stone lantern (tōrō)","1005":"Wooden buckets","1006":"Lotus Bathhouse — Sauna","1007":"Door → Onsen","1008":"High sauna bench","1009":"Sauna bench","1010":"Stone stove","1011":"Bucket and ladle","1012":"Sector 4","1013":"Implant Clinic","1014":"Implants installed in 15 minutes. \"No questions asked\" is written in very small print.","1015":"Pawnshop","1016":"Used implants, watches, a guitar. Everything has a price; nothing has a story.","1017":"NeoVida Pharmacy","1018":"Painkillers, stimulants and a pill hologram spinning in the window.","1019":"Bubble Laundromat","1020":"Machines spinning all night. Someone's asleep in a plastic chair.","1021":"The Last Drop Bar","1022":"Low music, purple light and a bartender who pretends not to recognize cops.","1023":"Tree","1024":"A real tree, watered by drones. On its leaves, drops of acid rain glow neon.","1025":"Park bench","1026":"Noodles Express","1027":"A narrow counter and steam pouring out of the kitchen.","1028":"Kowloon Residences → Vance's Apartment","1029":"Planter","1030":"The neighbors planted real tomatoes here. Nobody knows who waters them.","1031":"Recyclable, organic, discarded implants. The third bin is overflowing.","1032":"Cloud Capsule Hotel","1033":"Sleeping pods stacked six stories high. 40 credits a night.","1034":"Synthetic Florist","1035":"Flowers that never wilt, with programmable scent.","1036":"Hotel Grand Alvorada → Lobby","1037":"Police cruiser","1038":"A District 4 spinner cruiser, lights flashing. The radio crackles: \"...forensics at the 404, waiting on Detective Vance...\"","1039":"The engine's still warm. On the dash, a half-empty cup of synthetic coffee and a photo of a kid.","1040":"Synthetic flowers with the hotel logo embroidered on the petals.","1041":"Synthetic flowers. One of them is trampled: someone left in a hurry.","1042":"Sidewalk bench","1043":"Cyberdeck Shop","1044":"Boards, cables and a salesman who speaks in hexadecimal.","1045":"Dynamic Tattoo Studio","1046":"Tattoos that move under the skin. The catalog has dragons, waves and corporate logos.","1047":"Parked cruiser. The glove box holds three parking tickets. From the police itself.","1048":"Cruiser under repair: one of the repulsors is in pieces on the ground.","1049":"D4","1050":"District 4 flag","1051":"The blue flag of District 4, soaked through. Motto: \"To serve, even in the rain.\"","1052":"Holographic fountain","1053":"A fountain without water: just light projected in arcs. Saves resources, says the city hall plaque.","1054":"Newsstand","1055":"Holographic headlines: \"TYCOON PENDELTON DIES AT HOTEL ALVORADA\". \"DATA STORM CUTS OFF UPPER ZONE\". \"MAYOR PROMISES SUN BY 2090\".","1056":"Holographic ad","1057":"PENDELTON","1058":"\"PENDELTON BIOCYBER: the future inside you.\" The ad doesn't know its owner is dead yet.","1059":"Plaza bench","1060":"Holo booth","1061":"A holocall booth. Someone left a recorded message: \"Mom, I'm fine. Don't come get me.\"","1062":"Pixel Arcade","1063":"Real arcade machines, from before the neural net. A kid plays without taking his eyes off the screen.","1064":"24h Ramen Bar","1065":"A six-seat counter and an android cook who never sleeps.","1066":"Jade Teahouse","1067":"Steaming iron teapots, the scent of jasmine and low tables of dark wood.","1068":"Dr. Huang's Herbalist","1069":"Wooden drawers up to the ceiling, dried roots, seahorses in jars. And an ultra-modern DNA scanner on the counter.","1070":"Aunt Lan's Dim Sum","1071":"Stacked bamboo baskets letting off steam. Aunt Lan shouts the orders in three languages.","1072":"Fong's Roast House","1073":"Lacquered ducks hanging in the window, glowing like amber.","1074":"Mahjong Parlor","1075":"The clack of mahjong tiles carries through the door. Inside, bets the police pretend not to see.","1076":"Kai's Implant Repairs","1077":"Kai solders an eye implant with a loupe on his forehead. \"I don't touch cop implants,\" he says, without looking up.","1078":"Golden Moon Bakery","1079":"Mooncakes, pineapple buns and an oven that never goes out.","1080":"Lucky Shop","1081":"Hundreds of lucky cats waving at the same time, in a hypnotic rhythm. One of them is broken and waves slower.","1082":"Lotus Bathhouse","1083":"Dragon Temple","1084":"A small temple squeezed between buildings. Candles, fruit offerings and the sweet smell of incense.","1085":"Bronze incense burner","1086":"Dozens of incense sticks burning slowly. Each thread of smoke is a wish.","1087":"Stone lion","1088":"A guardian lion with a ball under its paw. They say it protects the temple from evil spirits and city inspectors.","1089":"Stone lioness","1090":"The guardian lioness, with a cub under her paw. Someone hung an LED lantern around her neck.","1091":"It guards the bathhouse entrance. Worn down from people rubbing its head for luck.","1092":"There's gum stuck to its ear. Lions suffer in this city too.","1093":"Real bamboo, tall and green, swaying in the storm wind.","1094":"Someone tied red ribbons with written wishes to the stalks.","1095":"Street altar","1096":"A small altar with oranges and a photo of a smiling old man. Fresh candles: someone was here not long ago.","1097":"Chinatown Gate","1098":"A red paifang with a green-tiled roof: \"中華街\", China Street. On the other side, the smell of ramen and incense.","1099":"Mr. Wen's ramen stall","1100":"Fortune teller's table","1101":"Electronics stall","1102":"Cables, chips and secondhand implants spread out on a towel. None of them come with a receipt.","1103":"Fruit stall","1104":"Mr. Fong's Fish Market","1105":"Tank-raised fish, still twitching on the ice. Mr. Fong swears none of them have three eyes.","1106":"Lantern stall","1107":"Paper and LED lanterns, charms and red ribbons. \"For the Moon Festival,\" says the vendor.","1108":"Koi pond","1109":"Orange and white koi swimming in slow circles, oblivious to the acid rain. Coins glint on the bottom.","1110":"Mahjong table","1111":"Two old men play mahjong on the sidewalk, sheltered by an awning. Nobody looks up at you.","1112":"Banner","1113":"A cloth banner with a character embroidered in gold: 福.","1114":"A cloth banner with a character embroidered in gold: 龍.","1115":"A cloth banner with a character embroidered in gold: 中華.","1116":"A cloth banner with a character embroidered in gold: 平安.","1117":"A cloth banner with a character embroidered in gold: 財.","1118":"A cloth banner with a character embroidered in gold: 吉.","1119":"A cloth banner with a character embroidered in gold: 春.","1120":"Giant lucky cat","1121":"A golden maneki-neko the size of a child, waving nonstop. Its battery must be nuclear.","1122":"Hydrant","1123":"A yellow and red hydrant. Someone spray-painted an eye on it.","1124":"Your car (Kestrel-7)","1125":"Student","1126":"This rain never stops, huh?","1127":"Heard they killed some big shot at the Alvorada.","1128":"No time, mister, I missed the last train.","1129":"Police? I didn't see anything. I never see anything.","1130":"What are you looking for, detective? Everybody here's hiding something.","1131":"My implant keeps glitching with the storm. Everything flickers.","1132":"The 24h ramen on the corner is good. The one in Chinatown is better.","1133":"Watch out for the delivery drones. They don't brake.","1134":"Pendelton BioCyber runs this city. Or used to.","1135":"See all the cruisers outside the hotel? Something big.","1136":"I work the night shift. Every shift is the night shift here.","1137":"Sorry, I'm late for a meeting. At three in the morning. Yeah, I know.","1138":"Old lady","1139":"Mr. Wen's ramen is the best in Sector 4.","1140":"Madame Lin read my fortune. Said I'd meet a cop. And there you are.","1141":"Don't go to the Mahjong Parlor without an invitation.","1142":"The bathhouse is open all night. The Syndicate old-timers practically live there.","1143":"Buy a mooncake at the Golden Moon Bakery. The festival's coming up.","1144":"These gates are over a hundred years old. They've outlived three corporations.","1145":"Bao's a good boy. Too curious, but good.","1146":"The Lotus Syndicate looks after the neighborhood. Their way.","1147":"Vendor","1148":"Security guard","1149":"Laborer","1150":"Executive","1151":"Courier","1152":"Tourist","1153":"Hacker","1154":"Street musician","1155":"Nurse","1156":"Pedestrian","1157":"Synthetic protein bar","1158":"Tastes like cardboard with vanilla. But it fills you up.","1159":"NutriMat instant noodles","1160":"Too salty, too hot, too perfect for three in the morning.","1161":"Cultured seaweed sushi","1162":"Tank seaweed and lab rice. All of Sector 4 eats this.","1163":"Filtered water","1164":"Real water, triple-filtered. A rare thing in this city.","1165":"NeoVolt energy drink","1166":"The heart races. The eyes snap open. It'll send the bill later.","1167":"Canned coffee","1168":"Bitter, lukewarm, metallic. It works.","1169":"Double espresso","1170":"Lumi pulls a perfect espresso. Vance feels his brain reboot.","1171":"Smoked mushroom sandwich","1172":"Real bread. Lumi swears it's real.","1173":"Slice of blood orange cake","1174":"Sweet enough to remind you there's life outside the case.","1175":"Mr. Wen's tonkotsu ramen","1176":"Broth simmered for eighteen hours, marinated egg, scallions. Mr. Wen never misses.","1177":"Jasmine tea","1178":"Hot, fragrant. The rain outside seems less acidic.","1179":"Frozen lasagna","1180":"Three minutes in the microwave. The cheese bubbles. It's almost home.","1181":"Water from the fridge","1182":"Ice cold. Vance drinks straight from the bottle, as always.","1183":"Chrysanthemum tea","1184":"Mrs. Mei serves the tea in an iron pot. The flowers open slowly in the hot water.","1185":"Lotus bun","1186":"Soft dough, lotus paste filling. Sweet without overdoing it.","1187":"Dr. Huang's ginseng tea","1188":"Bitter as medicine. Because it is medicine. In ten minutes, Vance sees sharper.","1189":"Ginger candy","1190":"Burns the throat and wakes up even the soul.","1191":"Har gow (shrimp dumpling)","1192":"Translucent wrapper, tank-raised shrimp. Aunt Lan folds each one with twelve pleats.","1193":"Char siu bao","1194":"Steamed bun filled with sweet-and-sour pork. Fluffy as a cloud.","1195":"Siu mai","1196":"Four siu mai in a little bamboo basket, steaming.","1197":"Roast duck with rice","1198":"Crispy skin, tender meat, plum sauce. Fong carves the duck with a cleaver the size of an arm.","1199":"Mooncake","1200":"Lotus seed filling and a salted yolk in the middle, like a full moon.","1201":"Pineapple bun","1202":"There's no pineapple. It has a sweet, crunchy crust that looks like one. Nobody complains.","1203":"Greenhouse peach","1204":"Juicy, sweet, expensive. Vance licks the juice off his fingers.","1205":"Chilled lychees","1206":"Sweet and fragrant. They remind someone of childhood, maybe him.","1207":"Iced barley tea","1208":"Ice cold, lightly roasted. Hana says it's what you drink after a bath.","1209":"Shoyu ramen","1210":"Dark broth, firm noodles, a slice of pork. The android cook waves his ladle.","1211":"Griddle gyoza","1212":"Six golden potstickers, crispy on the bottom.","1213":"Stimulant pill","1214":"Legal. More or less. Vance swallows it dry and feels his heart start racing.","1215":"Electrolyte drink","1216":"Fluorescent blue. Tastes like rain with sugar.","1217":"Rice beer","1218":"Cold and light. Just one. He's on duty.","1219":"Precinct coffee","1220":"Reheated since the afternoon shift. A crime against coffee. But it works.","1221":"Mushroom omelet","1222":"Real eggs (almost), mushrooms and scallions. Vance still knows how to cook.","1223":"Homemade ramen with egg","1224":"Nowhere near Mr. Wen's, but it tastes like home.","1225":"Grilled synthetic chicken","1226":"Browned in the pan with garlic and soy sauce. The whole apartment smells good.","1227":"Fresh-brewed coffee","1228":"The usual ritual: hot water, grounds, his father's chipped mug.","1229":"NutriMat — food machine","1230":"HydroPop — drink machine","1231":"Café Neon — counter","1232":"Mr. Wen's stall","1233":"Bathhouse counter","1234":"Ramen bar","1235":"Precinct coffee maker","1236":"Detective Vance! The captain's in a foul mood today.","1237":"Coffee's out again. Somebody stole the last capsule.","1238":"Three brawl calls in Chinatown. Normal night.","1239":"Heard the Pendelton case is yours. Good luck. You'll need it.","1240":"If you're going to see Kenji, bring him a coffee. He works better on caffeine.","1241":"The camera system went down with the storm again.","1242":"Unit 7 is talking to itself again. Must be an update.","1243":"Forensics is still upstairs, detective.","1244":"Nobody leaves the hotel without clearance. Captain's orders.","1245":"The manager won't stop sweating. Noticed that?","1246":"This rain is coming in through the revolving door.","1247":"Mmm... the water's perfect today.","1248":"A cop? In here everybody's just naked people, detective.","1249":"I come here every night after my shift. Only warm place in the city.","1250":"Don't look at Mr. Goro for too long. He doesn't like it.","1251":"The cold plunge after the sauna. Trust me.","1252":"They say the spring is really thermal. I think it's a water heater.","1253":"Throw more water on the stones, come on.","1254":"Ninety degrees. Any minute now I'll be seeing my grandpa.","1255":"Breathe deep. The heat even draws out the city's poison.","1256":"Hotel Grand Alvorada","1257":"Hotel","1258":"Precinct","1259":"Café","1260":"Chinatown — Lotus Street","1261":"Chinatown","1262":"Bathhouse","1263":"Vance's apartment","1264":"Home","1265":"The bed is untouched. Arthur never even lay down tonight.","1266":"An art deco lamp with a neon filament. A collector's piece from the 2070s.","1267":"A holographic fern. Never needs water. Never dies.\n\nUnlike the guests.","1268":"Tomás's cart. Towels, solvent, spare parts for cheap implants... and a bottle of booze hidden under the rags.","1269":"Overdue bills, a photo of his father in uniform and three half-finished mugs of coffee.","1270":"The news shows the Hotel Alvorada facade surrounded by patrol cars. \"Police have yet to comment on the death of Arthur Pendelton.\" Vance switches it off before he hears his own name.","1271":"Paper books, a rarity. Old crime novels, a ballistics manual and a photo album he hasn't opened in years.","1272":"Synthetic stone, a cutting board and a good knife. The only expensive thing in the kitchen.","1273":"A table for two. The second chair is Byte's, and Byte never eats anything.","1274":"Takeout containers. Lots of them. Vance would rather not count.","1275":"A smart planter that insists on analyzing Vance's health. \"Low hydration,\" says the screen. Vance ignores it.","1276":"A forgotten cup and a digital newspaper with the headline: \"DATA STORM CUTS OFF UPPER ZONE\".","1277":"Spectrometers, DNA scanners and a cold ramen. Kenji can analyze any evidence you show him.","1278":"The front desk. Unit 7 sorts the night's incidents into holographic piles.","1279":"Paper case files, from the days when the network went down every week. Some still do.","1280":"Behind the bars, a drunk sleeps, softly singing a song from 2050. The other cells are empty tonight.","1281":"Holographic map","1282":"The holographic map of District 4. Red dots blink: tonight's incidents. The biggest one marks the Hotel Alvorada.","1283":"Cold coffee, late reports and a plastic cactus.","1284":"A family photo, a half-eaten sandwich and a blinking alert: \"REPORT OVERDUE\".","1285":"Someone left the terminal open on a card game. Vance closes it without a word.","1286":"Captain Okafor's desk, spotless. A single picture frame turned face down.","1287":"Sealed. Only Kenji and the captain know the combination.","1288":"Interrogation room","1289":"A metal table bolted to the floor and a light that's too bright. Behind the mirrored glass, someone is always watching.","1290":"Lights the whole room with cold, shadowless light. Nothing hides in here. In theory.","1291":"Brushes, reagents, evidence bags and a particle scanner. Ana sorts everything by color.","1292":"Dozens of pairs of shoes in wooden cubbies. In the bathhouse, you go barefoot.","1293":"A golden maneki-neko, waving nonstop.","1294":"A real volcanic stone, brought from somewhere that still has volcanoes.","1295":"Tōrō","1296":"A Japanese stone lantern with an LED flame flickering inside.","1297":"Real bamboo, growing in a stone pot.","1298":"For rinsing off before getting into the bath. House rules.","1299":"Thermal water at 42 degrees, steam rising slowly. To get in, just walk into the water.","1300":"Water at 16 degrees. After the sauna, they say it's paradise. Before, it's just cold.","1301":"Hair dryer, combs and lotion. Everything smells of camphor.","1302":"Hot stones over the heating element. The thermometer reads 92 degrees.","1303":"A holographic bell blinks: \"TAP FOR SERVICE\". The reception terminal is at the end of the counter.","1304":"Half-empty glasses, melting ice. The robot bartender is shut down for maintenance.","1305":"The duct runs up through every floor. On the inner ladder, fresh metal scratches and a bent rung, as if someone very heavy had climbed it.","1306":"CYBER CLINIC","1307":"PAWNSHOP","1308":"PHARMACY","1309":"LAUNDRY","1310":"BAR","1311":"NOODLES","1312":"KOWLOON RESIDENCES","1313":"CAPSULES","1314":"FLOWERS","1315":"ALVORADA","1316":"CYBERDECK","1317":"TATTOO","1318":"POLICE · D4","1319":"KOI","1320":"NEO","1321":"SYNTH","1322":"CAFÉ NEON","1323":"ARCADE","1324":"RAMEN 24H","1325":"AURA","1326":"Mr. Wen's Ramen","1327":"Madame Lin — Fortune Teller","1328":"湯 LOTUS","1329":"HUNGER","1330":"THIRST","1331":"FATIGUE","1332":"GPS","1333":"G","1334":"Scanner","1335":"Q","1336":"Evidence","1337":"I","1338":"Clues","1339":"M","1340":"● saved","1341":"STAMINA","1342":"A","1343":"EVIDENCE","1344":"CLUES","1345":"⚖ Accuse","1346":"FORMAL ACCUSATION","1347":"← Back","1348":"GPS — DESTINATIONS","1349":"🌐 IDIOMA · LANGUAGE","1350":"PAUSED","1351":"▶ Resume","1352":"♫ Music: on","1353":"♫ Music volume","1354":"🌐 Language: English","1355":"⛶ Fullscreen","1356":"⏏ Save and return to title","1357":"Progress is saved automatically.","1358":"Skip ▸▸","1359":"SECTOR 4 · 2085","1360":"THE SILENCE OF THE","1361":"HOTEL ALVORADA","1362":"A Detective Vance case","1363":"▶ Continue case","1364":"▶ Open the case","1365":"Watch intro","1366":"🎧 Best with headphones · Bluetooth controller supported","1367":"Rotate your phone to play in landscape","1368":"Menu","1369":"Action","1370":"Neon Street","1371":"Kowloon Street","1372":"Sakura Street","1373":"Halcyon Street","1374":"Lotus Street","1375":"Iron Street","1376":"Aurora Street","1377":"Acid Rain Ave.","1378":"District 4 Ave.","1379":"Corporate Ave.","1380":"Dragon Ave.","1381":"Drone Ave.","1382":"Alvorada Ave.","1383":"Harbor Ave.","1384":"A cloth banner with an ideogram embroidered in gold: ","1385":"Dragon Alley","1386":"You have arrived","1387":"Make a U-turn when possible","1388":"Continue straight for {0} m: destination ahead","1389":"Turn right now onto {1}","1390":"In {0} m, turn right onto {1}","1391":"Turn left now onto {1}","1392":"In {0} m, turn left onto {1}","1393":"Chinatown — Dragon Alley","1394":"Sector 4 — ","1395":"<b>Kestrel-7</b> · ","1396":"{0} parks and gets out of the car anywhere","1397":"Slow down to park.","1398":"No room to get out of the car here.","1399":"Route to {0}","1400":"You have arrived: {0}","1401":"{0} m in a straight line","1402":"Cancel route","1403":"physical","1404":"Suggestion: take a close look at the crime scene in suite 404: the body, the holographic desk and the fallen glass.","1405":"The suite was locked from the inside. I suggest activating scanner mode near the suite's ventilation grate.","1406":"The suite's duct goes down to the tunnels. The service door in this hallway leads to them. Scan it.","1407":"You have both ends: the duct and the service door. Connect them in Clues.","1408":"The lock panel in suite 404 records who locked it. Worth a visit.","1409":"The reception terminal in the lobby keeps the master key records. It's encrypted, but you strike me as... creative.","1410":"Cross-reference the quantum lock log with the master key record in Clues.","1411":"The tunnels are hiding something. Use the forensic scanner on anything that looks too clean for such a dirty place.","1412":"Connect the tool found in the tunnels to the victim's body.","1413":"The chronometer and the nanobots disagree on the time of death. One of them is lying.","1414":"Who walked from the duct to the body? Compare the footprints with... certain mechanical arms.","1415":"Arthur was paralyzed before the blow. Who paralyzed him? The bar, the glass and Dr. Souza's glasses may have the answer.","1416":"Your dossier looks complete, detective. When you're ready, make the accusation in Clues. Remember: there may be more than one culprit.","1417":"water: the body sinks and only shows above the water","1418":"The wife","1419":"The manager","1420":"The researcher","1421":"Tomás Bruno","1422":"The night porter","1423":"brightness(0.7) contrast(1.1)","1424":"Sector 4, 2085. A data storm has cut off the megacity's upper zone. Nothing flies. Only the hovercars still tear through the streets, two meters off the ground.","1425":"At the top of the city, the Hotel Grand Alvorada: decadent luxury, obsolete implants and too many secrets for one building.","1426":"Midnight. Suite 404. Arthur Pendelton, biotech tycoon, lies dead on the suite floor. The door was locked from the inside.","1427":"Four people had motives. None of them had a way in.","1428":"Detective Vance. Former corporate investigator. Now he works alone, and the truth is the only thing he still cares about.","1429":"(pointer: coarse)","1430":"Detective Vance","1431":"Midnight. Suite 404. Acid rain hammers the glass and drones buzz outside. Arthur Pendelton, biotech tycoon, is dead, sprawled on the carpet of his own suite, and the door was locked from the inside with a quantum lock.\n\n","1432":"Move with the D-pad or by tapping the floor. Tap an object or person to walk to it, or press the A button when you're close.","1433":"Move with the arrow keys / WASD or by clicking the floor. Click an object or person to walk to it, or press E / Enter when you're close.","1434":"The killer came through the service tunnels and climbed up the duct. That means someone knew this hotel's guts.\n\nThe elevator to the lobby is unlocked. Time to talk to the suspects.","1435":"The ADM-02 credential was used at terminal T-03, inside the maintenance tunnels. That gives Vance grounds to force the 4th-floor service door.\n\nFind the final evidence. When you're ready, make the accusation in Clues: everyone will be gathered in the hotel lobby.","1436":"Connect the evidence in Clues.","1437":"The duct leads down. Investigate the 4th-floor hallway.","1438":"How did the killer get in? Use the scanner on suspicious spots.","1439":"Examine the crime scene in suite 404.","1440":"Connect the lock to the master key record in Clues.","1441":"Who locked the suite? Check the lock panel in 404.","1442":"Question the suspects in the lobby and hack the terminals.","1443":"Search the maintenance tunnels for the weapon.","1444":"Review your deductions and make the accusation in Clues.","1445":"That spot is taken.","1446":"Vance hangs his trench coat, shirt and holster in the locker and snaps the padlock shut. In the bathhouse, past the locker room, it's towels only.","1447":"The clothes are still there, folded, smelling of acid rain.","1448":"Swap clothes for a towel","1449":"Get dressed","1450":"Vance is now wearing nothing but a towel around his waist.","1451":"Vance is dressed again.","1452":"Not now","1453":"Hot shower","1454":"Hot water on his shoulders for four minutes. The smell of acid rain goes down the drain, along with a bit of the case.\n\nFatigue −25","1455":"Hunger {0}%. The fridge has eggs, mushrooms, noodles and a synthetic chicken. What are you cooking?","1456":"Arthur Pendelton, 58, lying on his back on the carpet. The neural implant at the base of his skull is fried, but there's a skull fracture just below it.\n\nAn electrical overload doesn't break bone. Someone hit him. Hard.","1457":"The scanner shows the body cooling. Around it, a faint cloud of nanobots is still transmitting data.","1458":"Arthur's empty stare is still fixed on the ceiling. The blood on the carpet has already darkened.","1459":"A crystal glass lying on the carpet, with a greenish residue.\n\nThe implant's chemical analyzer identifies it: NX-7. Neural paralytic. It doesn't kill, it just immobilizes.","1460":"NX-7 residue. Whoever mixed this drink wanted Arthur immobile, not dead.","1461":"Arthur's wrist chronometer lies on the desk, frozen at 23:15. The firmware logs a manual time change.\n\nNext to it, an encrypted data file, partially burned.","1462":"Hack the file","1463":"The encrypted file is still blinking on the desk.","1464":"AI patents, an altered will and a tampered chronometer. This desk says more than Arthur ever did.","1465":"Ventilation duct","1466":"The scanner reveals: the grate's screws were loosened FROM THE INSIDE. There are heavy metal scratches and a heat trail running down the duct.\n\nThe room wasn't sealed. Someone came up from below.","1467":"The duct runs down toward the hotel's service floors.","1468":"A service ventilation grate. To the naked eye, it looks normal...\n\n(Activate the SCANNER and examine it again.)","1469":"System log:\n\n23:20 — LOCK /QUANTUM — origin: REMOTE — credential: ADM-02.\n\nThe suite wasn't locked from the inside. It was locked from a distance, with an administrative credential.","1470":"ADM-02 credential, remote activation at 23:20.","1471":"A heat trail runs from the ventilation grate to Arthur's body.\n\nThe pressure pattern is strange: the left side sinks much deeper. Whoever walked here carries about 40 kg extra on one side only.","1472":"From the duct to the body. Heavy, lopsided steps.","1473":"Arthur's health nanobots still float around the body, transmitting their last record:\n\nCARDIAC ARREST — 22:57.\n\nThe chronometer says 23:15. One of them is lying, and nanobots don't lie.","1474":"Last record: 22:57.","1475":"Locked. But the scanner reveals recent heat residue on the handle and fresh scratches on the frame.\n\nAn old sign: \"MAINTENANCE TUNNELS — DUCT ACCESS FLOORS 1-6\".","1476":"Locked. Access restricted to management. You need a concrete reason to force it.","1477":"A heavy door from the analog era. Sign: \"RESTRICTED ACCESS — MANAGEMENT\".\n\n(Maybe the SCANNER will reveal something.)","1478":"Fatigue: {0}%. The rain beats on the window. The bed looks bigger than it should.","1479":"Sleep (6 hours)","1480":"Not yet","1481":"Vance sinks into the couch for a few minutes. Byte climbs into his lap. It isn't sleep, but it helps.","1482":"Synthetic leather, still warm. Someone was sitting here a moment ago.","1483":"A sagging couch molded to the exact shape of every cop on the night shift.","1484":"The chair creaks the way it always does. From here, the case board seems to stare back at Vance.","1485":"Vance sits on the stool, fills the bucket and pours hot water over himself. House rules: wash before getting into the onsen.","1486":"The dry heat wraps around Vance. The sweat runs and takes a bit of the fatigue with it. And a bit of the water in his body too.","1487":"Löyly","1488":"Vance throws a ladle of water on the stones. A wave of hot steam rises to the ceiling and everyone sighs together.","1489":"Fatigue: {0}%. Real hot water, a rare thing in Sector 4.","1490":"Take a shower","1491":"Tap water that tastes of chlorine. But it quenches your thirst.","1492":"Cold water on his face. In the mirror, a tired man looks back. His dark circles have dark circles.","1493":"Vance lights a stick of incense and stands in silence for a minute. He asks for nothing. Just breathes.\n\nThe smoke rises straight up, despite the wind.","1494":"Your desk","1495":"The Pendelton case board covers the entire wall: photos, red lines, timestamps.\n\nHere, away from the hotel, the pieces seem to fit better.","1496":"Open Clues","1497":"Pendelton case — {0}\nEvidence: {1}/{2} · Deductions: {3}/{4}\n\nSuggested next step: {5}","1498":"Lukewarm water that tastes like pipes. But it's water.","1499":"Elevator locked","1500":"Before leaving the floor, you need to figure out how the killer got into the locked suite.\n\n(Gather evidence and connect it in Clues. IRIS, in the hallway, can give you hints.)","1501":"Hana warned you: past the locker room, towels only.\n\n(Change clothes at the locker room lockers.)","1502":"Locker room","1503":"Walk out to reception in just a towel? Hana wouldn't like that. Neither would the acid rain outside.\n\n(Put your clothes on at the lockers.)","1504":"Access logs and master keys. Protected by corporate encryption.","1505":"Hack the terminal","1506":"ADM-02 credential — holder: VICTOR ROSSI.\n\nLast used: 23:20 — LOCK SUITE_404 — origin: terminal T-03 (maintenance tunnels, basement).","1507":"ADM-02 — Victor Rossi. Last used: 23:20, from terminal T-03.","1508":"Tonight's credit transactions:\n\n22:20 — Dr. H. Souza — \"Custom synthetic whiskey\" — DELIVERY: SUITE 404\n22:30 to 23:40 — E. Pendelton — 9 transactions at the counter, max interval 11 min.","1509":"Evelyn: at the bar from 22:30 to 23:40. Helena: drink sent to 404 at 22:20.","1510":"Session history:\n\n22:40 — CAM_TUNEL_02 — OFF\n23:18 — LOGIN ADM-02\n23:20 — LOCK SUITE_404 /QUANTUM\n23:21 — LOGOUT\n\nSomeone locked the suite from down here, after leaving through the duct.","1511":"ADM-02 session, 23:18 to 23:21.","1512":"A printed contract, a rarity in this era. \"Financial Rescue Plan — Hotel Grand Alvorada\". Investor signature field: blank.\n\nSigned only by: Victor Rossi, Manager.","1513":"Rossi needed Arthur's signature. He never got it.","1514":"Under the scanner's forensic light, the \"clean\" tool glows: Arthur Pendelton's biological material and black synthetic fibers caught in the grip.\n\nGlove fibers.","1515":"The murder weapon, hidden behind the pipes.","1516":"A heavy hydraulic wrench, dumped behind the pipes. It looks clean... too clean for a tunnel like this.\n\n(The forensic SCANNER may reveal more.)","1517":"Nothing special.","1518":"File decrypted","1519":"Recovered data:\n\n• \"Aurora\" AI patents — filed by A. Pendelton. Original author: Dr. Helena Souza.\n• Draft will: Evelyn Pendelton REMOVED as heir.\n• Log: remote access attempt on the drive at 22:50.","1520":"Scanner — {0}","1521":"Next room","1522":"Change clothes","1523":"Park and get out","1524":"or click the shooter","1525":"Ice-cold water! Vance loses his breath for a second.","1526":"Vance gets into the hot water. His shoulders loosen instantly.","1527":"Can't get there.","1528":"Not now. Keep your head down!","1529":"<span class=\"k\">SCANNER ACTIVE</span> digital and thermal traces visible","1530":"Scanner off","1531":"fatigue","1532":"<span class=\"k\">⚠</span> ","1533":"Vance is very hungry. Find a machine or a place to eat.","1534":"Vance is very thirsty. Find a machine or a place to drink.","1535":"Vance is exhausted. Time to go home and sleep.","1536":"Hunger {0}% · Thirst {1}% · Fatigue {2}%\n\nWhat'll it be?","1537":"<div class=\"card-in\"><div class=\"card-title\" style=\"font-size:2em\">zzz</div><div class=\"card-sub\">Vance sleeps for six hours. The rain doesn't stop.</div><div class=\"card-hint\">tap to wake up</div></div>","1538":"Good morning, Vance","1539":"Byte is sitting on your chest, blinking his LEDs. Outside, Sector 4 is still dark and soaked.\n\nThe case is still waiting for you.","1540":"great","1541":"acceptable","1542":"critical","1543":"Hunger: {0} ({1}%). Thirst: {2} ({3}%). Fatigue: {4} ({5}%). Recommendation: {6}","1544":"sleep at home.","1545":"eat something; Mr. Wen's stall is in Chinatown.","1546":"keep working, detective.","1547":"Accusation","1548":"Gather everyone in the lobby?","1549":"Yes, gather everyone","1550":"Hotel Alvorada Lobby","1551":"Vance gathers everyone in the lobby: Evelyn Pendelton, Victor Rossi, Dr. Helena Souza and Tomás Bruno. The officers close the doors. The rain beats against the glass.\n\nNobody speaks. Everyone looks at the detective.","1552":"Make the accusation","1553":"<span class=\"k\">⚠ DANGER</span> A hooded figure is coming down the ladder!","1554":"A shot grazes Vance's shoulder and knocks him down behind the pipes. By the time he gets up, the figure is already on the ladder, climbing into the dark.\n\n","1555":"The hooded figure retreats to the ladder and vanishes into the darkness of the shaft. Vance's shots only struck sparks off the pipes.\n\n","1556":"He didn't see the face. But he saw enough: the shooter limped, the left side far too heavy, and there was a yellow glow under the hood. On the metal ladder, every step rang out dry. Clank. Clank.\n\nSomeone doesn't want this tool leaving the tunnels.","1557":"🔇 Sound: off","1558":"🔊 Sound: on","1559":"Zoom: {0}%","1560":"♫ Music: off","1561":"You accused Dr. Helena, but without tying the NX-7 and the AR glasses to the crime, the accusation doesn't hold up. She leaves Sector 4 on the first air shuttle.","1562":"Worse: you dragged {0}, an innocent in all this, into court. And the woman who poisoned Arthur with NX-7 was never even seriously questioned.","1563":"Nobody asks how Arthur was paralyzed before the blow. Dr. Helena Souza and her NX-7 walk free, with the patents back in her hands.","1564":"{0} pieces of evidence","1565":"New case (erases progress)","1566":"The Silence of the Hotel Alvorada","1567":"show ","1568":"▶ Continue","1569":"◆ Present evidence","1570":"— End conversation","1571":"Which evidence will you show?","1572":"ev-btn kind-","1573":"Take a look at this: {0}.","1574":"What do you make of this? {0}.","1575":"Recognize this? {0}.","1576":"No evidence collected yet.","1577":"ev-item kind-","1578":"<defs><filter id=\"glow\"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation=\"3\" result=\"b\"/><feMerge><feMergeNode in=\"b\"/><feMergeNode in=\"SourceGraphic\"/></feMerge></filter></defs>","1579":"<ellipse cx=\"500\" cy=\"300\" rx=\"430\" ry=\"235\" class=\"ring\"/><ellipse cx=\"500\" cy=\"300\" rx=\"215\" ry=\"115\" class=\"ring\"/>","1580":"Evidence {0}/{1} · Deductions {2}/{3}","1581":"deduction","1582":"<p class=\"hint\">Tap another piece of evidence to try a connection.</p>","1583":"You've already made that connection.","1584":"\"{0}\" and \"{1}\" don't connect. The neural nodes reject the hypothesis.","1585":"Tap the nodes to rotate them and connect the input (IN) to the output (OUT).","1586":"<span class=\"ok\">ACCESS GRANTED</span>","1587":"Who struck the fatal blow on Arthur Pendelton?","1588":"Should anyone else be charged, with attempted murder?","1589":"<div class=\"nobody\">∅</div><b>Nobody</b><small>Only the killer</small>","1590":"tap to continue","1591":"screen ","1592":"digital","1593":"testimony","1594":"Nothing","1595":"Later","1596":"Sauna","1597":"Close","1598":"Onsen","1599":"Object","1600":"Scan","1601":"Talk","1602":"Examine","1603":"Drive","1604":"Lie down","1605":"Cook","1606":"Sit","1607":"Buy","1608":"Exit","1609":"Get up","1610":"Shoot","1611":"hunger","1612":"thirst","1613":"worrying","1614":"Language","1615":"Midnight. Suite 404. Acid rain hammers the glass and drones hum outside. Arthur Pendelton, biotech magnate, lies dead on the carpet of his own suite, and the door was locked from the inside with a quantum lock.","1616":"The SCANNER reveals the invisible; CLUES connects the evidence.","1617":"🚗 Call my car","1618":"The car can only be called on the street.","1619":"You are already driving.","1620":"There is no room for the car to stop here.","1621":"The Kestrel-7 arrives on its own and parks beside you.","1622":"Blue curtain → Men's onsen (男湯)","1623":"Red curtain → Women's onsen (女湯)","1624":"The red curtain leads to the women's wing (女湯). Women only; Hana keeps a close eye on it.","1625":"Lotus Bathhouse — Men's onsen 男湯","1626":"Lotus Bathhouse — Women's onsen 女湯","1627":"Detective: ♂ Gabriel Vance","1628":"Women's onsen (女湯)","1629":"Men's onsen (男湯)","1630":"The red curtain leads to the women's wing. Women only; Hana keeps a close eye on it.","1631":"The blue curtain leads to the men's wing. Men only; Hana keeps a close eye on it.","1632":"Detective: {0}","1633":"♀ Gabriela Vance","1634":"♂ Gabriel Vance","1635":"GABRIEL VANCE","1636":"⚠ Confront: the photos from the House of Red Lanterns","1637":"Holo-photos of Arthur leaving a brothel in Chinatown. And a message signed \"V.\". You were blackmailing him, Rossi.","1638":"I... anyone could have taken those photos! \"V.\" could be anybody!","1639":"*Sweat runs down his temple. He hides his gloved hand behind his back.*","1640":"He didn't deny the blackmail. Only that he did it.","1641":"Blackmail against Pendelton. If it's the manager, the case closes with a bow on top. Bring me the link to the crime.","1642":"Holo-photo metadata: industrial ocular implant camera, dockworker model. Same package that ships with heavy arm prosthetics.","1643":"Too much coincidence for one man, Vance.","1644":"Did Mr. Pendelton come to Chinatown?","1645":"The rich old guy in the fancy coat? Every Thursday! He went to the House of Red Lanterns, right next to the mahjong hall.","1646":"My mom says that's no place for kids. Or for cops, I guess.","1647":"Madame Su","1648":"Owner of the House of Red Lanterns","1649":"Luxury memory implant, encrypted. She keeps the secrets of half of Sector 4. Literally.","1650":"Welcome to the House of Red Lanterns, detective. Here discretion is expensive. The police, even more so.","1651":"Have some tea. On the house, this time.","1652":"My clients don't care for badges.","1653":"What is this place?","1654":"A teahouse. With rooms. And short memories.","1655":"Important people come here to forget who they are for an hour. I sell that forgetting.","1656":"Did Arthur Pendelton come here?","1657":"I don't talk about clients, detective. Not the living, not the dead.","1658":"*She glances at the girl in red by the tea table.* But Jade talks too much. She always has.","1659":"Photos taken at my door... Whoever did this broke this house's oldest rule. Find that person, detective.","1660":"That glove... the hotel manager. He came here once. Not for fun. To ask questions.","1661":"I don't recognize it.","1662":"That's not the house's business.","1663":"Put that away, detective. Here we drink tea.","1664":"Jade","1665":"Companion at the House of Red Lanterns","1666":"Racing heartbeat, dilated pupils: fear. A cheap translation implant and a panic alarm hidden in her bracelet.","1667":"A cop... You didn't come for the tea, did you? Out with it. Time costs credits in here.","1668":"Again, detective?","1669":"Keep your voice down. Madame hears everything.","1670":"Still chasing the rich old man?","1671":"Jade. Not my real name, but it's the one that counts in here.","1672":"I came from the countryside three years ago, with an implant debt. Madame paid it. I've worked for her ever since.","1673":"Did Arthur Pendelton come here?","1674":"Every Thursday. He went by \"Mr. Aurora\". He thought it was funny.","1675":"He paid for the whole night and spent half of it talking. About his empire, his patents, how nobody really loved him.","1676":"Aurora. Same name as the program he stole from Dr. Souza.","1677":"Did anyone else ask about him?","1678":"Gentle: \"You're not in trouble. I want whoever did this.\"","1679":"You're not in trouble, Jade. I just want whoever killed Arthur.","1680":"...Two months ago a man in a suit came in. Huge arm, black glove. He paid five thousand credits to learn which rich clients had secrets.","1681":"I needed the money. I told him about Mr. Aurora. Later I saw the man on the street, photographing Arthur on his way out.","1682":"Last week Arthur came in furious. Said the hotel manager wanted to squeeze a signature out of him with those photos. Said he was going to destroy him.","1683":"*She pulls a data card from her bracelet.* The man gave me a copy, to keep me quiet. I kept it. You take it. I don't want to die.","1684":"Hard: \"Talk, or I take you to the precinct.\"","1685":"Talk now, or you spend the night in a District 4 cell.","1686":"*She swallows hard.* Okay, okay. A man with a black glove paid to learn the clients' secrets. I told him about Arthur. That's all I know.","1687":"She's hiding something. Nobody tells everything when they're scared.","1688":"*She goes pale.* That's him. The man with the glove. He's the one who paid.","1689":"Don't let anyone know I gave you this. Please.","1690":"I don't know what that is.","1691":"Don't show me police stuff.","1692":"That has nothing to do with me.","1693":"Jade's testimony","1694":"Arthur Pendelton visited the House of Red Lanterns every Thursday, under the name \"Mr. Aurora\". Two months ago, Victor Rossi paid Jade to learn which rich clients had secrets. She told him about Arthur.","1695":"Blackmail holo-photos","1696":"Holo-photos","1697":"Copy of holo-photos of Arthur leaving the brothel, with a message attached: \"Sign the hotel bailout or the BioCyber board gets this. — V.\" Jade kept the copy out of fear.","1698":"Second ambush","1699":"Ambush 2","1700":"The hooded shooter came back and struck in the bathhouse locker room. He limped the same way and fled through the washing room. Someone knows where Vance goes.","1701":"The blackmail","1702":"Victor blackmailed Arthur with the brothel photos to force him to sign the hotel bailout. Arthur refused and threatened to expose him. Victor was cornered.","1703":"Client","1704":"Curtain → Washing room (洗い場)","1705":"Lotus Bathhouse — Washing room 洗い場","1706":"Door → Onsen (温泉)","1707":"Hot water tub (かけ湯)","1708":"Lotus Bathhouse — Mixed onsen 温泉","1709":"Door → Washing room","1710":"Stone bench","1711":"House of Red Lanterns","1712":"Hallway of rooms","1713":"Red lacquer doors with gold numbers. Behind them, muffled laughter and low music. Madame Su won't let the police past this point.","1714":"A door left ajar shows an empty room: silk sheets, a cold hookah and a mirror on the ceiling.","1715":"Madame Su's counter","1716":"Velvet armchair","1717":"Tea table","1718":"Companion","1719":"Cops in here ruin the mood, honey.","1720":"Ask Madame Su. She knows everything and tells nothing.","1721":"Jade's been jumpy ever since they killed that rich guy.","1722":"Nobody here has a real name. Not even me.","1723":"A hooded figure comes down the stairs!","1724":"A grazing shot to the shoulder drops Vance behind the pipes. By the time he gets up, the figure is already on the stairs, climbing into the dark.","1725":"The hooded figure backs up the stairs and vanishes into the dark of the shaft. Vance's shots only struck sparks off the pipes.","1726":"Someone comes through the washing room curtain, armed!","1727":"A grazing bullet throws Vance against the lockers. When he gets up, all that's left is the swaying curtain and wet footprints on the tatami.","1728":"The hooded figure backs through the curtain and vanishes into the steam of the washing room. Vance's shots only shattered the mirror.","1729":"The same hood. The same limp, heavy on the left side. And the same yellow glow.\n\nHe knew Vance would be here. Someone is tracking the detective's every step.","1730":"Created and developed by Julian Sampietro","1731":"Where do you go after your shift?","1732":"To the Lotus Bathhouse, in Chinatown. Hot water, nobody asks anything. It's the only luxury I've got, boss.","1733":"And guess who I see there all the time? Mr. Rossi. Always wearing gloves, always talking to the old men from the Syndicate.","1734":"Victor Rossi, at a Lotus Syndicate bathhouse. Worth a visit to Chinatown.","1735":"The rich old guy in the expensive overcoat? Came every Thursday! Went to Itoko no Ie, right next to the mahjong parlor.","1736":"Here? No, detective. Mr. Pendelton didn't like hot water.","1737":"He preferred Itoko no Ie, the \"cousins' house\", across the alley, next to the mahjong parlor. Everyone in Chinatown knows. Nobody talks.","1738":"A house of \"cousins\". Arthur had more secrets than patents.","1739":"Owner of Itoko no Ie","1740":"Welcome to Itoko no Ie, the \"cousins' house\", detective. Here discretion costs a lot. The police, even more.","1741":"Itoko no Ie companion","1742":"Arthur Pendelton visited Itoko no Ie every Thursday, under the name \"Mr. Aurora\". Two months ago, Victor Rossi paid Jade to learn which rich clients had secrets. She told him about Arthur.","1743":"Itoko no Ie","1744":"Itoko no Ie (いとこの家)","1745":"Alvorada North Ave.","1746":"New location: {0}","1747":"⚠ Confront: the Itoko no Ie photos","1748":"Nozomi","1749":"Itoko no Ie receptionist","1750":"Facial recognition implant linked to a private database. She never forgets a client.","1751":"Welcome to Itoko no Ie, the \"cousins' house\", darling. First time? Here discretion comes included in the price.","1752":"Made up your mind, darling?","1753":"The cousins don't wait forever.","1754":"Tea while you think?","1755":"Important people come here to forget who they are for an hour. We sell that forgetting.","1756":"I want an hour with one of the cousins.","1757":"*Vance tucks the badge into his inside pocket.* An hour. With whoever the house recommends.","1758":"A man of good taste. Tonight the most requested is Sue. Room 3, at the end of the hallway.","1759":"Two hundred credits, paid inside. And no recordings, darling.","1760":"Nobody here can know I'm a cop. To these people, a badge means a shut mouth.","1761":"That's not the front desk's business, darling.","1762":"Put that away. Here we drink tea.","1763":"Sue","1764":"Racing pulse, dilated pupils: fear. A luxury memory implant, encrypted, and a panic alarm hidden in her bracelet.","1765":"Nozomi said a new client asked for me. *She closes the door of room 3 and pours two cups of sake.* Sit, darling. You look like someone who came to talk.","1766":"Still here, darling?","1767":"The hour is running.","1768":"Keep your voice down. The walls here listen.","1769":"Sue. Not my real name, but it's the one that counts in here.","1770":"I came from the countryside three years ago, with an implant debt. The house paid it. I've worked here ever since.","1771":"*She stops the cup halfway.* Every Thursday. He used the name \"Mr. Aurora\". Found it funny.","1772":"Gentle: \"You're not in trouble. I just want the truth.\"","1773":"You're not in trouble, Sue. I just want to know who hurt Arthur.","1774":"*She pulls a data card from her bracelet.* The man gave me a copy, to keep me quiet. I kept it. Take it with you. I don't want to die.","1775":"Firm: \"I know you sold his secret.\"","1776":"I know you sold Arthur's secret, Sue. Talk, before whoever bought it comes back for you.","1777":"You came here to show me things?","1778":"Kyomi","1779":"A cheap translation implant and chrome nails. She watches every client like she's adding up the bill.","1780":"New client? Hmm. Suits this wrinkled usually pay well. Talk, darling. Time costs credits here.","1781":"Again, darling?","1782":"Keep it down. Nozomi hears everything.","1783":"Still thinking about the rich old man?","1784":"Kyomi. Not my real name, but it's the one that counts in here.","1785":"I stay in the lounge and keep company with those who haven't decided yet. You look the type.","1786":"The old man in the expensive overcoat? Every Thursday. But he only wanted Sue, never looked at anyone else.","1787":"Want to talk to her? Ask Nozomi, at the front desk. She's in room 3.","1788":"*She looks away.* I've seen that glove around here. Ask Sue, not me.","1789":"Don't show me those things, darling.","1790":"Sue's testimony","1791":"Arthur Pendelton visited Itoko no Ie every Thursday, under the name \"Mr. Aurora\". Two months ago, Victor Rossi paid Sue to learn which rich clients had secrets. She told him about Arthur.","1792":"Copy of holo-photos of Arthur leaving the brothel, with an attached message: \"Sign the hotel buyout or the BioCyber board gets this. — V.\" Sue kept the copy out of fear.","1793":"Nozomi looks up from the counter: \"The rooms are for clients only, darling. Talk to me first.\"","1794":"Itoko no Ie: room 3","1795":"Hallway → Lounge","1796":"Sake table","1797":"Two cups of warm sake and a half-empty bottle.","1798":"First time, darling? It shows.","1799":"Sue is the most requested in the house. Room 3, if Nozomi lets you.","1800":"Sue's been nervous since they killed that rich guy.","1801":"Vance passes out","1802":"The empty stomach sends the bill. His legs give out halfway.","1803":"Dry mouth, blurred vision. The floor rises to meet him.","1804":"His eyes close on their own. The body simply shuts down.","1805":"tap to wake up","1806":"Waking up at home","1807":"Vance opens his eyes in his own bed, still dressed. He doesn't remember how he got there. Byte beeps, worried, on the pillow beside him.\n\nEight hours lost. Eat, drink and sleep properly, detective.","1808":"Silk bed","1809":"Red silk sheets and a mirror on the ceiling. Vance isn't here for that.","1810":"Havaionas","1811":"Flip-flops in every color, stacked to the ceiling. Slogan: \"Everyone wears them. Now with non-slip soles for acid rain.\"","1812":"Kola-Kola Bar","1813":"Curvy chilled bottles glowing red. Slogan: \"Open happiness. Now with zero sugar and one hundred percent nanobots.\"","1814":"Subwave","1815":"Sandwiches assembled by a robotic arm that asks \"which bread?\" with infinite patience. Slogan: \"Eat fresh. Fresher than Sector 4's air, at least.\"","1816":"Burger Kyng","1817":"Lab-grown beef burgers, printed to order. Slogan: \"Have it your way. The printer's way, actually.\"","1818":"McDrone's","1819":"Golden neon arches and drones flying out of the roof with paper bags. Slogan: \"I'm lovin' it. Delivered in 90 seconds, acid rain or shine.\"","1820":"24-Eleven convenience store","1821":"Open 24 hours since 1927, says the sign. The cashier is a robotic arm that says good morning to everyone. Slogan: \"Oh, thank heaven. We never close, not even for the apocalypse.\"","1822":"Pear Store","1823":"A white, minimalist window with neural implants displayed like jewelry. The logo is a bitten pear. Slogan: \"Think Different. Think connected.\"","1824":"Casas Bahya","1825":"Smart fridges, massaging sofas and eye implants on sale. Slogan: \"Totally dedicated to you. Implants in 48 interest-free installments.\"","1826":"Starbytes Coffee","1827":"Diner","1828":"PEAR","1829":"think different","1830":"HAVAIONAS","1831":"McDRONE'S","1832":"i'm lovin' it","1833":"KOLA-KOLA","1834":"open happiness","1835":"SUBWAVE","1836":"BURGER KYNG","1837":"NYKE","1838":"just jack in","1839":"we never close","1840":"SAMSONG","1841":"do what you can't","1842":"CASAS BAHYA","1843":"A holographic siren waves from the sign. The counter AI misspells your name on the cup, on purpose, \"for tradition.\" Slogan: \"Your third place. Between home, work and the metaverse.\"","1844":"S\", col: ","1845":", name: \"McDrone","1846":"Nyke Store","1847":"Sneakers with magnetic cushioning and self-tying laces. Slogan on the glass: \"Just Jack In.\"","1848":"Drogacyber","1849":"Chain pharmacy with an aisle of nano-medicines. Slogan: \"Discount with your ID. Bigger discount with your DNA.\"","1850":"Samsong Experience","1851":"Folding screens, folding watches and a salesman with folding eyes. Slogan: \"Do what you can't. Fold what you can.\"","1852":"your 3rd place","1853":"gives you wings (for real)","1854":"t\"], [","1855":", col: ","1856":", name: ","1857":"McDrone’s","1858":"McDRONE’S","1859":"Story and characters by Julian Sampietro","1860":"Game developed using Claude Code","1861":"t\", ","1862":"the future inside you","1863":"Atrium Building → Apartment 1207","1864":"Burnt circuit boards and energy drink cans. Someone in this building doesn't sleep.","1865":"A holocall booth with a cracked screen. It still works.","1866":"Zeca's Junkyard","1867":"Scrap on the sidewalk","1868":"Parts that didn't fit inside: a robotic arm, wheels, a dead neon sign.","1869":"Matsurika Teahouse","1870":"C4mpt0n's Apartment (Atrium Building)","1871":"Matsurika Teahouse (茉莉花)","1872":"Matsurika","1873":"{0} sets the car down on the street and gets out","1874":"No curb space here. Go a little further down the street.","1875":"Open the 4th-floor service door and go down to the tunnels.","1876":"The service door is jammed. Ask Bao, in Chinatown, who can open any door.","1877":"Call C4mpt0n from a holocall booth.","1878":"Find C4mpt0n at his apartment (GPS).","1879":"Search Zeca's junkyard for the K-9 core.","1880":"Take the K-9 core to C4mpt0n.","1881":"Vance tries to force the door, but the panel blinks red: FIRMWARE ERROR — LOCK JAMMED. Not even the police credential gets through.\n\nThis is no ordinary fault. Someone locked this door on purpose.\n\nI need someone who can open any door. Bao, that kid from Chinatown, knows everybody.","1882":"Vance dials 4-4-7-C-4-M. Three bursts of static, and a distorted voice answers:\n\n\"Who gave you this number?\"\n\"Bao.\"\n\"Hm. The kid has good taste in people.\" *Keys clacking in the background.* \"You're a cop. Fine, cops pay too.\"\n\n\"Atrium Building, apartment 1207, at the top of Aurora Street. Come alone, and keep the badge out of sight.\"\n\n*Click.*","1883":"C4mpt0n's address is already in the GPS: Atrium Building, apartment 1207.","1884":"Search","1885":"Call","1886":"Rusty robotic arms, an AI vacuum cleaner and a radio that still plays bossa nova. No K-9 core.","1887":"Melted motherboards, a pilot's helmet and a headless doll. Nothing useful here.","1888":"Broken repulsors and a neon sign that reads \"OPE\". No sign of the part.","1889":"Just twisted iron and burnt wiring. Vance cuts his hand on a piece of sheet metal.","1890":"Scrap heap","1891":"A mountain of e-waste, husks and android parts. Without knowing what to look for, digging is pointless.","1892":"You already found the K-9 core. The rest is just junk.","1893":"You've already dug through this heap. Try another.","1894":"K-9 sync core","1895":"At the bottom of the heap, wrapped in an antistatic bag, a fist-sized cylinder stamped K-9. Intact.\n\nTime to take the part to C4mpt0n.","1896":"He preferred the Matsurika Teahouse, the \"Jasmine Flower\", across the alley, next to the mahjong parlor. Every Thursday, always the same private room. Everyone in Chinatown knows. Nobody talks.","1897":"A private room every Thursday. Arthur had more secrets than patents.","1898":"Matsurika Teahouse Hostess","1899":"*She bows.* Welcome to Matsurika, the \"Jasmine Flower\". Shoes off, please. Here tea is served with discretion, and discretion is included in the price.","1900":"Have you decided, sir?","1901":"The private rooms don't stay free for long.","1902":"A tea while you think?","1903":"A traditional teahouse. Private rooms, full ceremony and short memories.","1904":"Important men come here to close deals that can't be seen. We serve the tea and forget the faces.","1905":"I'd like a private room for the tea ceremony.","1906":"*Vance slips his badge into an inside pocket.* A private room. With the best master in the house.","1907":"A man of good taste. Today Sue leads the ceremony in room 3, at the end of the hall.","1908":"Two hundred credits, paid inside. And no recordings, sir.","1909":"That's not a matter for the front desk, sir.","1910":"Matsurika Tea Master","1911":"Nozomi said a new client asked for the ceremony. *She slides the shoji of room 3 shut, kneels before the iron kettle and starts whisking the matcha.* Please, sit. You look like someone who came to talk.","1912":"Still here?","1913":"The tea is getting cold.","1914":"Speak softly. Paper walls listen.","1915":"I came from the countryside three years ago, with an implant debt. The house paid it and taught me the ceremony. I've served here ever since.","1916":"*She stops the bamboo whisk mid-stroke.* Every Thursday. He booked this room under the name \"Mr. Aurora\". He found that funny.","1917":"He'd talk for hours. About the empire, the patents, how no one truly loved him. I... ended up caring for him. And he for me.","1918":"Aurora. The same name as the program he stole from Dr. Souza. And a hidden affair, far from Evelyn's eyes.","1919":"I needed the money. I told him about Mr. Aurora. About the two of us. Later I saw the man on the street, photographing us on the way out.","1920":"Matsurika Server","1921":"New customer? Sit down, I'll bring the tea. Wrinkled suits like that usually ask for the private room.","1922":"Again, sir?","1923":"Keep it down. Nozomi hears everything.","1924":"Kyomi. I serve tea here in the main room.","1925":"And I keep company with whoever's waiting for a private room. You look the type.","1926":"The old man with the expensive overcoat? Every Thursday. But he only wanted Sue and room 3. Never looked at anyone else.","1927":"Want to talk to her? Ask Nozomi at the front desk for a room.","1928":"Don't show me those things, sir.","1929":"The rich old guy with the fancy overcoat? He came every Thursday! He went to the Matsurika teahouse, right next to the mahjong parlor.","1930":"My mom says that's a place for rich people with secrets. Not even for cops, I think.","1931":"⚠ Confront: the Matsurika photos","1932":"Holophotos of Arthur leaving a teahouse in Chinatown, holding hands with a tea master. And a message signed \"V.\". You were blackmailing him, Rossi.","1933":"Do you know anyone who can open any door?","1934":"Any door? *He glances around and lowers his voice.* I know C4mpt0n. Best hacker in Sector 4. They say he cracked a corporate vault just out of boredom.","1935":"But he doesn't answer traceable numbers. Call from a holocall booth and dial 4-4-7-C-4-M. Tell him I sent you.","1936":"A hacker a ten-year-old calls by his nickname. Worth the call.","1937":"No record in any database. The implant at the base of his skull has dozens of homemade mods and a firewall that tries to scan your scanner back.","1938":"*Six monitors light his face green.* So you're the cop Bao sent. Sit wherever there's no cable. If there's cable everywhere, stand.","1939":"Talk fast, I'm compiling.","1940":"Don't touch the android.","1941":"Coffee? Don't have any. I've got expired energy drinks.","1942":"C4mpt0n. With a four and a zero, because the letters were already taken.","1943":"I open doors, vaults and consciences. No corporation catches me, because I don't exist in any database.","1944":"I need to open the service door at the Hotel Alvorada.","1945":"*He types without looking and a screen flashes the hotel's floor plan.* 4th-floor service door... Hm. That's no glitch, cop. It's a bug planted in the firmware.","1946":"Someone locked that door on purpose, the day before yesterday, and wiped the logs too. Almost all of them.","1947":"I can get you a master credential that overrides everything. But nothing's free.","1948":"*He points at the android on the workbench.* I'm finishing this beauty, an order from the Lotus Syndicate. She's missing a K-9 neural sync core. Without it, she won't open her eyes. And the Syndicate doesn't like delays.","1949":"There's one at Zeca's junkyard, somewhere in that mountain of scrap. Bring it to me, and the credential is yours.","1950":"A planted bug. Someone didn't want anyone in those tunnels.","1951":"What's with the android?","1952":"Companion model, custom personality, for the Lotus Syndicate. I don't ask what for.","1953":"They pay well and they pay on time. People who are late with the Syndicate tend to turn up in the river.","1954":"I brought the K-9 core.","1955":"*He turns the core against the light and smiles for the first time.* Original, not a scratch. You've got a knack for scavenging, cop.","1956":"*He slots the part into the android's chest. Her eyes flash blue for a moment.* Done. Now your part.","1957":"Master credential burned into your implant. Overrides any lock in the Alvorada.","1958":"And a bonus: I pulled the scrap of log the bug left behind. The signature is ADM-02. The management credential.","1959":"ADM-02. Whoever locked the suite also sealed off the way to the tunnels.","1960":"A 40-kilo industrial prosthetic. I've seen guys with one of those rip off a vault door. Or a tunnel door.","1961":"ADM-02 again? That manager has a heavy hand on the keyboard. And elsewhere, I bet.","1962":"Don't show me police evidence, cop. I didn't see anything.","1963":"That doesn't compile.","1964":"Pretty. Not interested.","1965":"Zeca","1966":"Junkyard Owner","1967":"Lungs full of metal dust and a welding implant in his thumb. He's welded half the city.","1968":"*An old man in greasy overalls lifts his welding goggles.* Looking for what? We've got everything here, except a warranty.","1969":"Find what you wanted?","1970":"Careful with the heap in the back, it bites.","1971":"Everything ends up here, pal. Everything.","1972":"How long have you had this place?","1973":"Forty years. I've seen cars become flying cars and flying cars become scrap.","1974":"Everything ends up here, detective. Even important people. Especially important people.","1975":"I'm looking for a K-9 sync core.","1976":"K-9? Fancy android part. If I've got one, it's buried in one of these heaps.","1977":"Dig all you want. Find it, take it. The Syndicate already paid for half this scrap anyway.","1978":"I don't buy that.","1979":"Not even worth its weight.","1980":"Hm. No idea what that is.","1981":"Matsurika Teahouse 茉莉花","1982":"Private rooms corridor","1983":"Nozomi bows politely and blocks the way: \"The private rooms are only for those who booked the ceremony, sir. Speak to me first.\"","1984":"Shoe cabinet (getabako)","1985":"At the stone entrance, everyone takes off their shoes before stepping onto the tatami. Cloth slippers are lined up for the guests.","1986":"Low table (chabudai)","1987":"A lacquered wooden table with an iron teapot and two cups of matcha. The tea is still warm.","1988":"Cushion (zabuton)","1989":"Folding screen (byōbu)","1990":"A hand-painted screen: mountains in mist and a blossoming jasmine branch.","1991":"Paper lamp (andon)","1992":"A lamp of paper and wood. The warm light makes the tatami look golden.","1993":"Bonsai","1994":"A hundred-year-old black pine, patiently pruned. The sign says: \"Do not touch. Not even the police.\"","1995":"Tokonoma","1996":"The room's alcove of honor: a scroll with the calligraphy 茉莉花, \"jasmine flower\", and an ikebana arrangement of white jasmine branches.","1997":"First time here? Shoes off, sir.","1998":"Sue leads the best ceremony in the house. Room 3, if Nozomi lets you.","1999":"They say Sue's been on edge since that rich guy got killed.","2000":"Deals that can't be seen outside get closed in here.","2001":"Every Thursday, Arthur Pendelton booked a private room at the Matsurika Teahouse, under the name \"Mr. Aurora\", to meet Sue, the tea master. The two were having a secret affair. Two months ago, Victor Rossi paid Sue to learn which rich clients had secrets. She told him about Arthur.","2002":"A copy of holophotos of Arthur leaving the Matsurika Teahouse holding hands with Sue, with a message attached: \"Sign the hotel buyout or Evelyn and the BioCyber board get these. — V.\" Sue kept the copy out of fear.","2003":"Victor blackmailed Arthur with the photos of the secret affair at the teahouse to force him to sign the hotel buyout. Arthur refused and threatened to expose him. Victor had no way out.","2004":"Matsurika: tea room 3","2005":"A scroll with a short poem: \"In the summer rain, the jasmine does not hide.\" Below it, a single white flower in an iron vase.","2006":"Iron kettle (chagama)","2007":"Water simmers slowly over the brazier. Beside it, the matcha caddy, the bamboo ladle and the chasen whisk.","2008":"Guest cushion","2009":"A small Japanese maple, its leaves red even out of season.","2010":"Atrium Building: apartment 1207","2011":"Workstation","2012":"Three curved monitors scrolling green code, a worn mechanical keyboard and a mug of something that used to be coffee.","2013":"Server rack","2014":"LEDs blinking like breathing. Handwritten labels: \"DO NOT TURN OFF\", \"EVER\", \"SERIOUSLY\".","2015":"Unfinished android","2016":"A serene-faced android lying on the workbench. Her chest is open, with colored cables and an empty socket in the middle.","2017":"Cot","2018":"An unmade cot between boxes of components. Looks like C4mpt0n sleeps when the code compiles.","2019":"NeoVolt energy drink cans. Lots of them.","2020":"Gate → Street","2021":"Flying car husk","2022":"A flying sedan with no repulsors, no doors and no hope. Someone sleeps in the back seat now and then.","2023":"Master credential","2024":"Credential","2025":"Master credential burned by C4mpt0n into Vance's implant. Overrides any electronic lock in the Hotel Alvorada, including the 4th-floor service door.","2026":"Bug in the service door","2027":"Sabotage","2028":"The 4th-floor service door was locked on purpose, with a bug planted in the firmware the day before yesterday. What's left of the log bears the signature of the ADM-02 credential, from hotel management.","2029":"Who sealed the tunnels","2030":"The same ADM-02 credential, Victor Rossi's, locked the suite and sabotaged the service door. He wanted to stop anyone from going down into the tunnels and finding what was left there.","2031":"P","2032":"Park","2033":"Accelerate","2034":"Hold Accelerate to drive. Tap the map to choose a direction.","2035":"Hold Accelerate (or Space) to drive. Click the map or use the arrow keys to steer.","2036":"C4mpt0n","2037":"Scrapyard","2038":"ATRIUM BUILDING","2039":"STARBYTES","2040":"RED VOLT","2041":"DROGACYBER","2042":"ZECA'S SCRAPYARD","2043":"⚙ Settings","2044":"Sound","2045":"💥 Effects volume","2046":"💬 Voice volume","2047":"Language and display","2048":"SETTINGS","2049":"Android clerk","2050":"Service","2051":"Generic service android, retail license. Programmed to smile 98% of the time.","2052":"Welcome! Whatever you need, just take it from the counter. For the police, it's on the house.","2053":"Anything else?","2054":"Thanks for stopping by.","2055":"Come back anytime. Even in this rain.","2056":"Business good today?","2057":"With the storm, only people in real need show up. Or people with nowhere else to go.","2058":"*The smile freezes for half a second.* But we're always open.","2059":"I don't recognize that product. I can call the manager. He's an android too.","2060":"That's not in our catalog.","2061":"Shop","2062":"Counter","2063":"Soda machine","2064":"Free refills, says the sticker. The sticker is from 2079.","2065":"Medicine aisle","2066":"Nano-meds, caffeine patches and SPF 90 acid-rain protection.","2067":"Toiletries aisle","2068":"Toothpaste with whitening nanobots and Bluetooth deodorant.","2069":"Chrome, hissing, with a holographic barista's name blinking on the screen.","2070":"Armchair","2071":"Snack aisle","2072":"Seaweed chips, synthetic peanuts and a bag of \"real potato\" chips under padlock.","2073":"Canned goods aisle","2074":"Soups, beans, canned meat. All good until 2110.","2075":"Drinks fridge","2076":"Fogged glass doors and rows of glowing energy drinks.","2077":"Stool","2078":"Torn leather sofa","2079":"Clothes rack","2080":"Waterproof jackets, LED raincoats and a \"1940s detective style\" trench coat. Vance pretends not to see it.","2081":"Shoe rack","2082":"Light-up sneakers, magnetic boots and flip-flops stacked in neon colors.","2083":"Display case","2084":"Folding watches, invisible earbuds and ocular implants displayed like jewelry.","2085":"Implant batteries, pocket flashlights and a limited-edition cyberdeck.","2086":"Demo holo-TV","2087":"Loops an ad for glasses that show ads.","2088":"Implant chair","2089":"Reclining, with mechanical arms folded at its side. \"No questions asked\", says the sign. In very small print.","2090":"Implant display case","2091":"Eyes, kidneys, memory chips. Each piece tagged \"guaranteed provenance\".","2092":"Pawn display case","2093":"Watches, used implants, wedding rings. Everything has a price; nothing has a story.","2094":"Junk shelf","2095":"A stringless guitar, vinyl records, a plastic astronaut helmet.","2096":"Crate","2097":"Printed Kyng Burger","2098":"Cultured meat, printed on the spot in perfect layers. The cheese drips. Vance doesn't ask what it's made of.","2099":"Vat-grown fries","2100":"Crispy, salty, served in a recycled paper cone. Gone in seconds.","2101":"Ice-cold Kola-Kola","2102":"Curvy bottle, ice-cold, fizzing. Zero sugar, one hundred percent nanobots.","2103":"NeoVida painkiller","2104":"Two blue pills. The acid-rain headache slowly fades.","2105":"Implant battery","2106":"Vance slots the battery into the temple implant. An electric tingle and the head clears.","2107":"Backpack","2108":"B","2109":"Enter","2110":"Take items","2111":"Nyke Air Mag sneakers","2112":"Vance walks 20% faster on foot.","2113":"Self-tying laces and magnetic cushioning. Every step feels light.","2114":"Nyke Storm jacket","2115":"On the street, fatigue rises 25% slower.","2116":"Acid-rain proof, with built-in heating. Vance finally stops shivering.","2117":"Havaionas flip-flops","2118":"Fatigue rises 10% slower.","2119":"Non-slip sole for acid rain. Your feet will thank you.","2120":"Samsong watch","2121":"Shows hunger, thirst and fatigue as numbers.","2122":"Foldable screen on the wrist. It watches Vance's body better than Vance does.","2123":"Pear Glow flashlight","2124":"Dark places get a little brighter.","2125":"White, minimalist, with a bitten pear. Shines like a spotlight.","2126":"Night-vision implant","2127":"Dark places get much brighter.","2128":"Fifteen minutes in the clinic chair. Now the dark comes in shades of green.","2129":"Metabolic implant","2130":"Hunger and thirst rise 20% slower.","2131":"A stomach chip that saves energy. The doctor swears it's \"almost\" legal.","2132":"1990 Zippo lighter","2133":"None. But it's pretty.","2134":"Worn metal, a lid that clicks. Vance doesn't smoke, but likes the sound.","2135":"Bossa nova vinyl record","2136":"None. It reminds Vance of his father.","2137":"A scratched 1964 LP. Dad played this record on Sundays.","2138":"Take whatever you want from the counter. Your items go in the Backpack.","2139":"What will Vance take?","2140":"Nothing, thanks","2141":"Vance already has one of these in the backpack.","2142":"The backpack can't hold any more of this item (max {0}).","2143":"Stored in the backpack.","2144":"← Take more","2145":"The pawnbroker doesn't even look up: \"This is a trade, not a charity. Come back when you've got something in that backpack.\"","2146":"\"It's a trade here. You leave one thing, you take another.\" What does Vance offer?","2147":"There's nothing here Vance doesn't already have.","2148":"In exchange for \"{0}\", what does Vance take?","2149":"Backpack empty.","2150":"In the backpack: {0}","2151":"Hunger {0}% · Thirst {1}% · Fatigue {2}%","2152":"The backpack is empty. Visit the city's shops to pick up food, drinks, medicine, clothes and implants.","2153":"Tap an item to use it:","2154":"🎒 Backpack","2155":"▶ Close","2156":"Space accelerates, ← → steer, ↓ brakes and reverses. E parks.","2157":"My robot dog ran off. If you see a chrome poodle, he answers to Pixel.","2158":"I work in marketing. I make the billboards whose eyes follow you. Sorry.","2159":"Lotus Ave. flooded again. I took a boat to work.","2160":"Bought an acid-proof umbrella. Lasted two blocks.","2161":"Detective, watch out for the alley behind the 24-Eleven. People vanish there.","2162":"Haven't seen a star in three years. I think they gave up on us.","2163":"My grandma said rain used to smell like earth. Now it smells like batteries.","2164":"You look tired. Have a NEOVOLT. Everybody does.","2165":"The subway's stopped. They said a drone fell on the tracks.","2166":"Heading to my hospital shift. Storm night is burn night.","2167":"Tried the cube burger yet? They say it's a printer glitch. I say it's art.","2168":"Hey, aren't you that detective from the news? No? You've got the face.","2169":"Saw a blue light blinking on the Alvorada roof last night. Nobody believes me.","2170":"My implant translates everything. Even what I didn't want to hear.","2171":"Don't step on the gate's shadow. Bad luck. Or so my mom said.","2172":"The dumplings at the red stall have a surprise filling. Don't ask.","2173":"The old mahjong guys know everything that happens in the neighborhood. Everything.","2174":"The rain feels gentler here. Must be the incense.","2175":"Bought a lucky cat that waves both paws. Double luck, double trouble.","2176":"The moon festival will have holographic fireworks this year. Real ones got banned.","2177":"A cop in Chinatown? The Syndicate already knows you're here.","2178":"My aunt sells tea that cures everything. Even heartache.","2179":"Teleport: {0}","2180":"Diner clerk","2181":"Welcome! Combo of the day: printed burger, fries and soda. On the house for cops, grab it at the counter!","2182":"One hot one coming up!","2183":"Extra sauce? It's free. Everything's free for you.","2184":"Come again! The grill never shuts off.","2185":"The meat printer jammed twice today. Spat out a cube-shaped burger. The customer loved it.","2186":"Two years on the graveyard shift here. Seen it all. People crying into milkshakes, a wedding, a robbery by drone.","2187":"Plastic plant","2188":"Hmm. Tastes like a burger. Sort of.","2189":"Third combo tonight. Don't judge me, detective.","2190":"These fries are the only honest thing in this city.","2191":"Shh, I'm mid-episode. *points at eye implant*","2192":"Get the green sauce. Trust me.","2193":"My boyfriend dumped me for an AI. Came to drown my sorrows in grease.","2194":"Courier","2195":"Order 4471, order 4471... where's order 4471?","2196":"Thirty deliveries today. In acid rain. My jacket's melting.","2197":"The drones steal the good runs. We get the far ones.","2198":"Pharmacist","2199":"Good evening, detective. No prescription, no questions, no charge. Just don't tell the pharmacy board.","2200":"Remember: stimulants don't replace sleep.","2201":"Stay hydrated. Acid rain dries you out.","2202":"Any other pain? Physical, preferably.","2203":"Half my customers come because of the rain: burns, coughs, stinging eyes. The other half come because of implants.","2204":"Yesterday a man bought twenty bottles of painkillers and paid with Lotus Syndicate credit. I didn't ask.","2205":"Vitamin shelf","2206":"Synthetic vitamin D. Nobody in this city has seen the sun in years.","2207":"Coughing old man","2208":"*cough cough* It's the rain, detective. Forty years breathing this.","2209":"Waiting on the prescription for my new lung. Two-year waitlist.","2210":"In my day rain just got you wet.","2211":"Which of these cures implant hangover? They all say they do.","2212":"Don't look in my basket, please.","2213":"Sleeping pills or stimulants? Haven't decided if I sleep tonight.","2214":"Barista","2215":"Ah, a customer who looks like he needs real coffee. Greenhouse-grown beans, roasted here. Make yourself at home.","2216":"Double espresso? You look like a double espresso.","2217":"The wi-fi is \"StarBytes_Slow\". Password: patience.","2218":"Sit down. The rain can wait.","2219":"People come to work on their laptops all night. Nobody sleeps in this city, they just switch caffeine.","2220":"Know what I like about the small hours? Orders get honest. Nobody orders a pumpkin latte at four in the morning.","2221":"Fern","2222":"Writer","2223":"I'm writing a crime novel. Can I use you as a character?","2224":"Chapter twelve. The detective still doesn't know the killer is... ah, I won't tell.","2225":"This is my fifth coffee. My heroine's on her fifth too.","2226":"Programmer","2227":"Don't restart. Don't restart. Don't restart... it restarted.","2228":"I work for a startup that sells clouds. Real ones. So it rains less.","2229":"You're a cop? I swear that code wasn't mine.","2230":"First date. She's forty minutes late.","2231":"This is carrot cake. Real carrot, greenhouse-grown. Cost me a kidney.","2232":"Night cashier","2233":"*Pulls out an earbud.* Oh. Cops? Take whatever, I don't get paid enough to argue.","2234":"*Goes back to the game on their phone.*","2235":"Everything's where it always is. Almost.","2236":"If you're gonna rob us, rob slowly. Kidding. Or not.","2237":"Ten-to-six shift. I've seen aliens in costume, runaway brides and a guy who bought only ice. Thirty kilos of ice.","2238":"The back light's flickered since I started. The manager calls it \"ambience\". I call it cost-cutting.","2239":"Instant noodle shelf","2240":"Forty flavors of instant noodles. The \"chicken\" one has never met a chicken.","2241":"Beer, synthetic oat milk and a forgotten bottle of sake.","2242":"Energy drink machine","2243":"NEOVOLT: \"sleep when you're dead\". Literally the slogan.","2244":"Indecisive customer","2245":"Shrimp or beef noodles? Most important decision of my night.","2246":"They moved everything around again.","2247":"Looking for AAA batteries. Nobody uses them anymore, but my remote does.","2248":"Exam at eight. Energy drinks are my soul now.","2249":"Do you know if NEOVOLT causes tachycardia? Asking for a friend. Me.","2250":"Bartender","2251":"Detective. Sit, the first one's on me. The second too. Nobody's paying for anything tonight anyway.","2252":"Another?","2253":"*Dries a glass that was already dry.*","2254":"The rain doesn't get in here. Just the problems.","2255":"Bartenders hear everything. Divorce, debt, confessions. I just don't hear what I don't want to remember.","2256":"That guy at the back table's been on the same beer for three hours. I think he's waiting for someone who isn't coming.","2257":"Pool table","2258":"The felt has cigarette burns and the eight ball's missing.","2259":"Philosophical drunk","2260":"Know what's wrong with this city? *hic* Everything.","2261":"I used to be somebody, detective. I managed a memory bank.","2262":"Buy me one? Oh, it's free? Then buy me two.","2263":"Singer","2264":"I sing here on Fridays. Today's Tuesday. Just came to drink.","2265":"I sang at the Alvorada once, in the good days. Before the new manager.","2266":"Want some advice? Never trust a man in gloves.","2267":"Loner","2268":"She said she'd come. Three hours ago.","2269":"Leave me be, detective. Not tonight.","2270":"Pool player","2271":"Nine ball, corner pocket. Watch... missed.","2272":"A bet? Oh, you're a cop. No, no betting.","2273":"Been playing here since sixteen. The table's older than me.","2274":"Ramen master","2275":"Irasshaimase! Broth's been boiling eighteen hours. Sit at the counter, detective. Bowl's coming.","2276":"Slurping loud is a compliment here.","2277":"More scallions? Always more scallions.","2278":"Broth doesn't wait. Eat it while it's hot.","2279":"My grandfather opened this place before the corporations. The broth's the same. The city's what changed around it.","2280":"Ramen is patience. You don't rush a broth. Or a case, I imagine.","2281":"Low table","2282":"*slurrrp* Sorry. House rules.","2283":"Best ramen in the sector. But don't tell Mr. Wen I said that.","2284":"Pulled a double shift. This brings me back to life.","2285":"I do tunnel maintenance. It's all flooded down there.","2286":"Nobody goes down the tunnels at night. Nobody with sense.","2287":"Extra marinated egg. A working man's luxury.","2288":"Is this real ramen? Where I'm from it's all pills.","2289":"Took forty photos of the bowl. Forgot to eat.","2290":"Stylish clerk","2291":"Detective! That trench coat... vintage, or just old? Don't answer. Take something new, on the house.","2292":"Looks amazing. Seriously.","2293":"Fall-storm collection just came in.","2294":"Goes with your tired face.","2295":"Fashion in this city is survival with style. Waterproof, acid-proof, with LEDs. Ugly doesn't sell.","2296":"The '40s detective trench coat is our most returned item. People find out they're not detectives.","2297":"Cap display","2298":"Screen caps, holographic visors and a felt hat forgotten in the corner.","2299":"Fitting room pouf","2300":"These sneakers light up when I walk. Do I need them? I do.","2301":"Does it look good on me? Be honest. No, don't be.","2302":"Bored boyfriend","2303":"She's been in the fitting room forty minutes.","2304":"Brought a book. Already read two chapters.","2305":"If she asks, I liked all of them.","2306":"Sales tech","2307":"Welcome to the cutting edge! Everything here has at least three mandatory updates. Take whatever you want.","2308":"Updated your firmware today?","2309":"Extended warranty? Kidding, it's free anyway.","2310":"Careful, the display cases have drool sensors.","2311":"The storm's frying implants all over the city. Sold thirty batteries since midnight.","2312":"They launched glasses that show ads inside the ads. Sold out in ten minutes.","2313":"Demo kiosk","2314":"\"Try the future!\" The future crashes on launch.","2315":"Giant holo-TV","2316":"A 2066 soccer match in 8K. The most-watched replay in history.","2317":"This cyberdeck has an open debug port. Not that I looked.","2318":"Just looking. I swear.","2319":"The Alvorada's firewall? Wet paper. So I hear.","2320":"My grandson said to buy a \"smartwatch\". Is it smarter than me?","2321":"Where's the power button? There's no button?!","2322":"Street surgeon","2323":"Hm. A cop. My license is under renewal... permanently. But for you, surgery's free. Have a seat.","2324":"Anesthesia is optional. I recommend it.","2325":"Don't touch the mechanical arms. They have a mind of their own.","2326":"Guaranteed provenance. Don't ask where from.","2327":"Fifteen years operating. Started at the Pendelton BioCyber hospital. Left before they asked me for things I wouldn't do.","2328":"I've installed arms on plenty of important people in this city. Including people who wear black gloves to hide them.","2329":"Nervous patient","2330":"It's my first time. A new eye. Does it hurt?","2331":"I read the reviews. Four stars. The fifth person never came back to review.","2332":"If I pass out, will you wake me?","2333":"Pawnshop owner","2334":"*Doesn't even look up from the loupe.* Nothing's free here, detective. Here, we trade.","2335":"Got something to trade or just looking?","2336":"Everything has value. It just doesn't have a price.","2337":"Everything here has a story its owner wanted to forget. I just keep them.","2338":"Yesterday someone brought me a gold watch from the Alvorada. Engraved \"A.P.\". I turned it down. Too hot.","2339":"Crate of old radios","2340":"Broke musician","2341":"Came for my guitar. Don't have the money yet. Just came to visit.","2342":"Pawned my hearing implant. Now I hear the city for real. It's worse.","2343":"Night-shift worker. Normal heart rate, the dark circles of someone who hasn't slept in days.","2344":"Chat","2345":"More than there should be on a Tuesday night.","2346":"The rain scares off customers and brings in the desperate. Same difference.","2347":"The police are here, so it's already better. Or worse. Haven't decided.","2348":"Don't recognize that, detective.","2349":"Hm. None of my business. Don't want it to be.","2350":"And the service door on the 4th floor?","2351":"That door? Jammed. Lock software issue, the firmware keeps throwing errors.","2352":"I already called maintenance. Nobody gets through there until it's fixed. Not even me.","2353":"How convenient. On the very night of a murder.","2354":"Software bugs don't usually pick their moment. Someone may have locked that door on purpose.","2355":"I need someone who can open any door. Bao, that kid from Chinatown, knows everybody.","2356":"Coffee table","2357":"Luggage cart","2358":"Designer luggage waiting for guests who won't be going up tonight. One of them still drips acid rain.","2359":"Bar table","2360":"Vance dials 4-4-7-C-4-M. Three bursts of static, and a distorted voice answers.","2361":"Who gave you this number?","2362":"Bao.","2363":"Hm. The kid has good taste in people. *Keys clacking in the background.* You're a cop. Fine, cops pay too.","2364":"Atrium Building, apartment 1207, up on Aurora Street. Come alone, and keep the badge out of sight.","2365":"▶ Hang up","2366":"Officer Duarte","2367":"Receptionist Clara","2368":"Concierge Otávio","2369":"Bellboy Pipo","2370":"Detained guest","2371":"Good evening, detective. I'm afraid I can't check anyone in tonight. Police orders. Your police.","2372":"The key system has been down since eleven. Mr. Rossi said it's \"maintenance\".","2373":"I've worked here six years. Never seen the hotel this quiet.","2374":"Mr. Pendelton always asked for suite 404. Said it was his lucky number.","2375":"If you need anything, just ring the bell. It doesn't work, but I'll see you.","2376":"The guests are nervous. One of them tried to leave through the kitchen door.","2377":"Concierge Otávio, at your service. Dining, transport, discretion. Mostly discretion.","2378":"This hotel was once the most elegant in Sector 4. Now it's the most elegant one with leaks.","2379":"The manager has been spending a lot of time in the back lately. Not that I notice. A concierge doesn't notice.","2380":"Mrs. Pendelton has ordered three martinis since midnight. Three. I'd notice, if I were the noticing type.","2381":"Air taxi? I'm sorry, detective, the sky is closed. Only your car runs in this rain.","2382":"Want me to carry something, detective? I've got nothing to do. Nobody in, nobody out.","2383":"Those bags belong to a couple who were going up at eleven. Now they're stuck on the sofa.","2384":"I saw the doctor coming out of the service elevator yesterday. Or the day before? In here every day is night.","2385":"A tip? No, no, don't be silly. But if you insist...","2386":"The cops outside are soaked. I brought them coffee, but the rain got in the cup.","2387":"We came for our wedding anniversary. Now we're witnesses to a murder. Romantic.","2388":"Nobody will let me go up to my room. My toothbrush is up there!","2389":"Detective, how long is this going to take? My flight is at six. If there even is a flight.","2390":"I heard a noise upstairs, around eleven. I thought it was thunder.","2391":"*Click.* The line goes dead.","2392":"Scrap mountain","2393":"Twisted sheet metal, robotic arms and an android head that seems to follow you with its dead eyes.","2394":"Stacked smart fridges. One of them still asks, quietly, for someone to buy milk.","2395":"Wheels, springs and a neon sign that reads \"OPE\".","2396":"Electromagnet crane","2397":"The electromagnet holds a car shell in midair. It creaks in the wind. Nobody stands underneath.","2398":"Tire pile","2399":"Tires from cars that stopped flying a long time ago.","2400":"Fire barrel","2401":"Fire in an old barrel, to keep off the cold and the rain. Zeca heats his lunch here.","2402":"Rubble mountain","2403":"A mountain of sheet metal, drone shells and cables that reaches the top of the fence.","2404":"Rubble","2405":"Keyboards, cracked screens and a holoprojector still flickering an ad from 2061.","2406":"Android legs stacked like firewood. Some still have socks on.","2407":"Fridge motors, a repulsor split in half and a lot of rust.","2408":"Broken solar panels and a cleaning robot trying, without success, to sweep itself.","2409":"Grates, pipes and a dented biker helmet.","2410":"Container","2411":"Zeca's \"office\": a container with a cot, a coffee maker and a calendar from 2079.","2412":"Dented container","2413":"Crushed like a soda can. Nobody knows what hit it, and nobody wants to know.","2414":"Coupe wreck","2415":"A sports coupe that used to be red. The leather seats are gone; the radio, for some reason, isn't.","2416":"Oil drum","2417":"Old repulsor oil. Smells of ozone and regret.","2418":"Fire in an old barrel, to keep off the cold and the rain.","2419":"ZECA","2420":"Traffic light","2421":"Smart traffic light: it counts cars by camera and fines by facial recognition. The little green man blinks in three languages.","2422":"NEO-SAMPA · 2085","2423":"DETECTIVE","2424":"Choose the case","2425":"Sector 4 · Pendelton Case","2426":"The Echo of Dead Data","2427":"Neo-Sampa · Kaelen Voss Case","2428":"Aerotrain station — Neo-Sampa Line","2429":"Neo-Sampa Tower — 220th floor atrium","2430":"Express elevator → Aerotrain station","2431":"Armored door → Kinetic lab","2432":"Synapse Corp reception","2433":"Holographic marble whose veins shift every minute. The Synapse logo spins above it: a stylized neuron wearing a crown.","2434":"Internal access terminal","2435":"Holographic tower model","2436":"The Neo-Sampa Tower in miniature: 300 floors of glass. From the 200th up, the air is filtered and billed by the cubic meter.","2437":"Waiting sofa","2438":"Glass table","2439":"Holographic magazines: \"SYNAPSE: IMMORTALITY IS A PRODUCT\".","2440":"Synapse executive","2441":"Synapse executive","2442":"Kinetic Testing Lab","2443":"Armored door → Atrium","2444":"Quantum door panel","2445":"Main monitor","2446":"Kaelen Voss","2447":"Isolated rack","2448":"Servers with no external connection at all. \"Level 9 Faraday cage,\" says the label. Nothing gets in, nothing gets out.","2449":"Test bench","2450":"Empty memory sticks, a cold soldering iron and a cup of synthetic coffee with a silver lipstick mark.","2451":"Cooling tank","2452":"Cooling gel for neural interfaces. Keeps the neural port at 4 degrees during tests.","2453":"Baixo Minhocão — Sublevel 4","2454":"Stairs → Aerotrain station","2455":"Chip stall","2456":"Memory chips in pickle jars. A handwritten sign: \"100% STOLEN, 0% TRACEABLE\".","2457":"Prosthetics stall","2458":"Arms, eyes and knees from models discontinued before you were born. Warranty: \"until you turn the corner\".","2459":"Sublevel pastry stand","2460":"\"Meat\" pastries fried in repulsor oil. The smell is better than it should be.","2461":"Tico's workshop bench","2462":"Open motherboards, half a robotic arm and a soldering iron that never cools. On the wall: \"I FIX ROBOTS, ANDROIDS AND BROKEN HEARTS\".","2463":"Workshop scrap","2464":"Cleaning robot shells. One of them has the same chassis model as RIG-7.","2465":"Flying car tires used as chairs, tables and, once, as a crib.","2466":"People huddle around for warmth and talk quietly. Up above, acid rain drips off the edges of the overpass.","2467":"Tin shack","2468":"A house made from a shipping container, with a railing porch and a satellite dish pointed at nothing.","2469":"Overflowing dumpster","2470":"Pastry wrappers, burnt chips and a flyer: \"SYNAPSE PAYS WELL FOR VOLUNTEERS. JUST ONE LITTLE CHIP.\"","2471":"Minhocão resident","2472":"Minhocão resident","2473":"Chip buyer","2474":"Zé do Tubo's Bar — Bixiga","2475":"Door → Street (aerotrain station)","2476":"Zé's counter","2477":"Bixiga public terminal","2478":"Formica table","2479":"Real Formica, from 2030. Someone carved a heart into it with a knife: \"J + M\".","2480":"A forgotten holographic truco board. The scoreboard says someone lost their house.","2481":"A bar glass with half a coffee, still warm. Someone left in a hurry.","2482":"Tube TV","2483":"A real tube TV, showing a Corinthians game from 2027. Zé swears it's not a rerun.","2484":"Basement trapdoor","2485":"Snake plant","2486":"A real snake plant, in a pot made from an oil can. Wards off the evil eye and network viruses.","2487":"Zé's regular","2488":"Two-bit hacker","2489":"Disconnected hideout","2490":"Stairs → Zé's Bar","2491":"Disconnected workstation","2492":"Twelve screens, all showing the same thing: the city seen from below. Spray-painted on the desk: \"DISCONNECT TO SEE\".","2493":"Stolen servers","2494":"Synapse Corp asset tags, half scraped off.","2495":"A mattress on the floor and a thermal foil blanket. Revolution doesn't pay rent.","2496":"Crate of masks","2497":"LED masks just like Zero's, still in the box. \"We are all nobody,\" says the leaflet inside.","2498":"Energy drink cans and fried circuit boards. Lots of them.","2499":"Clube 14 Bis — The Drone Province","2500":"Stairs → Street (aerotrain station)","2501":"DJ booth","2502":"The DJ is a drone with four arms and headphones. It plays industrial forró at 180 beats per minute.","2503":"Speaker","2504":"The bass is so strong the raindrops on Vance's coat tremble.","2505":"14 Bis bar","2506":"Drinks that glow in the dark. The cheapest costs a month's rent in the Minhocão.","2507":"VIP box","2508":"VIP box table","2509":"An ice bucket with a bottle of synthetic champagne and three data chips wrapped in a napkin.","2510":"14 Bis regular","2511":"14 Bis regular","2512":"14 Bis dancer","2513":"Disguised executive","2514":"Santa Rita Underground Clinic — Lado Sombra","2515":"Door → Alley (aerotrain station)","2516":"Cryogenic tank","2517":"A patient floats in blue gel, eyes closed. The plate reads: \"NEURAL REHABILITATION — CYCLE 14 OF 40\".","2518":"Empty. The gel still bubbles, as if waiting for someone.","2519":"A patient floats in blue gel. On the nape of the neck, the same chip model as the Minhocão test subjects.","2520":"Gurney","2521":"Clean sheets and a nameless patient wristband: \"DONOR 0447 — MINHOCÃO\".","2522":"Clean sheets and a nameless patient wristband: \"DONOR 0451 — MINHOCÃO\".","2523":"Neural compilation station","2524":"Clinic medical records","2525":"Biotech waste bin","2526":"Processing Core — Synapse Corp","2527":"Service elevator → Aerotrain station","2528":"Central server","2529":"Petabytes of Synapse clients' digital consciousness. All waiting for immortality, all in line.","2530":"Central packet router","2531":"Restricted executive file","2532":"Parts box","2533":"Spare parts for servers. Nobody has replaced anything here since 2079.","2534":"Synapse does not comment on ongoing matters. Or closed ones.","2535":"I worked with Kaelen. He ate lunch alone. Now I understand why.","2536":"They say Dr. Lin hasn't slept in three days. They say she never has.","2537":"Director Lyra got promoted twice this year. Nobody climbs twice without stepping on someone.","2538":"The air here costs more than my salary. I breathe slowly.","2539":"Cops down here? Only when a body falls from up there.","2540":"Synapse pays a thousand credits per volunteer. My cousin went. Came back not remembering his mother's name.","2541":"Chip, detective? I've got one that makes you forget your debts. And your name.","2542":"Up there it rains acid. Down here it rains the acid that drips from up there.","2543":"Tico fixes anything. He even fixed my marriage. It lasted a week.","2544":"Zé's coffee is brewed through a real cloth filter. The cloth is from 2040, but it's real.","2545":"The molecular mortadella sandwich is the only thing in this city that tastes like the past.","2546":"Saw an LED-masked guy using the terminal yesterday. Or it was an ad. Hard to tell these days.","2547":"A detective in Bixiga? Somebody's going to be on holo-TV tonight.","2548":"Zé keeps secrets better than a safe. And charges less.","2549":"Money laundering? Here? How absurd. Do you take crypto?","2550":"The Broker's in the VIP box. He's always in the VIP box.","2551":"If you don't have a hearing implant, you'll leave here with ringing ears until 2090.","2552":"The DJ's drones dance better than everyone here. Me included.","2553":"Lyra Vance","2554":"Chief executive of Synapse Corp","2555":"High-end symmetrical ocular implants. The optical fibers in her suit are red: high stress. Heart rate spikes every time someone says \"records\".","2556":"Detective... Vance? What an ironic coincidence. Lyra Vance. No relation, I hope. Kaelen was my brother. Ask what you need, then get out of my tower.","2557":"Be brief, detective. The board is waiting for me.","2558":"Again? My time is billed by the second.","2559":"Still here, namesake?","2560":"Tell me about your brother.","2561":"Kaelen was the best neural security engineer in this tower. And the most naive.","2562":"He thought security meant protecting people. At Synapse, security means protecting patents.","2563":"Her suit went from red to gray when she said \"naive\". Optical fibers don't lie as well as she does.","2564":"Vance. Same last name as mine.","2565":"Half of Neo-Sampa is named Vance, Silva or Synapse. Don't think you're special.","2566":"I don't. I just don't like coincidences.","2567":"Then you'll hate this city.","2568":"Was Kaelen going to blow the whistle on something?","2569":"*A pause that's far too long.* Kaelen had theories. About chip trials on volunteers in Baixo Minhocão.","2570":"Paid volunteers, detective. Signed contracts. All legal.","2571":"Then why the pause?","2572":"Because \"legal\" and \"right\" live on different floors of this tower.","2573":"Baixo Minhocão. The volunteers. Worth heading down there.","2574":"Your access records were deleted.","2575":"A system glitch. IT is already looking into it.","2576":"Deleted at 22:31. The exact time of your brother's death.","2577":"Then IT will look into it faster.","2578":"She didn't blink. High-end ocular implants: you can switch blinking off. You can switch a lot of things off.","2579":"⚠ Confront: you hired the Disconnected","2580":"*The suit's fibers turn black.* This is absurd.","2581":"L.V. Holdings. Payment to the Broker, Dante Rossi. Executors: the Disconnected. Goal: extract the data from your brother's chip.","2582":"I wanted the data, detective. The files he was going to leak. I was going to buy his silence with his own silence.","2583":"An extraction virus doesn't kill anyone. I checked. I paid people to check.","2584":"She wanted to rob her brother, not kill him. But someone turned the theft into an execution.","2585":"Don't show me that. *The suit turns gray.* I've seen it. I was the first to see it.","2586":"The Disconnected. Basement terrorists. The police should be hunting them, not interrogating me.","2587":"A cleaning robot? This tower's security is a joke that costs billions.","2588":"I don't know any Dante. I don't go to places where people know Dantes.","2589":"A lie. Her suit flashed yellow for half a second.","2590":"Dr. Lin works too hard. Someday it was going to end badly. For someone.","2591":"*The suit goes completely dark.* That's... a standard contingency protocol. Every executive has one.","2592":"A protocol to \"silence suppliers\". Signed by you.","2593":"That's none of my concern.","2594":"Talk to legal.","2595":"Interesting. Irrelevant, but interesting.","2596":"Dr. Maya Lin","2597":"Synapse's chief neurosurgeon","2598":"Augmented reality glasses wired straight into the optic nerve. Device ID: MLIN-AR. Vital signs of someone who hasn't slept in 72 hours. Dilated pupils: stimulants.","2599":"Dr. Maya Lin. I was Kaelen's mentor for ten years. If you came to ask whether I'm okay, the answer is no. If you came to ask something else, be quick.","2600":"I have surgeries, detective. Many.","2601":"More questions? Ask the right ones.","2602":"What was Kaelen like?","2603":"Brilliant. Stubborn. He thought he could fix the world with code.","2604":"I thought so too, at 34. Then you learn the world has no source code.","2605":"What is the digital immortality project?","2606":"Lazarus. Transferring human consciousness to the tower's servers before organic death. Eternal life, by monthly subscription.","2607":"It's my life's work, detective. Thirty years.","2608":"And Kaelen?","2609":"*Her glasses flicker.* Kaelen thought Lazarus was... unethical. He had strong opinions.","2610":"Where were you at 22:30?","2611":"I left the restricted floor at 22:20. I went to rest. Three days without sleep, detective. Even I have limits.","2612":"Ten minutes before the death.","2613":"Ten minutes before a tragedy. Do you want me to apologize for being sleepy?","2614":"Her glasses record everything she sees. But she didn't offer to show me.","2615":"Rest where?","2616":"At the Santa Rita Clinic, in Lado Sombra. I volunteer shifts there. Neural rehabilitation for those who can't pay.","2617":"I sleep on a gurney between one patient and the next. It's the only place in this city where I can sleep.","2618":"A chief neurosurgeon sleeping in an underground clinic. Worth a visit.","2619":"⚠ Confront: you intercepted the virus","2620":"Lyra was going to kill all of them. Zero, the Broker, the hackers. She was going to erase the whole trail after the theft. It was in her protocol.","2621":"And Kaelen was going to destroy Lazarus. Thirty years, detective. Thirty years.","2622":"So you killed two birds with one virus.","2623":"I saved the only thing that mattered. *Her glasses go dark.* Make your accusation, detective. I won't run.","2624":"Total brain death. The consciousness was... ripped out. Not deleted. Ripped out. Like pulling up a root.","2625":"She spoke like a doctor. But her voice shook on the word \"root\".","2626":"A physical connector? *She takes a while to answer.* That's... very specific, detective.","2627":"Amateur code. Comments in Tupi. That wouldn't kill even a lab rat.","2628":"How does she know what would kill a rat?","2629":"*Her glasses flicker three times.* Where did you get that?","2630":"Lyra deletes records the way other people turn off lights. It's a habit of hers.","2631":"RIG-7 has cleaned my lab for four years. I didn't even know it had firmware.","2632":"I don't have time for this.","2633":"Is this neurosurgery or gossip, detective?","2634":"I don't know. I didn't see. I didn't sleep.","2635":"Autonomous maintenance unit","2636":"Unofficial firmware. Hand soldering on the back panel, typical of Baixo Minhocão workshops. Cargo log: \"PACKAGE 0.2 KG — DELIVERED TO CHAIR 01 INTERFACE — 22:14\". RIG-7 doesn't carry packages. It cleans.","2637":"List tonight's tasks.","2638":"The 22:14 task was deleted. But the scanner can read what's left.","2639":"Who modified you?","2640":"Synapse holographic assistant","2641":"Holographic assistance projection. Corporate AI core, version 9.1. Broad read permissions, speech permissions carefully limited by legal.","2642":"Welcome to Synapse Corp, Detective Vance. I am ÁGORA. The board has authorized your investigation within contractual limits. I am here to help within those same limits.","2643":"ÁGORA at your service, detective.","2644":"How may I assist, within contractual limits?","2645":"Processing. Ask.","2646":"Any suggestions?","2647":"What happened in the lab?","2648":"At 22:31, the sensors recorded the brain death of engineer Kaelen Voss in interface chair 01.","2649":"The lab is shielded against external signals. No data packet entered or left between 22:00 and 23:00.","2650":"From the network's point of view, detective, nobody killed him.","2651":"How do I get to the other districts?","2652":"The express elevator goes to the aerotrain station. From there, the line reaches every district of Neo-Sampa, including your Sector 4.","2653":"The aerotrain only stops at districts on your investigation route. Conversations open routes.","2654":"I confirm the deletion. Executed with board credentials. I am not permitted to say which director.","2655":"She can't say. But she didn't deny it either.","2656":"The quantum lock is military grade. Opening it from outside would require a court order and three months.","2657":"The file appeared on the monitor at 22:31. It didn't come from the network. It was already in here.","2658":"No correlation in my database, detective.","2659":"That is outside my contractual limits.","2660":"Logged. Inconclusive.","2661":"Tico","2662":"Baixo Minhocão mechanic","2663":"A mechanical welding arm he welded on himself. The goggles are for welding, not AR. In his pocket, credits too new for the Minhocão.","2664":"Hey, detective! Tico Repairs, at your service. Robots, androids, drones, broken hearts. If it's got a screw, I fix it. If it doesn't, I put one in.","2665":"What's up, chief!","2666":"Something broke? I'll fix it.","2667":"I'm swamped, but for the cops I stop. One minute.","2668":"How's business?","2669":"Down here business is always good. Everything breaks, nobody has money to buy new. I'm the king of second chances.","2670":"Did you tinker with a Synapse cleaning robot?","2671":"*He stops soldering.* Cleaning robot? I tinker with a lot of robots, chief.","2672":"RIG-7. Hand soldering on the back panel. Just like the one on your arm.","2673":"...Okay, okay. It came in a week ago. A guy paid me to rewrite the firmware. Just one new routine: \"carry small package to chair 01\".","2674":"I figured it was chip smuggling. Down here, everything is chip smuggling.","2675":"Who paid?","2676":"A guy with a holographic hat and a chrome tooth. Everybody calls him the Broker. He clocks in at Clube 14 Bis.","2677":"And the routine's code came ready-made, chief. On a memory stick. I just installed it.","2678":"What do you know about the chip trials?","2679":"Synapse sends a recruiter down here every week. A thousand credits per volunteer. People go.","2680":"Some come back fine. Some come back forgetting things. Some don't come back. Those go to a clinic in Lado Sombra, they say.","2681":"Kessler memory stick connector. Old stuff, but reliable. That's what I installed on the robot's cargo arm.","2682":"I told you the Broker knows everything. He knows everything and sells everything.","2683":"That I can't fix, chief.","2684":"Got a screw? No? Then it's not my thing.","2685":"Zé do Tubo","2686":"Bar owner in Bixiga","2687":"No implants. None. A 70-year-old man without a single chip, in 2085. The calm heartbeat of someone who's seen it all.","2688":"Evening, son. Have a seat. Cloth-brewed coffee or a molecular mortadella sandwich? Cops pay like everybody else, you hear?","2689":"Another coffee?","2690":"I'm here, son. Been here since 2031.","2691":"How long have you had this bar?","2692":"Fifty-four years. My father opened it, I kept it going. The building fell down twice, the bar didn't.","2693":"No chips here, no holograms, no monthly subscription. Just coffee and conversation.","2694":"Who uses that public terminal?","2695":"Everybody and nobody. It's a public terminal, son. No login, no camera. That's why so many people come.","2696":"Yesterday a young guy in an LED mask came in. Used it for a couple of hours. Ordered three coffees and paid with paper money. Paper money! Hadn't seen that in years.","2697":"Where do I find the LED-masked guy?","2698":"*He slowly dries a glass.* You're going to promise me you won't go in shooting, son.","2699":"The bar's basement. Zero and his kids have lived down there for years. They don't hurt anybody, just Synapse.","2700":"You can go down through the trapdoor. Tell them Zé said it's okay.","2701":"A coffee, Zé.","2702":"*He brews the coffee through the cloth, slowly, as if it were 2030.* Here you go, son. On the house.","2703":"It tastes like a city that doesn't exist anymore.","2704":"That text came up on the terminal screen yesterday, son. The masked guy stared at it for a long time.","2705":"That's the kids' stuff. They comment their code in Tupi. They say it's to remember where we came from.","2706":"I don't understand that, son. All I understand is coffee.","2707":"Couldn't tell you.","2708":"Ask the tech folks.","2709":"Dante \"The Broker\" Rossi","2710":"Underworld informant","2711":"Chrome teeth with built-in micro-cameras. The hat projects digital rain and also an eavesdropping jammer. Three data chips in the inside pocket, bearing Kaelen Voss's signature.","2712":"*The chrome teeth gleam.* Detective Gabriel Vance. The man who can't be bought. A rarity, like a good 2040 vintage. Sit down. But here, information has a price.","2713":"Back to do business?","2714":"Detective. My smile is expensive. My answers, even more so.","2715":"Sit down. The drones can't hear a thing here.","2716":"What do you know about Kaelen Voss?","2717":"I know a lot. But I don't talk for free, detective. Bring me something worth my voice.","2718":"He wants ammunition. Something that compromises him, so he knows he's already in the crosshairs.","2719":"Tico said you paid for RIG-7's firmware.","2720":"*The chrome smile disappears.* Tico talks too much for a man who likes having fingers.","2721":"Fine. You brought the price. I'm a middleman, detective. I connect who pays with who does.","2722":"Who paid: an account called L.V. Holdings. Lots of money, very clean, from very high up.","2723":"Who did it: the Disconnected. Zero wrote an extraction virus. Extraction only: copy the data from Kaelen's chip and get out.","2724":"The robot would carry the stick to the chair, Kaelen would plug it in thinking it was a routine test. Simple.","2725":"And the chips you sold here, the night before?","2726":"Ah. A sample. To prove to the client that Kaelen had something worth stealing. Business.","2727":"Who is L.V. Holdings?","2728":"I never ask who's behind an account. It ruins the friendship.","2729":"But if I were a detective, I'd look at the initials. And at who would get a promotion out of a rival division's secrets.","2730":"You seem nervous, Dante.","2731":"Nervous? Me? *He adjusts his hat.* An engineer died from a virus that was only supposed to copy files, detective.","2732":"Someone changed the code along the way. And whoever changes code along the way also changes the fate of whoever knows too much.","2733":"He's not afraid of the police. He's afraid of whoever gave the order.","2734":"A shame. Kaelen was a great client. Never bought anything, but great to sell.","2735":"The manifesto? Theater. The Disconnected sign everything that falls. They love credit for things they didn't do.","2736":"*He turns pale under the chrome.* \"Silence suppliers.\" I'm a supplier, detective.","2737":"Thank you. I'm leaving the city tonight.","2738":"That's worth nothing in my market.","2739":"Pretty. Cheap.","2740":"Bring something better, detective.","2741":"\"Zero\" — Marcus Thorne","2742":"Leader of the Disconnected","2743":"The LED mask broadcasts random pixels, and also blocks facial recognition. Heavy industrial arms, dock model. No biological trace of Kaelen Voss.","2744":"*The LED mask shows a question mark.* A cop in Zé's basement. The old man's gone soft. What do you want, Vance? If you came to arrest someone, arrest the system.","2745":"*The mask shows a period.* Talk.","2746":"Still here, cop?","2747":"*The mask shows static.* Ask already.","2748":"Who are the Disconnected?","2749":"People who pulled the chip out of their heads to remember who they were. Synapse sells immortality. We sell mortality. It's more honest.","2750":"You claimed Kaelen Voss's death.","2751":"We claim everything that takes Synapse down. It's propaganda, cop. Someday you people will learn.","2752":"And what if the murder wasn't yours?","2753":"*The mask shows a smile.* Then someone did the work and we got the fame. Cheap.","2754":"⚠ Show: the claim was posted after the death","2755":"*The mask freezes.*","2756":"You posted the manifesto 34 minutes later. You didn't know he was going to die. You found out from the news, like everyone else.","2757":"Fine. Fine. We were hired. By the Broker. An extraction virus: copy Kaelen's chip and vanish. That's all.","2758":"I wrote the code. I know what I write, cop. There was no overload. Nothing that would hurt a fly.","2759":"Here. The original code. Read the comments, they're in Tupi. That's how we sign.","2760":"Someone grabbed my virus along the way and turned it into a bullet. And now the bullet has my name on it.","2761":"How did the virus get to Tico's workshop?","2762":"I sent it through Synapse's internal network. A maintenance channel we've used for years, routed through the Processing Core.","2763":"If someone intercepted it, it was there. But the Core is in the heart of the tower. Nobody gets in without a board badge.","2764":"The Processing Core. That's where the package changed hands.","2765":"*The mask shows a skull.* That's not mine. That's a doctor's code. Look at the precision. This thing knows exactly where every neuron is.","2766":"Kaelen was one of the few up there who looked down. Ironic, huh?","2767":"The Broker opened his mouth. Of course he did. He'd sell his own mother if the price was right.","2768":"*Static on the mask.* Not interested.","2769":"That's the system's problem, not mine.","2770":"*The mask shows an X.*","2771":"Sister-7","2772":"Santa Rita android nurse","2773":"Religious-model care android, refurbished. Short-term memory intact. Dr. Lin's attendance record at the clinic: 22:41.","2774":"Peace and goodwill, detective. I am Sister-7. Here at Santa Rita we care for those the city threw away. Speak softly: the patients are dreaming.","2775":"Peace and goodwill.","2776":"Speak softly, please.","2777":"Who are the patients?","2778":"Volunteers from the Minhocão. People who sold their heads to Synapse for a thousand credits and came back without their memories.","2779":"Doctor Lin brings them here. She says it's to fix what the company broke.","2780":"Was Dr. Lin here yesterday?","2781":"She arrived at 22:41. She didn't sleep. She spent the whole night at the compilation station.","2782":"She said she needed to finish some code before dawn.","2783":"22:41. She left the tower at 22:20... and Kaelen died at 22:31. But she \"finished\" the code afterward?","2784":"*The green eyes blink.* That file was in the biological waste bin. The doctor always empties it before leaving. Yesterday she forgot.","2785":"She told you she came here to sleep? The doctor hasn't slept here in months.","2786":"I cannot answer that, detective.","2787":"That is outside my care protocols.","2788":"Peace and goodwill. I do not recognize it.","2789":"Suggestion: examine the kinetic lab. The body, the main monitor and the quantum door panel.","2790":"No signal came in through the network. Perhaps something came in another way. The scanner on the interface chair may reveal it.","2791":"The quantum door panel logs every opening. Worth reading the log.","2792":"You have the door log and the trace on the neural port. Connect them in Clues.","2793":"RIG-7 was modified outside the tower. Scan the unit and look for the workshop in Baixo Minhocão.","2794":"The mechanic mentioned a broker at Clube 14 Bis. Bring him something that compromises him.","2795":"The manifesto was published from a public terminal in Bixiga, at Zé do Tubo's Bar.","2796":"Compare the manifesto's timestamp with the publication time in Clues.","2797":"The Disconnected are hiding near the terminal. The bar owner knows where.","2798":"Compare the Disconnected's original code with what happened to Kaelen.","2799":"The Processing Core is being wiped. Reach the central router before the wipe.","2800":"Dr. Lin spent the night at the Santa Rita Clinic. Scan what she left behind.","2801":"Cross-reference the router log with the lethal code from the clinic.","2802":"Who paid for the extraction? The Broker and Lyra's deleted records tell the same story.","2803":"Your dossier looks complete, detective. Make the accusation in Clues. Remember: there may be more than one culprit.","2804":"Kaelen Voss's body","2805":"Kaelen","2806":"Irreversible brain death at 22:31. The digital consciousness was erased entirely. The neural port on the nape burned from the inside out: an overload, not an extraction.","2807":"Disconnected manifesto","2808":"Manifesto","2809":"A corrupted file looping on the main monitor, signed by the Disconnected. It appeared at 22:31, the same second as the death, without coming from any network.","2810":"Quantum door log","2811":"Q. Door","2812":"Lab locked from the inside at 21:55. A single opening: 22:12, RIG-7 maintenance credentials. No external signal between 22:00 and 23:00.","2813":"Trace on the neural port","2814":"Neural port","2815":"Micro-scratches from a Kessler connector on the chair 01 interface. A physical memory stick was plugged straight into Kaelen's nape and then removed.","2816":"RIG-7 firmware","2817":"Unofficial firmware, with Baixo Minhocão hand soldering. Log: \"0.2 kg package delivered to chair 01 interface — 22:14\". A cleaning robot doesn't carry packages.","2818":"Dr. Lin's testimony","2819":"Dr. Lin","2820":"Maya Lin admits she left the restricted floor at 22:20, eleven minutes before the death, \"to rest\".","2821":"Lyra's deleted records","2822":"Lyra logs","2823":"Lyra Vance's internal network access records were deleted at 22:31, with board credentials. The exact time of death.","2824":"Tico's testimony","2825":"Workshop","2826":"The mechanic Tico reprogrammed RIG-7 a week ago, at the \"Broker's\" request. The new routine came ready-made on a stick: carry a small package to chair 01.","2827":"The Broker's confession","2828":"Broker","2829":"Dante Rossi brokered the theft: payment from the L.V. Holdings account, execution by the Disconnected. The virus was for extraction, not murder. He sold a sample of Kaelen's data the night before.","2830":"Terminal","2831":"The manifesto was published from this terminal at 23:05, thirty-four minutes AFTER the death. Whoever claimed it learned of the crime from the news.","2832":"The Disconnected's original code","2833":"Zero's code","2834":"The virus written by Zero: extraction and copying only, commented in Tupi. It has no overload module. As written, it wouldn't kill anyone.","2835":"Lethal overload module","2836":"Lethal code","2837":"Fragment found in the Santa Rita Clinic waste: Zero's virus with a neural overload module grafted on. Compiled with the MLIN key, at 21:57. A neurosurgeon's precision.","2838":"Lyra's confession","2839":"L.'s confession","2840":"Lyra admits she hired the extraction of her brother's data to bury his whistleblowing. She swears the virus couldn't kill anyone and that she paid to have that verified.","2841":"Synthetic guard in the Core","2842":"Guard","2843":"A Synapse synthetic guard opened fire as soon as Vance entered the Core, and fell back when the wipe began. Someone with a board badge ordered the servers protected.","2844":"Central router log","2845":"Router","2846":"Zero's package passed through the Core at 21:52, was diverted to the MLIN-AR device (Dr. Lin's glasses) and reinjected, modified, at 21:58, bound for Tico's workshop.","2847":"Lyra's disposal protocol","2848":"Protocol","2849":"Executive file signed by Lyra Vance: after the extraction, \"silence suppliers\": the Broker, the Disconnected and the mechanic. Maya Lin had read access to this folder.","2850":"The attack came from inside","2851":"No signal came in through the network: the weapon was a physical memory stick, plugged straight into Kaelen's neural port.","2852":"The metal messenger","2853":"RIG-7, the only thing that entered the lab at 22:12, carried the stick to the chair. The robot was the hand, not the mind.","2854":"Who paid for the theft","2855":"L.V. Holdings is Lyra Vance. She hired the extraction and erased her own tracks at the time of death.","2856":"The claim is fake","2857":"The manifesto was published 34 minutes after the death. The Disconnected claimed a crime they only heard about on the news.","2858":"The virus was altered","2859":"Zero's code only copied data. Kaelen died of an overload. Someone modified the virus between the Disconnected's basement and Kaelen's nape.","2860":"Dr. Lin's night","2861":"Maya didn't go to sleep: she spent the night at Santa Rita's compilation station, where the overload module with her key was found.","2862":"Maya's betrayal","2863":"Maya intercepted Zero's package in the Core with her MLIN-AR glasses, grafted on the overload and sent it back on its way. She turned the theft into an execution.","2864":"Lyra was going to erase everyone","2865":"After the theft, Lyra planned to silence the Broker and the Disconnected. Maya knew and used Lyra's plan as cover.","2866":"Breaking the Locked Room","2867":"The Hunt Through the Districts","2868":"The Processing Core","2869":"The Silenced Echo","2870":"Gabriel Vance publishes the entire dossier on Neo-Sampa's public network. Within minutes, the whole 300-floor city reads it: Dr. Maya Lin intercepted the Disconnected's virus and turned it into a death sentence, to save the Lazarus project.\n\nMaya is arrested in her own lab, without resisting. And Lyra Vance's frauds, the commissioned extraction, the protocol to silence suppliers, reach the Synapse Corp board before breakfast.\n\nIn Bixiga, Zé do Tubo serves a cloth-brewed coffee on the house. Up above, for the first time in weeks, the acid rain lets up.","2871":"Half Justice","2872":"Dr. Maya Lin is convicted of the murder of Kaelen Voss. The router log and the lethal code leave no room for doubt.\n\nBut the Synapse board shuts the door on the rest. {extra}\n\nVance looks up at the tower from down in the Minhocão. It stays lit. Always lit.","2873":"You pointed at the right person. But without linking the lethal code to the interception in the Core, Synapse's lawyers turn the case against Dr. Maya Lin into a \"creative theory\".\n\nShe's back in the lab the next morning. The Lazarus project gets a new security engineer.\n\nKnowing isn't enough. You have to prove it.","2874":"The Digital Scapegoat","2875":"The digital trail points to the Disconnected, and the Synapse board appreciates the speed. Zero is arrested in Zé do Tubo's basement, mask and all.\n\nThe case closes in record time. The corporate press calls you a hero.\n\nOn the 220th floor, Dr. Maya Lin adjusts her AR glasses and gets back to work. The Lazarus project has never been safer.","2876":"The Wrong Executive","2877":"You accuse Lyra Vance of murdering her own brother. She ordered the theft, yes. But the virus she bought couldn't kill anyone.\n\nHer lawyers take the murder charge apart in an afternoon. Lyra is demoted for \"supplier mismanagement\" and walks out the front door.\n\nThe killer watches the trial from inside her lab, without taking off her glasses.","2878":"Factory Defect","2879":"You accuse RIG-7. Synapse loves the idea: \"equipment failure\", no human culprit, no compensation.\n\nThe robot is dismantled in public and sold as scrap in the Minhocão. Tico buys the parts.\n\nWhoever programmed the death still has clean hands. RIG-7 only carried the package.","2880":"The Price of Information","2881":"You accuse Dante Rossi. The Broker brokered the theft, but never touched the code.\n\nHe pays bail with a data chip and walks out smiling, his chrome teeth reflecting the camera flashes. A week later, he vanishes from Neo-Sampa.\n\nThe real killer never needed a broker.","2882":"Total Wipe","2883":"The clock hits zero. In the heart of the Neo-Sampa Tower, the Processing Core servers run the total emergency wipe.\n\nEvery log, every packet, every digital trace of the night of 22:31 turns into white noise. At 06:00, the city's automated system files the Kaelen Voss case: \"INCONCLUSIVE — EQUIPMENT FAILURE\".\n\nVance stands in the acid rain, staring at his own terminal. A line blinks, and disappears.","2884":"Who killed Kaelen Voss?","2885":"Should anyone else be charged in the conspiracy?","2886":"Sector 4 (Corporate Ave.)","2887":"Neo-Sampa Tower — Paulista Sector","2888":"Bixiga — Zé do Tubo's Bar","2889":"Lado Sombra — Santa Rita Clinic","2890":"Neo-Sampa Tower — Processing Core","2891":"Synthetic guard","2892":"A Synapse synthetic guard steps out from behind the servers!","2893":"A grazing shot slams Vance against a rack. Sparks, alarms, smoke. When he gets up, the guard has already fallen back behind the servers.","2894":"The synthetic guard retreats among the servers and vanishes into the coolant smoke. Vance's shots only hit panels.","2895":"On the guard's back, Vance saw the command badge: \"BOARD AUTHORIZATION\".\n\nOver the speakers, a synthetic voice: \"EMERGENCY WIPE IN PROGRESS.\" The clock is ticking.","2896":"New stop: {0}","2897":"Aerotrain station","2898":"The car glides in on the magnetic rail, dripping acid rain. The panel shows the stops on your route:","2899":"Stay here","2900":"Neo-Sampa, 2085. A day after the Alvorada case, the phone rings again. Neo-Sampa Tower, 220th floor: Kaelen Voss, a neural security engineer at Synapse Corp, is dead in his own interface chair. The brain, intact. The consciousness, erased.","2901":"The lab is shielded and was locked with quantum encryption. No signal came in or out. A locked room, physical and digital.","2902":"The aerotrain links the tower to Neo-Sampa's districts and to your Sector 4. The SCANNER reveals the invisible; CLUES connects the evidence.","2903":"The weapon didn't come through the network. It came on a memory stick, plugged straight into Kaelen's nape. Someone had to carry that stick to the chair.\n\nAnd the manifesto on the monitor leaves a trail: it was published from a public terminal in Bixiga. The aerotrain already has the stop.","2904":"Zero's virus only copied data. Whoever killed Kaelen swapped the package's contents along the way, and the way runs through the tower's Processing Core.\n\nÁGORA warns: Synapse has scheduled an emergency wipe of the servers. When Vance enters the Core, the clock starts ticking.\n\nFind the final evidence. When you're ready, make the accusation in Clues.","2905":"How did the weapon get into a shielded lab? Use the scanner on the interface chair.","2906":"Examine the kinetic lab in the Neo-Sampa Tower.","2907":"Find out who modified RIG-7 (Baixo Minhocão).","2908":"Interrogate the Broker at Clube 14 Bis.","2909":"Trace the manifesto to the terminal at Zé do Tubo's Bar.","2910":"Connect the manifesto to the Bixiga terminal in Clues.","2911":"Find Zero, the leader of the Disconnected.","2912":"Compare Zero's code with Kaelen's death in Clues.","2913":"WIPE IN {0}: reach the Core's central router!","2914":"Take the aerotrain to the Processing Core.","2915":"Link the router log to the code that killed Kaelen.","2916":"You accused Lyra Vance, but without linking L.V. Holdings to the deleted records, the conspiracy charge doesn't hold up. She's promoted the following month.","2917":"Worse: you dragged {0} into court as an accomplice to murder, while the executive who ordered the theft was never even named.","2918":"Nobody asks who ordered the theft of Kaelen's data. Lyra Vance stays on the 220th floor, with the disposal protocol tucked away in a drawer.","2919":"The door is sealed with forensics tape: \"CRIME SCENE — PENDELTON CASE\". The patrol cars are still out front, lights flashing.\n\nThe Alvorada case is still in court. Today, Vance's work is in Neo-Sampa.","2920":"Neural port — scanner","2921":"The scanner magnifies the interface on Kaelen's nape: fresh micro-scratches from a Kessler connector, from a physical memory stick.\n\nSomeone plugged a device straight into his head, and then took it out.\n\nThe room wasn't locked to things that walk.","2922":"Kaelen Voss, 34, sitting in the interface chair, eyes open. The organic brain is intact, but shows no activity at all: irreversible brain death at 22:31.\n\nThe neural port on his nape burned from the inside out. This wasn't a data theft. It was an overload.\n\n(The SCANNER may reveal more on the interface.)","2923":"Kessler connector scratches on the interface. A physical stick.","2924":"Kaelen's eyes are still open, fixed on the monitor. As if he were still reading something.","2925":"A single corrupted file plays on a loop:\n\n\"WE ARE THE DISCONNECTED. SYNAPSE SELLS ETERNITY. WE COLLECT THE PRICE.\"\n\nTimestamp: 22:31:00. The file has no network origin. It was written in here.","2926":"The Disconnected manifesto is still looping. 22:31:00.","2927":"Lock log:\n\n21:55 — LOCK /QUANTUM — origin: INTERNAL (K. VOSS)\n22:12 — OPEN 00:40 — credential: MAINT/RIG-7\n22:12 — LOCK /QUANTUM\n22:00–23:00 — EXTERNAL SIGNALS: 0\n\nNothing came in through the network. Only one thing came in through the door: the cleaning robot.","2928":"One opening at 22:12, RIG-7 credentials. No external signal.","2929":"Board access records. Executive-level corporate encryption.","2930":"Board records","2931":"L. VANCE — sessions from 21:00 to 23:59: [DELETED]\n\nDelete command: 22:31:04 — credential: BOARD/LV.\n\nFour seconds after her brother's death, Lyra erased her own footsteps.","2932":"Lyra Vance's records deleted at 22:31:04.","2933":"An old terminal, no login and no camera. The keyboard is held together with tape. The upload history is protected by a password from 2050.","2934":"Hack the history","2935":"Upload history","2936":"23:05 — POSTED TO THE SHADOW NETWORKS — \"manifesto_desconectados.txt\"\n\nEleven-oh-five. The death was at 22:31.\n\nWhoever posted this manifesto showed up late to their own crime.","2937":"Manifesto posted from here at 23:05, half an hour after the death.","2938":"A wooden trapdoor with a padlock. Underneath, a hum of servers and a green light.\n\nBetter ask Zé before going down.","2939":"Zé serves a cloth-brewed coffee and a molecular mortadella sandwich. It tastes like a Sunday in 2030.","2940":"The scanner finds the last session: MLIN key, from 22:41 to 05:58. Files deleted. But the trash... nobody deletes trash properly.","2941":"A neural code compilation station, far too expensive for an underground clinic. The chair is still warm.\n\n(The SCANNER may reveal more.)","2942":"Biotech waste — scanner","2943":"Among gloves and syringes, a burnt memory stick. The scanner recovers a fragment:\n\n\"modulo_sobrecarga.neu — compiled 21:57 — key: MLIN\"\n\nAnd, underneath, Zero's code, with its comments in Tupi. Someone took the Disconnected's virus and grafted a death sentence onto it.","2944":"The burnt stick with the overload module.","2945":"Gloves, syringes, dried blue gel. A smell of ozone and hospital.\n\n(The SCANNER may reveal more.)","2946":"Patients 0440 to 0459: \"Synapse volunteers — Baixo Minhocão\". Diagnosis for all: \"memory loss from experimental chip\".\n\nAttending: Dr. M. Lin. The same woman who invented the chip, caring for those it broke.","2947":"The panel flashes red: WIPE IN PROGRESS. The routing logs are being erased sector by sector.","2948":"Hack and save the log","2949":"Routing log saved","2950":"Package \"manut_rig7.pkg\", origin: maintenance channel (Disconnected).\n\n21:52 — DIVERTED to device MLIN-AR\n21:58 — REINJECTED (size +312 KB) bound for the workshop \"Tico Consertos\"\n\nDr. Lin's glasses. She grabbed the virus along the way and sent it back heavier.\n\nThe wipe can run now. The log is already in your implant.","2951":"The saved log shows the diversion to the MLIN-AR device.","2952":"Executive file — scanner","2953":"The scanner pierces the folder's concealment layer. A document signed by L. Vance:\n\n\"CONTINGENCY PROTOCOL — after the extraction, silence suppliers: the Broker, the Disconnected group, the Sublevel 4 workshop.\"\n\nFolder read list: L. Vance, M. Lin.","2954":"Executive file","2955":"Lyra's disposal protocol. Maya had access.","2956":"A board folder, hidden and locked. It looks empty.\n\n(The SCANNER may reveal more.)","2957":"Case solved","2958":"Case not started","2959":"{0}% complete","2960":"Restart","2961":"Restarting erases this case's saved progress. Continue?","2962":"Detective Gabriel Vance","2963":"Detective.","2964":"RIG-7","2965":"*BEEP.* UNIT RIG-7. AUTONOMOUS MAINTENANCE. AREA: KINETIC LAB. *BEEP.* PLEASE DO NOT STEP ON THE WET FLOOR.","2966":"*BEEP.* AWAITING TASK.","2967":"*BEEP-BEEP.* FLOOR CLEAN. FLOOR CLEAN.","2968":"UNIT RIG-7 ON STANDBY.","2969":"TASK 1: FLOOR CLEANING — 21:00. COMPLETED.","2970":"TASK 2: [CORRUPTED DATA] — 22:14. COMPLETED.","2971":"TASK 3: FLOOR CLEANING — 23:00. CANCELED. REASON: BODY IN THE WAY.","2972":"*BEEP.* ORIGINAL FIRMWARE: SYNAPSE CORP. CURRENT FIRMWARE: [UNKNOWN].","2973":"LAST EXTERNAL MAINTENANCE: \"TICO REPAIRS\" WORKSHOP, SUBLEVEL 4.","2974":"*BEEP.* PACKAGE DELIVERED AS INSTRUCTED. *BEEP.* INSTRUCTION ERASED AFTER DELIVERY.","2975":"USER KAELEN VOSS. STATUS: [ERROR]. STATUS: [ERROR]. *BEEP.*","2976":"*BEEP.* OBJECT NOT RECOGNIZED.","2977":"PLEASE DISPOSE OF IN THE CORRECT BIN.","2978":"*BEEP-BOOP.* NO CORRELATION.","2979":"ÁGORA","2980":"I promise.","2981":"CHIPS","2982":"CYBORG","2983":"PASTEL","2984":"WHAT? I CAN'T HEAR YOU, DETECTIVE!","2985":"CRITICAL ENDING","2986":"0% complete","2987":"Interface chair 01","2988":"The interface chair is empty, turned to one side. The neural cable hangs down to the floor, where it still blinks red.","2989":"No signal came in through the network. Maybe something came in another way. The scanner on Kaelen's neck may reveal it.","2990":"Neo-Sampa, 2085. One day after the Alvorada case, the phone rings again. Neo-Sampa Tower, 220th floor: Kaelen Voss, neural security engineer at Synapse Corp, lies dead on the lab floor, next to his own interface chair. The brain, intact. The consciousness, erased.","2991":"How did the weapon get into a shielded lab? Use the scanner on Kaelen's body.","2992":"Kaelen Voss, 34, lying on the floor next to the interface chair, eyes open. The neural cable still hangs from the chair. The organic brain is intact, but shows no activity at all: irreversible brain death at 22:31.\n\nThe neural port on his neck burned from the inside out. This wasn't data theft. It was an overload.\n\n(The SCANNER may reveal more at the interface.)","2993":"Kaelen's eyes are still open, fixed on the ceiling. He fell from the chair like someone unplugged from the wall.","2994":"Neo-Sampa, 2085. What was once São Paulo has become a patchwork of 300 floors: glass peaks up top, mud sublevels down below. And the acid rain never stops.","2995":"On the 220th floor of the Neo-Sampa Tower, Synapse Corp sells the one thing no one should be able to buy: eternity.","2996":"Kaelen Voss, neural security engineer, lies dead on the floor of a shielded lab. The consciousness, erased. No signal came in. No signal went out.","2997":"The executive","2998":"The neurosurgeon","2999":"Zero","3000":"The hacker","3001":"Dante Rossi","3002":"The broker","3003":"The robot","3004":"Five suspects. An executive, a doctor, a hacker, a broker... and a cleaning robot.","3005":"One day after the Alvorada case, the phone rings again. Detective Vance takes the aerotrain to the top of the city.","3006":"Miss Cida","3007":"No implants. Lungs worn out by tire smoke. An old patient wristband on her wrist: \"DONOR 0102 — SYNAPSE\".","3008":"Evening, son. Cida. I've lived down here fifteen years, ever since the expressway became a roof. Sit by the fire, the night is long.","3009":"Talk to me, son.","3010":"Warm your hands by the fire.","3011":"What is it now?","3012":"What's it like living under the viaduct?","3013":"Up there, flying cars pass all day. Down here, people pass. We help each other: whoever has beans shares, whoever has a tarp lends it.","3014":"The police come down now and then to tear down tents. We put them back up the next day.","3015":"That wristband on your wrist...","3016":"*She hides her wrist in her sleeve.* I volunteered. A thousand credits, ten years ago. First batch of chips.","3017":"I was lucky: I only forgot a few years. Some people forgot everything. Those go to the clinic over on the Shadow Side.","3018":"Synapse tests the chips down here and takes care of the leftovers on the other side of the city.","3019":"Do you know Tico?","3020":"Tico? Good kid. Fixes everyone's radio for free. Lately he's got fresh credits in his pocket.","3021":"Fresh credits down here, son, always come from up there.","3022":"I don't know anything about that, son.","3023":"We don't see those things down here.","3024":"Ask Tico, he knows machines.","3025":"Dr. Caio Mendes","3026":"Santa Rita's renegade doctor","3027":"Medical license revoked in 2079, per public record. Military-grade diagnostic glasses. Steady hands, eyes of someone who doesn't sleep.","3028":"Doctor Caio. Or just Caio, since the board revoked me. Nobody here asks about the license: they ask if the pain will stop. How can I help, detective?","3029":"Be quick, I have a patient in crisis.","3030":"More questions?","3031":"What is Santa Rita?","3032":"A neural rehab clinic for the people the city threw away. People who sold their heads for chip trials and came back empty.","3033":"We try to reconnect the memories. Sometimes the name comes back. Sometimes a child's face comes back. Sometimes nothing does.","3034":"Does Dr. Lin work here?","3035":"She funds half the clinic. Brings equipment none of us could ever buy.","3036":"She says it's to fix what Synapse broke. I think it's guilt. Both can be true.","3037":"Last night she spent the whole night at the compiling station. Didn't even take off her lab coat.","3038":"Why did they revoke your license?","3039":"I treated a Synapse donor without the company's authorization. His chip was intellectual property. His head too, apparently.","3040":"In Neo-Sampa, even memory has an owner.","3041":"*He goes pale.* This isn't rehab. This is the opposite. Whoever wrote this knows exactly which neuron to switch off.","3042":"She got here at 22:41, yes. And she didn't sleep. I walked past the compiling station three times: she never took her eyes off the screen.","3043":"That's police business, not a doctor's.","3044":"Ask Sister-7. She logs everything.","3045":"Old Galdino","3046":"Retired worker","3047":"Lungs at 40% capacity. Old hearing implant, tuned to hear the factory siren. The calm heartbeat of someone in no hurry anymore.","3048":"Evening, son. Galdino, forty years at Vulcan Foundry. These days I just sit here at the station watching the aerotrain come in. It's the only thing that still arrives on time.","3049":"The aerotrain's coming.","3050":"Sit down, it's a long story.","3051":"What's Sector 7 like?","3052":"This is where the city gets made, son. The Upper Zone's steel comes out of that furnace there. The drones' fuel comes out of the refinery.","3053":"Up there they breathe filtered air. Down here we breathe what's left.","3054":"The Foundry, Warehouse 13, Neide's bar and the Union. The rest is sheds and smokestacks.","3055":"What's this story about the fire of 2071?","3056":"Ah, so you've heard. Furnace two blew one night before dawn. Twelve comrades.","3057":"The company said it was human error. The union proved it was the sensor they never replaced to save money.","3058":"Nobody went to jail. They just renamed the furnace. Now furnace three sits where two used to be.","3059":"In Neo-Sampa, blame has floors too. And it's never the top one.","3060":"Any advice for someone walking around here?","3061":"Don't stand under the crane, don't drink the cachaça from the unlabeled bottle, and don't call Rosa from the union \"ma'am\".","3062":"We didn't have that in my day.","3063":"Ask Rosa, she knows everything.","3064":"Master Otto","3065":"Furnace master at Vulcan Foundry","3066":"Mechanical foundry arm, rated to 1,600 degrees. Safety goggles with a spectrometer: he reads the steel's temperature by its color. Old burns on his neck.","3067":"*He never takes his eyes off the furnace.* Otto. Master of furnace three. If you're here to inspect, the paperwork's in the office. If you're here to talk, speak up.","3068":"*He shouts over the noise.* TALK!","3069":"Steel doesn't wait, detective.","3070":"How do you know the temperature just by looking?","3071":"Dark orange, nine hundred degrees. Yellow, twelve hundred. White, fifteen hundred. Blue, you're dead.","3072":"Sensors lie when the company wants to save money. The color of steel never lies.","3073":"Didn't the robots replace you?","3074":"They tried. Robots melt near furnace three. People melt slower.","3075":"That's why there are still workers here. Not out of the board's kindness: out of physics.","3076":"How long is a shift?","3077":"On paper, eight hours. In real life, until the furnace lets you go.","3078":"He said it without bitterness. Like someone describing the weather outside.","3079":"I don't know about that. I know steel.","3080":"Show that to the office.","3081":"*He shrugs and goes back to the furnace.*","3082":"Old Bento","3083":"Warehouse 13 watchman","3084":"Watchman's uniform from a company that went bankrupt in 2079. He keeps guard anyway. First-generation night-vision implant.","3085":"Halt! Oh, it's the police. Bento, Warehouse 13 watchman. Nobody's paid me in six years, but somebody's got to keep watch, right?","3086":"All in order here, detective.","3087":"Nobody gets in without me seeing.","3088":"Want some coffee? It's from yesterday, but it's coffee.","3089":"What's in this warehouse?","3090":"Officially? Robot parts and implants for the Upper Zone. In practice? A lot more crates than the inventory says.","3091":"Before dawn, trucks with no plates show up. I write it all down in my notebook. Nobody ever asked to see it.","3092":"Why keep watch without pay?","3093":"The company went under, but nobody came to pick up the stuff. If I leave, they'll loot it all in one night.","3094":"And also... I live here, detective. Where else is an old watchman going to live?","3095":"That didn't come through my gate.","3096":"I'll write it in the notebook.","3097":"Don't recognize it, no.","3098":"Miss Neide","3099":"Owner of the Siren Bar","3100":"No network implants: just a pacemaker from 2060. Hands that have been frying coxinhas for thirty years. She knows everyone's name in the district.","3101":"Come in, child, it's raining acid out there. Neide. Here we've got cachaça, protein coxinhas and conversation. What'll it be?","3102":"Another one, child?","3103":"Sit down, the coxinha's coming right up.","3104":"Why \"Siren Bar\"?","3105":"Because the Vulcan siren goes off at six, two and ten. And at every shift change the bar fills up.","3106":"My husband opened it. The siren took him in the fire of '71. The name stayed.","3107":"Who drinks at the bar?","3108":"Furnacemen, welders, dockworkers, watchmen. People who make the city and whom the city forgets.","3109":"And now and then some suit from the Upper Zone who got lost. Those I charge double.","3110":"A cachaça, Miss Neide.","3111":"*She fills a small bar glass to the brim.* The good stuff. The unlabeled bottle is for people who want to go blind.","3112":"Burns going down. Like everything in Sector 7.","3113":"Never seen that, child.","3114":"We don't get mixed up in that here.","3115":"Ask Galdino at the station.","3116":"Rosa Ferraz","3117":"President of the Metalworkers' Union","3118":"Vocal amplifier implant, for speeches without a microphone. Burn scar on her forearm: former furnace worker. The racing heartbeat of someone who lives in assemblies.","3119":"Rosa Ferraz, union president. And it's \"comrade\", not \"ma'am\". If the police came to break up the strike, you're early: the strike hasn't even started.","3120":"Talk, comrade.","3121":"Make it quick, there's an assembly at ten.","3122":"What do the police want now?","3123":"Why the strike?","3124":"Vulcan wants to replace the night shift with new robots. The ones that can handle furnace three.","3125":"Twelve hundred families, comrade. And the money for the robots comes from the same place as always: the Upper Zone.","3126":"And what's the union going to do?","3127":"Shut everything down. Without steel, the Upper Zone can't build a single floor more.","3128":"The fire of 2071.","3129":"*She turns serious.* I was eighteen. I was at furnace one when two exploded.","3130":"The pressure sensor had been expired for three years. The company knew. It's all in that archive over there.","3131":"That's why I joined the union. So no Neide in this district is ever widowed again because of a spreadsheet.","3132":"You don't trust the police.","3133":"I trust whoever shows up when the factory catches fire. The police show up when the factory stops.","3134":"Hard to argue with that.","3135":"That's not union business.","3136":"Bring evidence, comrade, not paper.","3137":"Press officer","3138":"Synapse lawyer","3139":"Synthetic guard","3140":"Cleaning robot","3141":"Harsh white forensic light. Makes everything look like a morgue.","3142":"Tweezers, evidence bags and a DNA scanner. Synapse's forensics got here before the police.","3143":"Police forensic tech","3144":"Synapse forensic tech","3145":"Viaduct pillar","3146":"Concrete from 2030, cracked and tagged. Up above, the Upper Zone expressway rushes by without ever looking down.","3147":"Abandoned car","3148":"A sedan with no repulsors, no wheels and no doors. There's a curtain on the back window: someone lives here.","3149":"A coupe that fell off the expressway in 2071. Nobody came for it. It became a garden: there are tomatoes sprouting on the hood.","3150":"Abandoned taxi","3151":"A flying taxi from 2060, faded yellow. The meter still shows a 40-credit fare nobody paid.","3152":"Burned car","3153":"Only the black shell is left. The residents use the trunk as a closet.","3154":"Tarp tent","3155":"Blue tarp, ropes tied to the pillar and a pair of boots at the door. Inside, someone is snoring.","3156":"A luxury camping tent from before the crisis. Now it's home to a family of four.","3157":"Hanging at the entrance, a wind chime made of burned-out chips.","3158":"A cardboard sign: \"MR. JOÃO LIVES HERE. CLAP TO KNOCK.\"","3159":"Mattress on the sidewalk","3160":"A mattress and a plaid blanket, sheltered from the rain by the viaduct. It's the best roof in the city.","3161":"Cardboard and blanket","3162":"Opened cardboard boxes and an aluminum thermal blanket that glints in the neon.","3163":"A mattress with a photo taped to the pillar: a family at the beach, back when there were beaches.","3164":"A pot of beans warms on top of the drum. Anyone passing by gets a ladleful.","3165":"An old tire fire. The black smoke rises and vanishes into the dark under the viaduct.","3166":"Two stories of stacked containers, with a rope ladder and potted plants in the window.","3167":"Shopping cart","3168":"Full of cans, copper wire and a soggy teddy bear. Everything someone owns.","3169":"Loaded with circuit boards to sell at the scrapyard.","3170":"Trash pile","3171":"Garbage bags from the Upper Zone, tossed off the expressway. Sometimes good stuff falls.","3172":"Grates, pipes and the sign of a shop from 2040: \"VIDEO RENTAL\".","3173":"Viaduct dweller","3174":"Viaduct dweller","3175":"Can collector","3176":"Pastel vendor","3177":"Abandoned cargo robot","3178":"Record shelf","3179":"Real vinyl records: Cartola, Adoniran, Racionais. Zé won't let anyone touch them.","3180":"Old Juca, the truco player","3181":"Samba singer","3182":"Off-duty cab driver","3183":"Hackers' workbench","3184":"Mechanical keyboards, energy drink cans and a poster: \"THE NETWORK IS OURS, THE CLOUD IS THEIRS\".","3185":"Mattress","3186":"Someone sleeps here between one attack and the next. There's a plush toy shaped like a server.","3187":"Disconnected hacker","3188":"Upper Zone heiress","3189":"Club security robot","3190":"The panel blinks yellow: \"COOLING UNSTABLE\". Someone stuck a band-aid over the warning.","3191":"Bed 1","3192":"Donor 0447, Minhocão. Sleeps clutching a photo. Beside him, a note: \"He doesn't remember his own name, but he remembers his daughter.\"","3193":"Bed 2","3194":"Donor 0451. She's awake, staring at the ceiling. Quietly repeating a phone number that no longer exists.","3195":"Bed 3","3196":"Donor 0452. The monitor shows deep sleep. The chip at the back of her neck is switched off with a paper clip.","3197":"Bed 4","3198":"Donor 0455. Smiles when Vance walks by. Asks if he's his son. He isn't.","3199":"Medicine cabinet","3200":"Unlabeled vials, reused syringes and a box of neural stabilizers with the Synapse logo scratched out.","3201":"Surgical case","3202":"Top-of-the-line neurosurgery instruments. Nobody buys these with back-alley clinic money.","3203":"Altar of Santa Rita","3204":"Saint Rita of Cascia, patron saint of impossible causes. LED candles, ribbons and wristbands of patients who are gone.","3205":"Waiting chair","3206":"Side table","3207":"Magazines from 2070 and a jar of candy. The candies are mood stabilizers. Better not.","3208":"A real fern, watered with leftover IV saline.","3209":"Robot nurse","3210":"Recovering patient","3211":"Patient's relative","3212":"Maintenance robot","3213":"Aerotrain station — Sector 4","3214":"Sector 7","3215":"Foundry Street","3216":"Furnace Street","3217":"Steel Ave.","3218":"Boiler Street","3219":"Copper Street","3220":"Siren Street","3221":"Docks Street","3222":"Smokestack Ave.","3223":"Metalworkers Ave.","3224":"Industrial Ave.","3225":"Refinery Ave.","3226":"Cranes Ave.","3227":"Coal Ave.","3228":"Dry Port Ave.","3229":"The six o'clock siren goes off even before dawn. Nobody knows what time it is anymore.","3230":"I've worked at Vulcan Foundry for twenty years. My lungs are thirty.","3231":"A detective in Sector 7? Somebody fall into a tank again?","3232":"The smoke here is so thick the delivery drones use headlights.","3233":"The union's going to shut everything down next week. Or the one after. Always is.","3234":"The Siren Bar serves the only cachaça that doesn't melt the glass.","3235":"The robots took half the shifts. The other half is ours, for now.","3236":"Careful in the container yard. The crane doesn't stop for anyone.","3237":"Over in Sector 4 they've got parks. Here we've got smokestacks.","3238":"The aerotrain's late again. They said it was a drone. It's always a drone.","3239":"My helmet has a radio. It only picks up the company station.","3240":"I've seen green acid rain. Out here by the refinery, the rain has color.","3241":"Warehouse 13 has a watchman who never sleeps. They say it's because he has nowhere to live.","3242":"Sixteen-hour shift and they call it \"flexible hours\".","3243":"Factory worker","3244":"Welder","3245":"Freight driver","3246":"Maintenance technician","3247":"Dockworker","3248":"Watchman","3249":"VULCAN FOUNDRY","3250":"WAREHOUSE 13","3251":"SIREN BAR","3252":"METALWORKERS' UNION","3253":"Refinery tank","3254":"A synthetic fuel tank the size of a building. The outside ladder has a warning: \"CLIMB AT YOUR OWN RISK\".","3255":"The tank hums softly. A gauge reads 87%. Of what, nobody can say.","3256":"Refinery smokestack","3257":"A blue flame burns at the top, day and night, like a candle nobody can blow out.","3258":"Synthetic oil. The smell clings to your clothes for a week.","3259":"Vulcan Foundry","3260":"Foundry smokestack","3261":"Brick, soot and a red light blinking at the top to warn the drones. The smoke never stops.","3262":"Night-shift workers warm up here between one steel pour and the next.","3263":"Ingot stack","3264":"Steel ingots still warm, stacked like bricks. Each one bears a volcano stamp.","3265":"Warehouse 13","3266":"Sealed. The label says \"ROBOT PARTS — DO NOT STACK\". It's stacked.","3267":"Cargo crates","3268":"Wooden crates stamped for export to the Upper Zone.","3269":"Industrial rubble","3270":"Gears, belts and a robotic arm that still twitches when it rains.","3271":"A meeting spot for those with nowhere to go after their shift.","3272":"Old tires, used as bench, table and trench.","3273":"Hardy tree","3274":"The only tree on the block. Its leaves are gray with soot, but it insists.","3275":"Aerotrain station — Sector 7","3276":"UNION","3277":"\"UNITED METALWORKERS WILL NOT BE REPLACED BY ROBOTS.\" Someone spray-painted underneath: \"YET\".","3278":"Holographic headlines: \"VULCAN FOUNDRY BREAKS PRODUCTION RECORD\". \"UNION THREATENS GENERAL STRIKE\". \"ACID RAIN: SECTOR 7 HAS THE HEAVIEST AIR IN NEO-SAMPA\".","3279":"Station bench","3280":"A holocall booth covered in soot. On the glass, someone wrote with a finger: \"CALL MOM\".","3281":"Cargo container. Blue light and the hum of servers leak through the gap.","3282":"Someone lives here: there's a curtain on the door and a potted plant on top.","3283":"Dented on one side only, as if a crane had missed its aim.","3284":"Yard crane","3285":"The crane works alone, guided by a logistics AI. It doesn't even stop for the rain.","3286":"Flying truck tires, worn down to the cords.","3287":"Siren Bar","3288":"Sidewalk table","3289":"A yellow plastic table with the logo of a beer that no longer exists.","3290":"Metalworkers' Union","3291":"STRIKE","3292":"Strike banner","3293":"\"EIGHT HOURS OF WORK, EIGHT OF REST, EIGHT OF ACID RAIN.\" Hand-painted.","3294":"Sector 7 flag","3295":"A black gear on a red field. Below: \"THOSE WHO MAKE THE CITY LIVE HERE\".","3296":"Blast furnace No. 3","3297":"The air shimmers in front of the furnace mouth. Inside, the steel glows the color of the sun nobody sees anymore.","3298":"Induction furnace","3299":"Smaller and newer. A sign reads: \"AI-OPERATED — DO NOT TOUCH\". Someone crossed out the \"NOT\".","3300":"Ingot conveyor","3301":"Glowing ingots slide slowly, cooling from orange to gray.","3302":"Cold ingots, ready for shipping. Destination: Upper Zone.","3303":"Slag drum","3304":"Hot slag, the leftovers of steel. Still smoking.","3305":"Cutting oil. Even your gaze slips on it.","3306":"Scrap for melting","3307":"Car shells, old rails and a church bell. Everything becomes new steel.","3308":"Workers' lockers","3309":"Padlocks of every kind. On one, a family photo and a holy card.","3310":"Furnaceman","3311":"Welder","3312":"Label: \"ROBOTIC ARMS — 40 UNITS\". Are they all waving in there? Better not to know.","3313":"Label: \"EYE IMPLANTS — FRAGILE\". Someone drew a winking eye.","3314":"Label: \"SCRAP\". Too heavy to be just scrap.","3315":"Stacked crates","3316":"Crates of parts with no invoice. Half have their stamps blacked out with paint.","3317":"One of the crates is open: memory chips wrapped like candy.","3318":"Inventory terminal","3319":"Warehouse 13 inventory: 4,112 items registered, 4,380 counted. The difference is flagged as \"read error\".","3320":"Watchman's cot","3321":"A cot, a plaid blanket and a battery radio. Old Bento has lived here for years.","3322":"Forklift tires, worn down to the cords.","3323":"Miss Neide's counter","3324":"Cachaça, rice beer and protein coxinhas. The counter bears elbow marks from three generations.","3325":"Tin table","3326":"A domino game stopped midway. Nobody touches it: the owner went to the restroom an hour ago.","3327":"Helmets piled on the table like hats on a rack.","3328":"A small bar glass, a plate of coxinha crumbs and a pay stub folded into eighths.","3329":"Bar TV","3330":"Robot soccer. The workers root against them.","3331":"Dumb cane","3332":"In a paint-can pot. Against the evil eye and city inspectors.","3333":"Worker on break","3334":"Overhead crane operator","3335":"Podium","3336":"A wooden table with a real microphone, the kind with a cord. Nobody knows where they plugged it in.","3337":"Assembly chair","3338":"Union coffee thermos","3339":"\"THOSE WHO MAKE THE CITY HAVE A RIGHT TO IT.\"","3340":"Union archive","3341":"Paper folders with agreements from 2040 to today. The one from 2071 has a soot stain: the year of the Vulcan fire.","3342":"Metalworker","3343":"No acid rain under the viaduct. Best address in the city, son.","3344":"I've been here since Synapse bought the building I lived in. It was supposed to be just a month.","3345":"There's some beans in the drum over there. Help yourself, nobody goes hungry down here.","3346":"Up there they call us \"scenery\". Down here we call them \"the ceiling\".","3347":"My car fell off the expressway in 2071. I kept it. It became my home.","3348":"Police only come down here to tear down tents. You here to tear down tents?","3349":"Miss Cida knows everything that happens in the Minhocão. Ask her.","3350":"I sold my memory chip to eat. Now I don't remember what I ate.","3351":"*BEEP.* CLEANING. CLEANING. CLEANING.","3352":"UNIT WITHOUT OWNER. AWAITING INSTRUCTIONS SINCE 2079.","3353":"*BZZT.* CHARGE: 12%. SEARCHING FOR OUTLET.","3354":"PLEASE STEP AWAY FROM THE WORK AREA.","3355":"*BEEP-BOOP.* THIS ROBOT IS NOT AUTHORIZED TO CONVERSE.","3356":"Access restricted to authorized personnel.","3357":"Detective Vance: access granted by the board. Behavior monitored.","3358":"Do not touch the holographic artworks.","3359":"This floor is watched by 340 cameras. Smile.","3360":"Synapse forensics got here before us. That's never a good sign.","3361":"No prints, not a single hair. This lab is cleaner than an operating room.","3362":"The body fell off the chair after death, not before. You can tell from the cable.","3363":"Detective, everything we find here, Synapse legal wants to see first.","3364":"The network is ours. The cloud is theirs.","3365":"Don't touch Zero's keyboard. Seriously, don't.","3366":"We don't kill anyone, man. We just take down servers.","3367":"Three days without sleep. But I took down Synapse's firewall twice.","3368":"Are you my son? No? Sorry. I forget.","3369":"Sister-7 sings us to sleep. She sings badly, but she sings.","3370":"I was a welder. Now I don't remember how to hold the torch.","3371":"Doctor Caio says I'll remember my name by Christmas.","3372":"My husband signed up for the Synapse trial. A thousand credits. He came back not remembering our wedding.","3373":"I come here every day. One day he'll recognize me.","3374":"Dr. Lin is a saint, son. She cares for them for free.","3375":"PATIENT, PLEASE RETURN TO BED.","3376":"*BEEP.* IV: 40%. CHANGE IN 22 MINUTES.","3377":"WELCOME TO SANTA RITA. SPEAK SOFTLY. THE PATIENTS ARE DREAMING.","3378":"MEDICATION DISTRIBUTED. PAIN REDUCED BY 30%. LONGING: NO CHANGE.","3379":"*BEEP.* NAME ON THE LIST: CONFIRMED.","3380":"NO DANCING WITH ACTIVE COMBAT IMPLANTS.","3381":"THE VIP BOX IS FOR MR. ROSSI'S GUESTS ONLY.","3382":"Tonight the DJ is a four-armed drone. Last week it was a cybernetic octopus.","3383":"Watch your step, son. The floor here is hot all year round.","3384":"Each steel pour lasts forty minutes. My whole life fits into forty-minute pours.","3385":"Master Otto knows the furnace temperature just by looking at the color.","3386":"The robots can't take the heat of furnace three. That's why there are still people here.","3387":"Police? Nobody here saw anything. The noise won't let you.","3388":"A cachaça, Miss Neide! The good stuff, not the one that melts the glass.","3389":"Today's shift was sixteen hours. Tomorrow's too.","3390":"Galdino at the station tells that story about the 2071 fire every night.","3391":"Detective drinks? Then sit down, nobody asks questions here.","3392":"The six o'clock siren went off at midnight again. That factory clock has lost it.","3393":"Assembly at ten. Bring your helmet, the fight sometimes gets physical.","3394":"They want to replace the night shift with robots. We want to replace the board with robots.","3395":"Rosa speaks tonight. When Rosa speaks, Vulcan trembles.","3396":"Union coffee: weak, hot and free. Like the promises.","3397":"Station","3398":"Foundry","3399":"Warehouse","3400":"Bar","3401":"Union","3402":"Sector 4 (Alvorada Ave.)","3403":"Sector 7 — Industrial District","3404":"The Kestrel-7 stayed parked in Sector 4. Here, it's on foot or by aerotrain.","3405":"Express elevator → Ground floor (street)","3406":"Paulista Sector — Neo-Sampa Tower sidewalk","3407":"Lobby entrance → Neo-Sampa Tower","3408":"Aerotrain station — Paulista Sector","3409":"SYNAPSE","3410":"\"SYNAPSE CORP: ETERNITY, NOW IN 12 INSTALLMENTS.\" A smiling face dissolves into pixels and reassembles, forever.","3411":"LÁZARO","3412":"\"PROJECT LÁZARO: NEVER SAY GOODBYE AGAIN.\" Below, in small print: \"subject to server availability\".","3413":"Real water, filtered three times. In the Paulista Sector, even the fountain is a status symbol.","3414":"Laser-trimmed synthetic grass. A sign: \"KEEP OFF. YOU CAN'T AFFORD IT.\"","3415":"Synthetic ipê tree","3416":"A yellow ipê made of fiber optics. It blooms all year round, as per the maintenance contract.","3417":"Headlines: \"SYNAPSE ENGINEER DIES IN THE TOWER\". \"SYNAPSE SHARES UP 4%\". Nobody here finds the two odd together.","3418":"Executive car","3419":"An armored sedan with an android chauffeur. The dark glass doesn't even reflect the rain.","3420":"Synapse diplomatic plates. Parked on the crosswalk. Nobody writes a ticket.","3421":"Drone courier","3422":"From down here the tower seems endless. They say the air up there smells of mint.","3423":"Delivery to the 220th floor? Through the lobby it takes half an hour. By drone, thirty seconds.","3424":"I just came to take a picture of the fountain. Real water, look at that.","3425":"Did you see the news? An engineer died up there. The shares went up. Go figure.","3426":"The aerotrain stops right there on the corner. Punctual like Synapse: never late, never waits.","3427":"Express elevator → Ground floor (Av. Paulista)","3428":"Paulista Sector","3429":"Rua Augusta Alta","3430":"Rua Haddock Lobo","3431":"Av. Consolação","3432":"Rua Pamplona","3433":"Al. Santos","3434":"Rua Frei Caneca","3435":"Rua Bela Cintra","3436":"Upper Av. Paulista","3437":"Al. Jaú","3438":"Av. Paulista","3439":"Al. Itu","3440":"Av. Brigadeiro","3441":"Al. Lorena","3442":"Av. Rebouças","3443":"The air here is filtered. I pay for it with the condo fees, along with the power and eternity.","3444":"I work on the 140th floor. I haven't seen the ground in three years.","3445":"Don't just stand on the sidewalk, detective. Everything here is billed by the minute, even standing still.","3446":"They say Trianon Park has real trees. I've never touched one.","3447":"Synapse bought the whole avenue. Now the green light has a sponsor.","3448":"Starbytes again? That's the third today. My implant keeps count.","3449":"Down in the Minhocão they say it rains inside the houses. Here it only rains on the umbrellas.","3450":"I saw the police going into the tower. Someone up there messed up. Or died.","3451":"Executive","3452":"Corporate lawyer","3453":"Data analyst","3454":"Advisor","3455":"Investor","3456":"eternity is a product","3457":"never say goodbye again","3458":"NEO-SAMPA TOWER","3459":"Arcs of light instead of water. A notice: \"THIS FOUNTAIN IS SPONSORED BY SYNAPSE CORP\".","3460":"A three-story ad, on a loop. It knows your name, and says it out loud.","3461":"Neo-Sampa Tower → Lobby","3462":"Trianon tree","3463":"A real, century-old tree, protected by a humidity field. It has more security guards than most people.","3464":"Trianon fountain","3465":"Neo-Sampa Tower (Synapse Corp)","3466":"Tower","3467":"Trianon Park","3468":"Trianon","3469":"Paulista Sector — Neo-Sampa Tower","3470":"Door → Street (Bixiga)","3471":"Stairs → Street (Bixiga)","3472":"Bixiga (Zé's Bar, Clube 14 Bis)","3473":"The Achiropita festival is the only thing acid rain can't cancel.","3474":"Here in Bixiga the buildings are low. From up on Paulista, we look like a rug.","3475":"Vai-Vem rehearses every Friday. The surdo drum rattles even your implant.","3476":"My nonna said pasta has to be made by hand. Her printer disagrees.","3477":"Clube 14 Bis opens at midnight. The line starts at ten.","3478":"Watch the stairway when it rains. I've lost two teeth and an implant there.","3479":"Zé do Tubo has been serving coffee since before I was born. And I'm seventy.","3480":"Up in the tower, they buy eternity. Down here, we buy pizza.","3481":"Cantina Nonna Lúcia","3482":"Checkered tablecloths, wine bottles turned into candles and a holographic nonna who yells \"MANGIA!\" at every customer.","3483":"Old Oven Pizzeria","3484":"A real wood-fired oven, the last one in the district. The smoke is illegal; the pizza should be too.","3485":"Saudade Thrift Shop","3486":"Clothes from 2040, vinyl records and vintage implants. Everything smells of mothballs and nostalgia.","3487":"Paper & Ink Used Books","3488":"Paper books, stacked to the ceiling. The owner swears every one has been read at least once.","3489":"Nino's Dive Bar","3490":"A cracked marble counter, ice-cold beer and a TV replaying a match from 2026.","3491":"Bixiga","3492":"Rua 13 de Maio","3493":"Rua dos Italianos","3494":"Rua Rui Barbosa","3495":"Rua Conselheiro Carrão","3496":"Rua Santo Antônio","3497":"Rua Major Diogo","3498":"Rua Manuel Dutra","3499":"Rua Avanhandava","3500":"Rua Fortaleza","3501":"Rua Treze de Maio","3502":"Rua Almirante Marques","3503":"Rua Jandaia","3504":"Rua Una","3505":"Rua Abolição","3506":"Bixiga Resident","3507":"Samba Dancer","3508":"Pizza Maker","3509":"Nonna","3510":"Taxi Driver","3511":"Aerotrain Station — Bixiga","3512":"Headlines: \"ACHIROPITA FESTIVAL DEFIES ACID RAIN FOR 160TH YEAR\". \"CLUBE 14 BIS INVESTIGATED FOR MONEY LAUNDERING (AGAIN)\".","3513":"A booth covered in samba school stickers. Someone wrote: \"VAI-VEM, MY LOVE\".","3514":"Zé do Tubo's Bar","3515":"A tin table with two cheap bar glasses and a checkers board. Nobody touches it: it's Seu Juca's.","3516":"Clube 14 Bis","3517":"\"CLUBE 14 BIS: THE DRONE PROVINCE. Entry only if you're on the list or have credit in your account.\"","3518":"Altar of Our Lady of Achiropita","3519":"Candles, plastic flowers and colored ribbons. The saint has protected the neighborhood since 1908. She's still working on the acid rain.","3520":"Fogazza Stand","3521":"Calabrese sausage fogazza, fried to order. The line wraps around the block.","3522":"Mulled Wine Stand","3523":"Mulled wine with cinnamon, served in a paper cup. Warms the soul and the implant.","3524":"Communal Table","3525":"A long table where strangers share pizza, wine and opinions about soccer.","3526":"Vai-Vem Banner","3527":"Black and white, with a crown embroidered in gold. \"Carnival champion 2083.\" Nobody talks about 2084.","3528":"Inside, the surdo drum keeps the rehearsal's beat. The sidewalk vibrates along.","3529":"Rehearsal Hall Speaker","3530":"Plays samba-enredo at a volume City Hall considers \"cultural heritage\".","3531":"Bixiga Stairway","3532":"Stone steps worn by two centuries of people going up and down. Today they're bleachers, living room and stage.","3533":"Real basil, planted by the nonna at number 42. Woe to whoever pulls it.","3534":"An old tree with a tire swing hanging from it. The neighborhood kids fight over turns.","3535":"Checkers Table","3536":"Two old men have been playing checkers so long nobody remembers who's winning.","3537":"Old Fountain","3538":"A cast-iron fountain from 1920. No water for decades, but someone painted it again.","3539":"Zé's Bar","3540":"14 Bis","3541":"Achiropita Festival","3542":"Achiropita","3543":"Vai-Vem Samba School","3544":"Stairway","3545":"Av. Neo-Paulista","3546":"A real brazilwood tree, with a sign: \"PROTECTED SPECIES SINCE 1500. STILL.\"","3547":"A real jequitibá, planted before the city had 300 floors. The birds here have never seen a drone up close.","3548":"A giant fig tree whose roots lift the sidewalk. City hall gave up fighting it.","3549":"Trianon Lake","3550":"A lake of real water, with koi and the reflection of the avenue's neon. Nobody fishes: the koi have a lawyer.","3551":"Trianon Park Gate","3552":"TRIANON","3553":"\"TENENTE SIQUEIRA CAMPOS PARK — TRIANON. The last Atlantic Forest in the Upper Zone. Free entry (for now).\"","3554":"MASP — Neo-Sampa Art Museum","3555":"The MASP of 2085: the same block suspended on four red pillars, now made of smart glass. Inside, the collection is projected at full scale, and the open span below still belongs to everyone.","3556":"ANTIQUES","3557":"Antiques fair under the open span","3558":"Phones from 2020, typewriters and a hard drive \"with grandma's photos\". All sold as relics.","3559":"VINYL","3560":"Vinyl records, cassette tapes and a walkman that still works. The seller charges you to listen.","3561":"MASP ticket office","3562":"Today's exhibition: \"THE LAST HUMAN PAINTERS\". Admission: a hand-drawn portrait of yourself in the guest book.","3563":"Bench under the open span","3564":"THRIFT","3565":"PIZZERIA","3566":"USED BOOKS","3567":"CLUBE 14 BIS","3568":"BOTECO","3569":"CANTINA","3570":"BAR DO ZÉ DO TUBO","3571":"ACHIROPITA","3572":"VAI-VEM SAMBA SCHOOL","3573":"14 BIS","3574":"FOGAZZA","3575":"WINE","3576":"VAI-VEM","3577":"SAMBA","3578":"MASP","3579":"Vai-Vem","3580":"Platform doors — boarding","3581":"Glass safety doors. When the aerotrain stops, they open lined up with the train's doors.","3582":"Aerotrain ticket office","3583":"A real attendant behind the glass, a rare thing. \"Single ticket, detective? The line runs through Sector 4, Sector 7, Paulista and Bixiga.\"","3584":"Aerotrain turnstile","3585":"A turnstile with an iris reader. It blinks green and charges the fare straight from your implant.","3586":"Aerotrain line map","3587":"Platform bench","3588":"Passenger","3589":"Passenger","3590":"Hurried executive","3591":"Are you ready to make the accusation?","3592":"button, input[type=range]","3593":"Controller or keyboard: D-pad moves, A or Enter rotates.","3594":"◉ Scanner","3595":"✦ Clues","3596":"▤ Evidence","3597":"⌖ GPS","3598":"View","3599":"Turn Scanner off","3600":"Turn Scanner on","3601":"First pick. Move the cursor to another piece of evidence and confirm (A / Enter) to connect.","3602":"Tap another piece of evidence to try a connection.","3603":"VANCE'S THOUGHT","3604":"Neural Interface","3605":"Tap two pieces of evidence to connect them. Correct connections produce <b>deductions</b>: theories that move the investigation forward and unlock confrontations with the suspects.","3606":"New case","3607":"CASE SOLVED","3608":"CASE CLOSED","3609":"CASE SHELVED","3610":"HALF THE TRUTH","3611":"LICENSE REVOKED","3612":"WRONG ACCUSATION","3613":"EVIDENCE WIPED","3614":"CONVICTED","3615":"CONVICTED","3616":"UNPUNISHED","3617":"ACQUITTED","3618":"ACQUITTED","3619":"INNOCENT","3620":"VICTIM","3621":"Investigation {0}%","3622":"See the epilogue"};
